helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090001.xhp	0	help	tit				0	bs	Document				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090001.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150017				0	bs	\<link href=\"text/swriter/01/04090001.xhp\" name=\"Document\"\>Document\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090001.xhp	0	help	par_id3147167				0	bs	Fields are used to insert information about the current document, for example, file name, template, statistics, user data, date, and time.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090001.xhp	0	help	par_id3154470				0	bs	For the HTML export and import of date and time fields, \<link href=\"text/swriter/01/04090007.xhp#datumuhrzeit\" name=\"special $[officename] formats\"\>special $[officename] formats\</link\> are used.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090001.xhp	0	help	hd_id3151312				0	bs	Type				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090001.xhp	0	help	par_id3153672	5			0	bs	\<ahelp hid=\"SW:LISTBOX:TP_FLD_DOK:LB_DOKTYPE\"\>Lists the available field types. To add a field to your document, click a field type, click a field in the \<emph\>Select \</emph\>list, and then click \<emph\>Insert\</emph\>.\</ahelp\> The following fields are available:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090001.xhp	0	help	par_id3155182				0	bs	Type				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090001.xhp	0	help	par_id3143272				0	bs	Meaning				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090001.xhp	0	help	par_id3151248				0	bs	Author				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090001.xhp	0	help	par_id3148975	11			0	bs	Inserts the name of the user who first saved the document. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090001.xhp	0	help	par_id3145759				0	bs	Chapter				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090001.xhp	0	help	par_id3149172				0	bs	Inserts the chapter number and/or the chapter name.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090001.xhp	0	help	par_id3145771				0	bs	Date				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090001.xhp	0	help	par_id3151370				0	bs	Inserts the current date. You can insert the date as a fixed field - \<item type=\"literal\"\>Date (fixed)\</item\> - that does not change, or as a dynamic field - \<item type=\"literal\"\>Date\</item\> - that it is updated automatically. To manually update the \<item type=\"literal\"\>Date\</item\> field, press F9.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090001.xhp	0	help	par_id3150699				0	bs	File name				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090001.xhp	0	help	par_id3150122				0	bs	Inserts the filename and/or the directory path of the current document, as well as the filename without extension.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090001.xhp	0	help	par_id3147495				0	bs	Page				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090001.xhp	0	help	par_id3145264				0	bs	Inserts the page number of the current, previous, or next page.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090001.xhp	0	help	par_id3150561				0	bs	Sender				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090001.xhp	0	help	par_id3148863				0	bs	Statistics				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090001.xhp	0	help	par_id3151091	23			0	bs	Inserts document statistics, such as page and word counts, as a field. To view the statistics of a document, choose \<emph\>File - Properties\</emph\>, and then click the\<emph\> Statistics tab. \</emph\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090001.xhp	0	help	par_id3153302				0	bs	Templates				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090001.xhp	0	help	par_id3156123				0	bs	Inserts the filename, the path, or the filename without the file extension of the current template. You can also insert the names of the "Category" and the "Style" formats used in the current template. To view the names of the template categories and the styles used in the templates, choose \<emph\>File - Templates -\</emph\>\<link href=\"text/shared/01/01110100.xhp\" name=\"Organize\"\>\<emph\>Organize\</emph\>\</link\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090001.xhp	0	help	par_id3146939				0	bs	Time				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090001.xhp	0	help	par_id3154340				0	bs	Inserts the current time. You can insert the time as a fixed field - \<item type=\"literal\"\>Time (fixed)\</item\> - that does not change, or as a dynamic field - \<item type=\"literal\"\>Time\</item\> - that it is updated automatically. To manually update the \<item type=\"literal\"\>Time\</item\> field, press F9.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090001.xhp	0	help	par_id3154631	26			0	bs	The following fields can only be inserted if the corresponding field type is selected in the \<emph\>Type \</emph\>list.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090001.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150660				0	bs	Select				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090001.xhp	0	help	par_id3150678	28			0	bs	\<ahelp hid=\"SW:LISTBOX:TP_FLD_DOK:LB_DOKSELECTION\"\>Lists the available fields for the field type selected in the \<emph\>Type \</emph\>list. To insert a field, click the field, and then click \<emph\>Insert\</emph\>.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090001.xhp	0	help	par_id3155359				0	bs	Fields				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090001.xhp	0	help	par_id3154220				0	bs	Function				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090001.xhp	0	help	par_id3145107				0	bs	Previous page				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090001.xhp	0	help	par_id3149595				0	bs	Inserts the page number of the previous page in the document.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090001.xhp	0	help	par_id3146896	34			0	bs	Next page 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090001.xhp	0	help	par_id3148923				0	bs	Inserts the page number of the next page in the document.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090001.xhp	0	help	par_id3156032	36			0	bs	Page Number 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090001.xhp	0	help	par_id3159212				0	bs	Inserts the current page number.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090001.xhp	0	help	par_id3159229				0	bs	In the \<emph\>Format\</emph\>, click the numbering format that you want to use.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090001.xhp	0	help	par_id3145188	39			0	bs	If you want, you can enter an \<emph\>Offset \</emph\>for the displayed page number. With an \<emph\>Offset\</emph\> value of 1, the field will display a number that is 1 more than the current page number, but only if a page with that number exists. On the last page of the document, this same field will be empty.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090001.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150891				0	bs	Offset				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090001.xhp	0	help	par_id3155312				0	bs	\<ahelp hid=\"SW:EDIT:TP_FLD_DOK:ED_DOKVALUE\"\>Enter the offset value that you want to apply to a page number field, for example "+1".\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090001.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145595				0	bs	Format				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090001.xhp	0	help	par_id3145613				0	bs	\<ahelp hid=\"SW:LISTBOX:TP_FLD_DOK:LB_DOKFORMAT\"\>Click the format that you want to apply to the selected field, or click "Additional formats" to define a custom format.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090001.xhp	0	help	par_id3150138				0	bs	\<variable id=\"datumuhrzeitformat\"\>When you click "Additional formats", the \<link href=\"text/shared/01/05020300.xhp\" name=\"Number Format\"\>\<emph\>Number Format\</emph\>\</link\> dialog opens, where you can define a custom format. \</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090001.xhp	0	help	par_id3154867				0	bs	If you choose "Chapter number without separator" for a chapter field, the separators that are specified for chapter number in \<link href=\"text/swriter/01/06060000.xhp\" name=\"Tools - Chapter numbering\"\>\<emph\>Tools - Chapter numbering\</emph\>\</link\> are not displayed.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090001.xhp	0	help	par_id3156079				0	bs	If you choose "chapter number" as the \<emph\>format\</emph\> for reference fields, only the number of the chapter heading containing the referenced object is displayed in the field. If the paragraph style for the chapter heading is not numbered, the field is left blank.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090001.xhp	0	help	par_id3148682				0	bs	The following number range formats are for paragraphs formatted with numbered or bulleted lists:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090001.xhp	0	help	par_id3150006				0	bs	Category and number				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090001.xhp	0	help	par_id3155386				0	bs	The format contains everything between the beginning of the paragraph and directly after the number-range field				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090001.xhp	0	help	par_id3146919				0	bs	Caption text				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090001.xhp	0	help	par_id3155929				0	bs	The format contains the text following the number-range field up to the end of the paragraph				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090001.xhp	0	help	par_id3148755				0	bs	The format only contains the reference number				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090001.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153026				0	bs	Layer				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090001.xhp	0	help	par_id3154580				0	bs	\<ahelp hid=\"SW:NUMERICFIELD:TP_FLD_DOK:ED_DOKLEVEL\"\>Select the chapter heading level that you want to include in the selected field.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090001.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154598				0	bs	Offset in days/minutes				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090001.xhp	0	help	par_id3154899				0	bs	\<ahelp hid=\"SW:NUMERICFIELD:TP_FLD_DOK:ED_DOKDATEOFF\"\>Enter the offset that you want to apply to a date or time field.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090001.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154922				0	bs	Value				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090001.xhp	0	help	par_id3153049				0	bs	\<ahelp hid=\"SW:NUMERICFIELD:TP_FLD_DOK:ED_DOKDATEOFF\"\>Enter the contents that you want to add to a user-defined fields.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\01160400.xhp	0	help	tit				0	bs	AutoAbstract to Presentation				2002-02-02 02:02:02
