helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\mm_seladdblo.xhp	0	help	par_idN10598				0	bs	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>Deletes the selected address block layout.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04010000.xhp	0	help	tit				0	bs	Insert Manual Break				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04010000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145827				0	bs	Insert Manual Break				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04010000.xhp	0	help	par_id3147176				0	bs	\<variable id=\"umbruch\"\>\<ahelp hid=\".uno:InsertBreak\"\>Inserts a manual line break, column break or a page break at the current cursor position.\</ahelp\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04010000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3151176				0	bs	Type				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04010000.xhp	0	help	par_id3145420				0	bs	Select the type of break that you want to insert.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04010000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154097				0	bs	Line Break				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04010000.xhp	0	help	par_id3149805				0	bs	\<ahelp hid=\"SW:RADIOBUTTON:DLG_BREAK:RB_LINE\"\>Ends the current line, and moves the text found to the right of the cursor to the next line, without creating a new paragraph.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04010000.xhp	0	help	par_id3149685				0	bs	You can also insert a line break by pressing Shift+Enter.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04010000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148566				0	bs	Column Break				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04010000.xhp	0	help	par_id3155182				0	bs	\<ahelp hid=\"SW:RADIOBUTTON:DLG_BREAK:RB_COL\"\>Inserts a manual column break (in a multiple column layout), and moves the text found to the right of the cursor to the beginning of the next \<link href=\"text/swriter/01/05040500.xhp\" name=\"column\"\>column\</link\>. A manual column break is indicated by a nonprinting border at the top of the new column.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04010000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149487				0	bs	Page Break				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04010000.xhp	0	help	par_id3149102				0	bs	\<ahelp hid=\"SW:RADIOBUTTON:DLG_BREAK:RB_PAGE\"\>Inserts a manual page break, and moves the text found to the right of the cursor to the beginning of the next page. The inserted page break is indicated by a nonprinting border at the top of the new page.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04010000.xhp	0	help	par_id3145758	13			0	bs	You can also insert a page break by pressing \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command \</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+Enter. However, if you want to assign the following page a different Page Style, you must use the menu command to insert the manual page break.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04010000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149175				0	bs	Style				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04010000.xhp	0	help	par_id3156275				0	bs	\<ahelp hid=\"SW:LISTBOX:DLG_BREAK:LB_COLL\"\>Select the page style for the page that follows the manual page break.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04010000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145782				0	bs	Change page number				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04010000.xhp	0	help	par_id3155917				0	bs	\<ahelp hid=\"SW:CHECKBOX:DLG_BREAK:CB_PAGENUM\"\>Assigns the page number that you specify to the page that follows the manual page break. This option is only available if you assign a different page style to the page that follows manual page break.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04010000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3151384				0	bs	Page number				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04010000.xhp	0	help	par_id3150700				0	bs	\<ahelp hid=\"SW:NUMERICFIELD:DLG_BREAK:ED_PAGENUM\"\>Enter the new page number for the page that follows the manual page break.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04010000.xhp	0	help	par_id3150554				0	bs	To display manual breaks, choose \<link href=\"text/swriter/01/03100000.xhp\" name=\"View - Nonprinting Characters\"\>\<emph\>View - Nonprinting Characters\</emph\>\</link\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090007.xhp	0	help	tit				0	bs	Special Tags				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090007.xhp	0	help	bm_id3154106				0	bs	\<bookmark_value\>tags; in $[officename] Writer\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>$[officename] Writer; tags\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>HTML;fields\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>fields;HTML import and export\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>time fields;HTML\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>date fields;HTML\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>DocInformation fields\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090007.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154106				0	bs	\<link href=\"text/swriter/01/04090007.xhp\" name=\"Special Tags\"\>Special Tags\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090007.xhp	0	help	par_id3153669				0	bs	When you save a document that contains fields as an HTML document, $[officename] automatically converts date, time, and DocInformation fields to special HTML tags. The field contents are inserted between the opening and closing HTML tags of the converted fields. These special HTML tags do not correspond to standard HTML tags.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090007.xhp	0	help	par_id3152960				0	bs	$[officename] Writer fields are identified by the <SDFIELD> tag in an HTML document. The field type, the format, and the name of the special field are included in the opening HTML tag. The format of a field tag that is recognized by an HTML filter depends on the field type.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090007.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154570				0	bs	Date and Time Fields				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090007.xhp	0	help	par_id3149696				0	bs	For "Date" and "Time" fields, the TYPE parameter equals DATETIME. The format of the date or the time is specified by the SDNUM parameter, for example, DD:MM:YY for dates, or HH:MM:SS for time.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090007.xhp	0	help	par_id3155183				0	bs	For fixed date and time fields, the date or the time is specified by the SDVAL parameter.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090007.xhp	0	help	par_id3149485				0	bs	Examples of date and time special HTML tags that are recognized by $[officename] as fields are shown in the following table:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090007.xhp	0	help	par_id3151257				0	bs	Fields				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090007.xhp	0	help	par_id3148970				0	bs	$[officename] Tag				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090007.xhp	0	help	par_id3147102				0	bs	Date is fixed				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090007.xhp	0	help	par_id3153634				0	bs	<SDFIELD TYPE=DATETIME SDVAL="35843,4239988426" SDNUM="1031;1031;DD/MM/YY">17/02/98</SDFIELD>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090007.xhp	0	help	par_id3155137				0	bs	Date is variable				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090007.xhp	0	help	par_id3156275				0	bs	<SDFIELD TYPE=DATETIME SDNUM="1031;1031;DD/MM/YY">17/02/98</SDFIELD>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090007.xhp	0	help	par_id3145774				0	bs	Time is fixed				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090007.xhp	0	help	par_id3155915				0	bs	<SDFIELD TYPE=DATETIME SDVAL="35843,4240335648" SDNUM="1031;1031;HH:MM:SS">10:10:36</SDFIELD>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090007.xhp	0	help	par_id3150110				0	bs	Time is variable				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090007.xhp	0	help	par_id3155862				0	bs	<SDFIELD TYPE=DATETIME SDNUM="1031;1031;HH:MM:SS">10:10:36</SDFIELD>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090007.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147409				0	bs	DocInformation Fields				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090007.xhp	0	help	par_id3147487				0	bs	For DocInformation fields, the TYPE parameter equals DOCINFO. The SUBTYPE parameter displays the specific field type, for example, for the "Created" DocInformation field, SUBTYPE=CREATE. For date and time DocInformation fields, the FORMAT parameter equals DATE or TIME, and the SDNUM parameter indicates the number format that is used. The SDFIXED parameter indicates if the content of the DocInformation field is fixed or not.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090007.xhp	0	help	par_id3147501				0	bs	The contents of a fixed date or time field are equal to the SDVAL parameter, otherwise the contents are equal to the text found between the SDFIELD HTML tags.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090007.xhp	0	help	par_id3149562				0	bs	Examples of DocInformation special HTML tags that are recognized by $[officename] as fields are shown in the following table:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
