helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\05200000.xhp	0	help	par_id3147401				0	bs	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:MergeTable\"\>Combines two consecutive tables into a single table. The tables must be directly next to each other and not separated by an empty paragraph.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\05200000.xhp	0	help	par_id3146325				0	bs	If you choose this command when the cursor is in the middle of three consecutive tables, you are prompted to select the table that you want to merge with.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\02120000.xhp	0	help	tit				0	bs	AutoText				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\02120000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147512				0	bs	\<link href=\"text/swriter/01/02120000.xhp\" name=\"AutoText\"\>AutoText\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\02120000.xhp	0	help	par_id3154571				0	bs	\<variable id=\"autotexttext\"\>\<ahelp hid=\".uno:EditGlossary\"\>Creates, edits, or inserts AutoText. You can store formatted text, text with graphics, tables, and fields as AutoText. To quickly insert AutoText, type the shortcut for the AutoText in your document, and then press F3.\</ahelp\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\02120000.xhp	0	help	par_id3143277				0	bs	You can also click the arrow next to the \<emph\>AutoText\</emph\> icon on the \<emph\>Insert\</emph\> bar, and then choose the AutoText that you want to insert.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\02120000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148982				0	bs	AutoText				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\02120000.xhp	0	help	par_id3153640	5			0	bs	The \<emph\>AutoText \</emph\>dialog lists the AutoText categories and entries.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\02120000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3152766				0	bs	Display remainder of name as a suggestion while typing				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\02120000.xhp	0	help	par_id3145758				0	bs	\<ahelp hid=\"SW:CHECKBOX:DLG_GLOSSARY:CB_INSERT_TIP\"\>Displays a suggestion for completing a word as a Help Tip after you type the first three letters of a word that matches an AutoText entry. To accept the suggestion, press Enter. If more than one AutoText entry matches the letters that you type, press Ctrl+Tab to advance through the entries.\</ahelp\> For example, to insert dummy text, type "Dum", and then press Enter.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\02120000.xhp	0	help	par_id3149177	53			0	bs	To display the list in reverse order, press \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command \</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+Shift+Tab.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\02120000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3151378				0	bs	Name				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\02120000.xhp	0	help	par_id3155862	10			0	bs	\<ahelp hid=\"SW:EDIT:DLG_GLOSSARY:ED_NAME\"\>Lists the name of the currently selected AutoText entry. If you have selected text in the document, type the name of the new AutoText entry, click the \<emph\>AutoText \</emph\>button, and then choose \<emph\>New\</emph\>.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\02120000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150113				0	bs	Shortcut				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\02120000.xhp	0	help	par_id3147413				0	bs	\<ahelp hid=\"SW:EDIT:DLG_GLOSSARY:ED_SHORTNAME\"\>Displays the shortcut for the selected AutoText entry. If you are creating a new AutoText entry, type the shortcut that you want to use for the entry.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\02120000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149558				0	bs	List box				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\02120000.xhp	0	help	par_id3145257				0	bs	Lists the AutoText categories. To view the AutoText entries in a category, double-click the category, or click the plus sign (+) in front of the category. To insert an AutoText entry into the current document, select the entry in the list, and then click \<emph\>Insert\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\02120000.xhp	0	help	par_id3153300				0	bs	You can drag and drop AutoText entries from one category to another.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\02120000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156124				0	bs	Insert				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\02120000.xhp	0	help	par_id3156094				0	bs	Inserts the selected AutoText into the current document.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\02120000.xhp	0	help	par_id3148788				0	bs	If you insert an unformatted AutoText entry into a paragraph, the entry is formatted with the current paragraph style.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\02120000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150039				0	bs	AutoText				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\02120000.xhp	0	help	par_id3153127				0	bs	\<ahelp hid=\"SW:MENUBUTTON:DLG_GLOSSARY:PB_EDIT\"\>Click to display additional AutoText commands, for example, to create a new AutoText entry from a text selection in the current document.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\02120000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154618				0	bs	New				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\02120000.xhp	0	help	par_id3154635				0	bs	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_MD_GLOS_DEFINE\"\>Creates a new AutoText entry from the selection that you made in the current document. The entry is added to the currently selected AutoText category. You must first enter a name before you see this command.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\02120000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149643				0	bs	New (text only)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\02120000.xhp	0	help	par_id3150668				0	bs	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_MD_GLOS_DEFINE_TEXT\"\>Creates a new AutoText entry only from the text in the selection that you made in the current document. Graphics, tables and other objects are not included. You must first enter a name before you see this command.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\02120000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154025				0	bs	Copy				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\02120000.xhp	0	help	par_id3154043				0	bs	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_MD_COPY_TO_CLIPBOARD\"\>Copies the selected AutoText to the clipboard.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\02120000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149965				0	bs	Replace				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\02120000.xhp	0	help	par_id3149607				0	bs	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_MD_GLOS_REPLACE\"\>Replaces the contents of the selected AutoText entry with the selection that was made in the current document.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\02120000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150768				0	bs	Rename				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\02120000.xhp	0	help	par_id3150786	24			0	bs	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Opens the Rename AutoText dialog, where you can change the name of the selected AutoText entry.\</ahelp\>Opens the \<link href=\"text/swriter/01/02120100.xhp\" name=\"Rename Text Block\"\>Rename AutoText\</link\> dialog, where you can change the name of the selected AutoText entry.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\02120000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155341				0	bs	Edit				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\02120000.xhp	0	help	par_id3155358				0	bs	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_MD_GLOS_EDIT\"\>Opens the selected AutoText entry for editing in a separate document. Make the changes that you want, choose \<emph\>File - Save AutoText\</emph\>, and then choose \<emph\>File - Close\</emph\>.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\02120000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155555				0	bs	Macro				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\02120000.xhp	0	help	par_id3145106	44			0	bs	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Opens the Assign Macro dialog, where you attach a macro to the selected AutoText entry.\</ahelp\>Opens the \<link href=\"text/swriter/01/05060700.xhp\" name=\"Assign Macro\"\>Assign Macro\</link\> dialog, where you attach a macro to the selected AutoText entry.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\02120000.xhp	0	help	par_id3149583				0	bs	You can also use the macros that are linked to some of the provided AutoText entries in AutoText entries that you create. The AutoText entries must be created with the "text only" option. For example, insert the string <field:company> in an AutoText entry, and $[officename] replaces the string with the contents of the corresponding database field.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
