helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\06120000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155961				0	bs	\<link href=\"text/swriter/01/06120000.xhp\" name=\"Page Formatting\"\>Page Formatting\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\06120000.xhp	0	help	par_id3150249				0	bs	\<ahelp visibility=\"visible\" hid=\".uno:Repaginate\"\>Updates the page formats in the document and recalculates the total number of pages that is displayed on the \<emph\>Status Bar\</emph\>.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\06120000.xhp	0	help	par_id3154766				0	bs	In long documents, updating the page formatting can take a while.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090003.xhp	0	help	tit				0	bs	Functions				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090003.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149123				0	bs	\<link href=\"text/swriter/01/04090003.xhp\" name=\"Functions\"\>Functions\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090003.xhp	0	help	par_id3150343				0	bs	\<ahelp hid=\"SW_EDIT_TP_FLD_FUNC_ED_FUNCVALUE\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Sets additional function parameters for fields. The type of parameter depends on the field type that you select.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090003.xhp	0	help	par_id3151242				0	bs	Depending on the field type that you select, you can assign conditions to certain functions. For example, you can define a field that executes a macro when you click the field in the document, or a condition that, when met, hides a field. You can also define placeholder fields that insert graphics, tables, frames and other objects into your document when needed.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090003.xhp	0	help	par_id3150537				0	bs	Type				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090003.xhp	0	help	par_id3155623				0	bs	Meaning				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090003.xhp	0	help	par_id3152999				0	bs	Conditional text				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090003.xhp	0	help	par_id3149881	6			0	bs	Inserts text if a certain \<link href=\"text/swriter/01/04090200.xhp\" name=\"condition\"\>condition\</link\> is met. For example, enter "sun eq 1" in the \<emph\>Condition\</emph\> box, and then the text that you want to insert when the variable "sun" equals "1" in the \<emph\>Then \</emph\>box. If you want, you can also enter the text that you want to display when this condition is not met in the \<emph\>Else\</emph\> box. To define the variable "sun", click the \<link href=\"text/swriter/01/04090005.xhp\" name=\"Variables\"\>\<emph\>Variables\</emph\>\</link\> tab, select "Set variable", type "sun" in the\<emph\> Name\</emph\> box, and its value in the\<emph\> Value\</emph\> box.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090003.xhp	0	help	par_id3153719				0	bs	Input list				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090003.xhp	0	help	par_id3147564				0	bs	Inserts a text field that displays one item from a list. You can add, edit, and remove items, and change their order in the list. Click an \<emph\>Input list\</emph\> field in your document or press Ctrl+Shift+F9 to display the \<link href=\"text/swriter/01/04090003.xhp\" name=\"Choose Item\"\>\<emph\>Choose Item\</emph\>\</link\> dialog.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090003.xhp	0	help	par_id3153146				0	bs	Input field				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090003.xhp	0	help	par_id3149287				0	bs	Inserts a text field that you can open by \<link href=\"text/swriter/01/04090100.xhp\" name=\"clicking\"\>clicking\</link\> it in the document. You can then change the text that is displayed.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090003.xhp	0	help	par_id3154691				0	bs	Execute macro				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090003.xhp	0	help	par_id3147515	10			0	bs	Inserts a text field that runs a macro when you click the field in the document. To assign a macro to the field, click the \<emph\>Macro\</emph\> button. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090003.xhp	0	help	par_id3152946				0	bs	Placeholder				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090003.xhp	0	help	par_id3153527				0	bs	Inserts a placeholder field in the document, for example, for graphics. When you click a placeholder field in the document, you are prompted to insert the item that is missing.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090003.xhp	0	help	par_id3150973				0	bs	Hidden text				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090003.xhp	0	help	par_id3154480				0	bs	Hidden Paragraph				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090003.xhp	0	help	par_id3154192	39			0	bs	Combine characters 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090003.xhp	0	help	par_id3159199				0	bs	Combines up to 6 characters, so that they behave as a single character. This feature is only available when Asian fonts are supported.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090003.xhp	0	help	par_id3151329				0	bs	For function fields, the format field is only used for fields of the type placeholder. Here, the format determines the object for which the placeholder stands.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090003.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149494				0	bs	Condition				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090003.xhp	0	help	par_id3143281				0	bs	\<ahelp hid=\"SW:EDIT:TP_FLD_DB:ED_DBCONDITION\"\>For fields linked to a \<link href=\"text/swriter/01/04090200.xhp\" name=\"condition\"\>condition\</link\>, enter the criteria here.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090003.xhp	0	help	hd_id3151248				0	bs	Then, Else				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090003.xhp	0	help	par_id3154830	21			0	bs	\<ahelp hid=\"SW_EDIT_TP_FLD_FUNC_ED_FUNCCOND2\"\>Enter the text to display when the condition is met in the \<emph\>Then \</emph\>box, and the text to display when the condition is not met in the \<emph\>Else \</emph\>box.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090003.xhp	0	help	par_id3146865	22			0	bs	You can also insert database fields in the \<emph\>Then \</emph\>and \<emph\>Else \</emph\>boxes using the format "databasename.tablename.fieldname".				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090003.xhp	0	help	par_id3147583				0	bs	If the table or the field name does not exist in a database, nothing is inserted.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090003.xhp	0	help	par_id3152585				0	bs	If you include the quotes in "databasename.tablename.fieldname", the expression is inserted as text.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090003.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155136				0	bs	Reference				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090003.xhp	0	help	par_id3155149	27			0	bs	Type the text that you want to display in the field. If you are inserting a placeholder field, type the text that you want to display as a help tip when you rest the mouse pointer over the field. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090003.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147071				0	bs	Format				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090003.xhp	0	help	par_id3147084				0	bs	Select the macro that you want to run when the field is clicked.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090003.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154384				0	bs	Macro name				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090003.xhp	0	help	par_id3153351				0	bs	Displays the name of the selected macro.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090003.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156269				0	bs	Placeholder				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090003.xhp	0	help	par_id3156282				0	bs	Type the text that you want to appear in the placeholder field.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090003.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150587				0	bs	Hidden text				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090003.xhp	0	help	par_id3149173				0	bs	Type the text that you want to hide if a condition is met.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090003.xhp	0	help	hd_id3151028				0	bs	Characters				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090003.xhp	0	help	par_id3145771				0	bs	Enter the characters that you want to combine. You can combine a maximum of 6 characters. This option is only available for the \<emph\>Combine characters\</emph\> field type.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090003.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156369				0	bs	Value				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090003.xhp	0	help	par_id3151370				0	bs	Enter a value for the selected field.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090003.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148877				0	bs	Macro				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090003.xhp	0	help	par_id3155912				0	bs	\<ahelp hid=\"SW_PUSHBUTTON_TP_FLD_FUNC_BT_FUNCMACRO\"\>Opens the \<emph\>Macro Selector\</emph\>, where you can choose the macro that will run when you click the selected field in the document.\</ahelp\> This button is only available for the "Execute macro" function field.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090003.xhp	0	help	par_id3150111				0	bs	The following controls are displayed for \<emph\>Input list\</emph\> fields:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
