helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04120200.xhp	0	help	par_id3154476				0	bs	\<variable id=\"verzeichnisse\"\>\<ahelp hid=\".uno:InsertMultiIndex\" visibility=\"visible\"\>Inserts an index or a table of contents at the current cursor position.\</ahelp\> To edit an index or table of contents, place the cursor in the index or table of contents, and then choose \<emph\>Insert - Indexes and Tables - Indexes and Tables\</emph\>.\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04120200.xhp	0	help	par_id3154575				0	bs	You can also preview the index or table in this dialog.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04120200.xhp	0	help	par_id3155905				0	bs	Depending on the type of index or table that you select, the following tabs are present.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04120200.xhp	0	help	par_id3149481				0	bs	Use this tab to specify the column layout for the index or table of contents. By default, the index title is one-column wide and extends out from left page margin.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04120200.xhp	0	help	par_id3149095				0	bs	\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/main.xhp\" name=\"Using Tables of Content and Indexes\"\>Using Tables of Content and Indexes\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04180400.xhp	0	help	tit				0	bs	Exchange Database				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04180400.xhp	0	help	bm_id3145799				0	bs	\<bookmark_value\>databases; exchanging\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>address books; exchanging\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>exchanging databases\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>replacing;databases\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04180400.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145799				0	bs	Exchange Database				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04180400.xhp	0	help	par_id3156384	2			0	bs	\<variable id=\"datenbankaustext\"\>\<ahelp hid=\".uno:ChangeDatabaseField\"\>Change the data sources for the current document.\</ahelp\> To correctly display the contents of inserted fields, the replacement database must contain identical field names. \</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04180400.xhp	0	help	par_id3153818				0	bs	For example, if you inserting address fields in a form letter from an address database, you can then exchange the database with another address database to insert different addresses.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04180400.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149130				0	bs	Exchanging Databases				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04180400.xhp	0	help	par_id3154651				0	bs	You can only change one database at a time in this dialog.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04180400.xhp	0	help	hd_id3146965				0	bs	Databases in Use				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04180400.xhp	0	help	par_id3149053				0	bs	\<ahelp hid=\"SW_MODALDIALOG_DLG_CHANGE_DB\"\>Lists the databases that are currently in use.\</ahelp\> The current document contains at least one data field from each of the databases in the list.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04180400.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147300				0	bs	Available Databases				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04180400.xhp	0	help	par_id3150533				0	bs	\<ahelp hid=\"SW_MODALDIALOG_DLG_CHANGE_DB\"\>Lists the databases that are registered in \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\>.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04180400.xhp	0	help	par_idN106DB				0	bs	Browse				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04180400.xhp	0	help	par_idN106DF				0	bs	\<ahelp hid=\"1419596301\"\>Opens a file open dialog to select a database file (*.odb). The selected file is added to the Available Databases list.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04180400.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149349				0	bs	Define				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04180400.xhp	0	help	par_id3145827	11			0	bs	\<ahelp hid=\"SW_MODALDIALOG_DLG_CHANGE_DB\"\>Replaces the current data source with the data source that you selected in the \<emph\>Available Databases \</emph\>list.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04180400.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154506				0	bs	To exchange a database:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04180400.xhp	0	help	par_id3149881				0	bs	Ensure that both databases contain matching field names and field types.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04180400.xhp	0	help	par_id3148386				0	bs	Click in the document that you want to change the data source for.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04180400.xhp	0	help	par_id3150564				0	bs	Choose \<emph\>Edit - Exchange Database\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04180400.xhp	0	help	par_id3153925				0	bs	In the \<emph\>Databases in Use\</emph\> list, select the database table that you want to replace.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04180400.xhp	0	help	par_id3147169				0	bs	In the \<emph\>Available Databases\</emph\> list, select the replacement database table.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04180400.xhp	0	help	par_id3151273				0	bs	Click \<emph\>Define\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090005.xhp	0	help	tit				0	bs	Variables				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090005.xhp	0	help	bm_id8526261				0	bs	\<bookmark_value\>user-defined fields, restriction\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090005.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153716				0	bs	\<link href=\"text/swriter/01/04090005.xhp\" name=\"Variables\"\>Variables\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090005.xhp	0	help	par_id3150764				0	bs	Variable fields let you add dynamic content to your document. For example, you can use a variable to reset the page numbering.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090005.xhp	0	help	par_id3149759				0	bs	User-defined fields are only available in the current document.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090005.xhp	0	help	par_id3150703				0	bs	Type				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090005.xhp	0	help	par_id3154096				0	bs	Description				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090005.xhp	0	help	par_id3149803				0	bs	Set Variable				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090005.xhp	0	help	par_id3150996				0	bs	Defines a variable and its value. You can change the value of a variable by clicking in front of the variable field, and then choosing \<emph\>Edit - Field\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090005.xhp	0	help	par_id3154571				0	bs	Show Variable				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090005.xhp	0	help	par_id3153669	9			0	bs	Inserts the current value of the variable that you click in the \<emph\>Selection \</emph\>list.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090005.xhp	0	help	par_id3147531				0	bs	DDE field				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090005.xhp	0	help	par_id3149684				0	bs	Inserts a \<link href=\"text/shared/00/00000005.xhp#dde\" name=\"DDE\"\>DDE\</link\> link into the document, that you can update as often as you want through the assigned name.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090005.xhp	0	help	par_id3159196				0	bs	Insert Formula				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090005.xhp	0	help	par_id3151322				0	bs	Inserts a fixed number, or the result of a formula.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090005.xhp	0	help	par_id3149494				0	bs	Input field				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090005.xhp	0	help	par_id3154829				0	bs	Inserts a new value for a variable or a User Field.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090005.xhp	0	help	par_id3149098				0	bs	The value of a variable in an Input field is only valid from where the field is inserted and onwards. To change the value of the variable later in the document, insert another Input field of the same name, but with a different value. However, the value of a User Field is changed globally.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090005.xhp	0	help	par_id3151255				0	bs	The variables are displayed in the \<emph\>Selection\</emph\> field. When you click the \<emph\>Insert\</emph\> button, the dialog\<link href=\"text/swriter/01/04090100.xhp\" name=\"Input Field\"\>\<emph\>Input Field\</emph\>\</link\> appears, where you can enter the new value or additional text as a remark.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090005.xhp	0	help	par_id3149034				0	bs	Number range				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090005.xhp	0	help	par_id3152772				0	bs	Inserts automatic numbering for tables, graphics, or text frames.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090005.xhp	0	help	par_id3147073				0	bs	Set page variable				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090005.xhp	0	help	par_id3154389				0	bs	Inserts a reference point in the document, after which the page count restarts. Select "on" to enable the reference point, and "off" to disable it. You can also enter an offset to start the page count at a different number.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090005.xhp	0	help	par_id3156267				0	bs	Show Page Variable				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090005.xhp	0	help	par_id3150588				0	bs	Displays the number of pages from the "Set page variable" reference point to this field.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090005.xhp	0	help	par_id3145779				0	bs	User Field				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090005.xhp	0	help	par_id3151377				0	bs	Inserts a custom global variable. You can use the User Field to define a variable for a condition statement. When you change a User Field, all instances of the variable in the document are updated.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090005.xhp	0	help	par_id3148886	25			0	bs	For user-defined fields, click the format that you want to apply in the \<emph\>Format \</emph\>list, or click "Additional formats" to define a custom format.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090005.xhp	0	help	par_id3155860				0	bs	\<ahelp hid=\"SW_LISTBOX_TP_FLD_VAR_LB_VARFORMAT\"\>In the \<emph\>Format\</emph\> list, define if the value is inserted as text or a number.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090005.xhp	0	help	par_id3150696	36			0	bs	In an HTML document, two additional fields are available for the "Set variable" field type: HTML_ON and HTML_OFF. The text that you type in the \<emph\>Value \</emph\>box is converted to an opening HTML \<link href=\"text/shared/00/00000002.xhp#tags\" name=\"tag\"\>tag\</link\> (<Value>) or to a closing HTML (</Value>) tag when the file is saved as an HTML document, depending on the option that you select.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090005.xhp	0	help	par_id3149555				0	bs	If you double-click an entry while holding the Ctrl key or select the desired variable and press the spacebar, it is immediately inserted into your document.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090005.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155969				0	bs	Formula				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090005.xhp	0	help	par_id3155982				0	bs	This option is only available if the "Insert formula" field type is selected.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090005.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149229				0	bs	Invisible				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090005.xhp	0	help	par_id3156233				0	bs	\<ahelp hid=\"SW_CHECKBOX_TP_FLD_VAR_CB_VARINVISIBLE\"\>Hides the field contents in the document.\</ahelp\> The field is inserted as a thin gray mark in the document. This option is only available for the "Set Variable" and "User Field" field types.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090005.xhp	0	help	hd_id3146326				0	bs	Chapter numbering				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090005.xhp	0	help	par_id3146340				0	bs	Sets the options for resetting chapter numbers.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090005.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147456				0	bs	Level				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090005.xhp	0	help	par_id3149836				0	bs	\<ahelp hid=\"SW_LISTBOX_TP_FLD_VAR_LB_VARCHAPTERLEVEL\"\>Choose the heading or chapter level at which to restart numbering in the document.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090005.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147594				0	bs	Separator				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090005.xhp	0	help	par_id3148846				0	bs	\<ahelp hid=\"SW_EDIT_TP_FLD_VAR_ED_VARSEPARATOR\"\>Type the character that you want to use as a separator between the heading or chapter levels.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090005.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147057				0	bs	Apply				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090005.xhp	0	help	par_id3155562				0	bs	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FLDVAR_APPLY\"\>Adds the user-defined field to the \<emph\>Selection\</emph\> list.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090005.xhp	0	help	hd_id3151080				0	bs	Delete				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090005.xhp	0	help	par_id3154769				0	bs	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FLDVAR_DELETE\"\>Removes the user-defined field from the selection list. You can only remove fields that are not used in the current document.\</ahelp\> To remove a field that is used in the current document from the list, first delete all instances of the field in the document, and then remove it from the list.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090005.xhp	0	help	par_id3145318				0	bs	\<image id=\"img_id3153293\" src=\"svx/res/nu02.png\" width=\"0.222inch\" height=\"0.222inch\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3153293\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090005.xhp	0	help	par_id3150169				0	bs	Delete				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04130100.xhp	0	help	tit				0	bs	Resizing and Moving Frames, Objects With the Keyboard				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04130100.xhp	0	help	bm_id3154506				0	bs	\<bookmark_value\>moving; objects and frames\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>objects; moving using keyboard\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>objects;resizing using keyboard\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>resizing;objects and frames\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04130100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154506				0	bs	Resizing and Moving Frames, Objects With the Keyboard				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04130100.xhp	0	help	par_id3145248				0	bs	You can resize and move selected frames and objects with the keyboard.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04130100.xhp	0	help	par_id3148771				0	bs	To move a selected frame or object, press an arrow key. To move by one pixel, hold down \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Option\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Alt\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>, and then press an arrow key.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04130100.xhp	0	help	par_id3150762				0	bs	To resize a selected frame or object, first press Ctrl+Tab. Now one of the handles blinks to show that it is selected. TO select another handle, press Ctrl+Tab again. Press an arrow key to resize the object by one grid unit. To resize by one pixel, hold down \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Option\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Alt\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>, and then press an arrow key.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090002.xhp	0	help	tit				0	bs	References				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090002.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153641				0	bs	\<link href=\"text/swriter/01/04090002.xhp\" name=\"References\"\>References\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090002.xhp	0	help	par_id3155142				0	bs	\<variable id=\"reftext\"\>\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>This is where you insert the references or referenced fields into the current document. References are referenced fields within the same document or within sub-documents of a master document.\</ahelp\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090002.xhp	0	help	par_id3159197				0	bs	The advantage of entering a cross-reference as a field is that you do not have to adjust the references manually every time you change the document. Just update the fields with F9 and the references in the document are updated too.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090002.xhp	0	help	par_id3151380				0	bs	Type				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090002.xhp	0	help	par_id3150700				0	bs	Meaning				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090002.xhp	0	help	par_id3155862				0	bs	Set Reference				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090002.xhp	0	help	par_id3147422				0	bs	Set target for a referenced field. Under \<emph\>Name\</emph\>, enter a name for the reference. When inserting the reference, the name will then appear as an identification in the list box \<emph\>Selection\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090002.xhp	0	help	par_id3149556				0	bs	In an HTML document, reference fields entered this way will be ignored. For the target in HTML documents, you have to \<link href=\"text/swriter/01/04040000.xhp\" name=\"insert a bookmark\"\>insert a bookmark\</link\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090002.xhp	0	help	par_id3150548				0	bs	Insert Reference				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090002.xhp	0	help	par_id3147746				0	bs	Inserting a reference to another position in the document. The corresponding text position has to be defined with "Set Reference" first. Otherwise, inserting a reference by choosing a field name under \<emph\>Selection\</emph\> is not possible.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090002.xhp	0	help	par_id3146344				0	bs	In master documents, you can also reference from one sub-document to another. Note that the reference name will not appear in the selection field and has to be entered "by hand".				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090002.xhp	0	help	par_id3149847				0	bs	In an HTML document, reference fields entered this way will be ignored. For referenced fields in HTML documents, you have to \<link href=\"text/shared/01/05020400.xhp\" name=\"insert a hyperlink\"\>insert a hyperlink\</link\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090002.xhp	0	help	par_id3150907				0	bs	After inserting a bookmark in the document with \<emph\>Insert - Bookmark\</emph\>, the bookmarks entry on the \<emph\>References\</emph\> tab becomes usable. Bookmarks are used to mark certain text passages in a document. In a text document, you can use the bookmarks, for example, to jump from one passage in the document to another.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090002.xhp	0	help	par_id3155080				0	bs	In an HTML document, these bookmarks become anchors <A name>, which determine the target of hyperlinks for example.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090002.xhp	0	help	par_id3154772				0	bs	References are fields. To remove a reference, delete the field. If you set a longer text as a reference and you do not want to reenter it after deleting the reference, select the text and copy it to the clipboard. You can then reinsert it as "unformatted text" at the same position using the command \<emph\>Edit - Paste special\</emph\>. The text remains intact while the reference is deleted.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090002.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154333				0	bs	Format				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090002.xhp	0	help	par_id3148786				0	bs	\<ahelp hid=\"SW:LISTBOX:TP_FLD_REF:LB_REFFORMAT\"\>Select the format that you want to use for the selected reference field.\</ahelp\> The following formats are available:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090002.xhp	0	help	par_id3150039				0	bs	Page				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090002.xhp	0	help	par_id3153134				0	bs	Inserts the number of the page containing the reference target.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090002.xhp	0	help	par_id3150681				0	bs	Reference				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090002.xhp	0	help	par_id3154040				0	bs	Inserts the complete reference target text.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090002.xhp	0	help	par_id3149972				0	bs	Above/Below				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090002.xhp	0	help	par_id3149619				0	bs	Inserts "above" or "below", depending on the location of the reference target relative to the position of the reference field.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090002.xhp	0	help	par_id3148705				0	bs	As Page Style				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090002.xhp	0	help	par_id3148728				0	bs	Inserts the number of the page containing the reference target using the format specified in the page style.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
