helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\page_break.xhp	0	help	tit				0	bs	Inserting and Deleting Page Breaks				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\page_break.xhp	0	help	bm_id3155183				0	bs	\<bookmark_value\>page breaks; inserting and deleting\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>inserting; page breaks\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>deleting;page breaks\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>pages; inserting/deleting page breaks\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>manual page breaks\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\page_break.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155183				0	bs	\<variable id=\"page_break\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/page_break.xhp\" name=\"Inserting and Deleting Page Breaks\"\>Inserting and Deleting Page Breaks\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\page_break.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149833				0	bs	To insert a manual page break:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\page_break.xhp	0	help	par_id3153402				0	bs	Click in your document where you want the new page to begin.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\page_break.xhp	0	help	par_id3153119				0	bs	Press Ctrl+Enter.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\page_break.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153135				0	bs	To delete a manual page break:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\page_break.xhp	0	help	par_id3149641				0	bs	Click in front of the first character on the page that follows the manual page break.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\page_break.xhp	0	help	par_id3149608				0	bs	Press Backspace.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\page_break.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149624				0	bs	To delete a manual page break that occurs before a table:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\page_break.xhp	0	help	par_id3145111				0	bs	Right-click in the table, and choose \<emph\>Table\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\page_break.xhp	0	help	par_id3156254				0	bs	Click the \<link href=\"text/swriter/01/05090300.xhp\" name=\"Text Flow\"\>\<emph\>Text Flow\</emph\>\</link\> tab.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\page_break.xhp	0	help	par_id3153380				0	bs	Clear the \<emph\>Break\</emph\> check box.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\page_break.xhp	0	help	par_id3154249				0	bs	\<link href=\"text/swriter/01/04010000.xhp\" name=\"Insert Break dialog\"\>Insert Break dialog\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\section_insert.xhp	0	help	tit				0	bs	Inserting Sections				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\section_insert.xhp	0	help	bm_id3149695				0	bs	\<bookmark_value\>sections; inserting\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>inserting; sections\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>HTML;text sections\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>HTML documents;inserting sections\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>updating;links, manually\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>links;inserting sections\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\section_insert.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149695				0	bs	\<variable id=\"section_insert\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/section_insert.xhp\" name=\"Inserting Sections\"\>Inserting Sections\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\section_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id3155917				0	bs	You can insert new sections, or links to sections in other documents into the current document. If you insert a section as a link, the content of the link changes when you modify the source document.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\section_insert.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155863				0	bs	To insert a new section:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\section_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id3149843				0	bs	Click in your document where you want to insert a new section, or select the text that you want to convert to a section.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\section_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id3156103				0	bs	If you select a text that occurs within a paragraph, the text is automatically converted into a new paragraph.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\section_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id3149281				0	bs	Choose \<emph\>Insert - Section\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\section_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id3153404				0	bs	In the \<emph\>New Section \</emph\>box, type a name for the section.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\section_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id3153127				0	bs	Set the options for the section, and then click \<emph\>Insert\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\section_insert.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149635				0	bs	To insert a section as a link:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\section_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id3149648				0	bs	Before you can insert a section as link, you must first create sections in the source document.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\section_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id3149611				0	bs	When you open a document that contains linked sections, $[officename] prompts you to update the contents of the sections. To manually update a link, choose \<emph\>Tools - Update - Links\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\section_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id3149860				0	bs	You can also insert linked sections in HTML documents. When you view the page in a web browsers, the content of the sections corresponds to the content of the sections at the time the HTML document was last saved.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\section_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id3145104				0	bs	Click in your document where you want to insert the linked section.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\section_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id3156241				0	bs	Choose \<emph\>Insert - Section\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\section_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id3153363				0	bs	In the \<emph\>New Section \</emph\>box, type a name for the section.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\section_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id3153387				0	bs	In the \<emph\>Link \</emph\>area, select the \<emph\>Link \</emph\>check box. \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"WIN\"\>Under Windows, you can also select the \<emph\>DDE\</emph\> check box to automatically update the contents of the section when the section in the source document is changed. \</caseinline\>\</switchinline\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\section_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id3154852				0	bs	Click the browse button (\<emph\>...\</emph\>) next to the \<emph\>File name \</emph\>box.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\section_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id3155882				0	bs	Locate the document containing the section that you want to link to, and then click \<emph\>Insert\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\section_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id3149978				0	bs	In the \<emph\>Section \</emph\>box, select the section that you want to insert.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\section_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id3150003				0	bs	Click \<emph\>Insert\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_form.xhp	0	help	tit				0	bs	Formatting an Index or a Table of Contents				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_form.xhp	0	help	bm_id3155855				0	bs	\<bookmark_value\>indexes; formatting\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>editing; index format\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>tables of contents; formatting\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>entries; formatting indexes\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>tables of contents; hyperlinks as entries\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>hyperlinks; in tables of contents and indexes\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>formatting;indexes and tables of contents\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_form.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155855				0	bs	\<variable id=\"indices_form\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/indices_form.xhp\" name=\"Formatting an Index or a Table of Contents\"\>Formatting an Index or a Table of Contents\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_form.xhp	0	help	par_id3154259				0	bs	You can apply different paragraph styles, assign hyperlinks to entries, change the layout of indexes, and change the background color of indexes in the \<emph\>Insert Index\</emph\> dialog.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_form.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155888				0	bs	To apply a different paragraph style to an index level:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_form.xhp	0	help	par_id3147110				0	bs	Right-click in the index or table of contents, and then choose \<emph\>Edit Index/Table\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_form.xhp	0	help	par_id3147135	46			0	bs	Click the \<emph\>Styles \</emph\>tab.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_form.xhp	0	help	par_id3150229	47			0	bs	Click an index level in the \<emph\>Levels \</emph\>list.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_form.xhp	0	help	par_id3150934	48			0	bs	Click the style that you want to apply in the \<emph\>Paragraph Style \</emph\>list.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_form.xhp	0	help	par_id3150960				0	bs	Click the assign button \<emph\><\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_form.xhp	0	help	par_id3150516				0	bs	Click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_form.xhp	0	help	hd_id3146878				0	bs	To assign hyperlinks to entries in a table of contents:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_form.xhp	0	help	par_id3146890				0	bs	You can assign a cross-reference as a hyperlink to entries in a table of contents.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_form.xhp	0	help	par_id3150712				0	bs	Right-click in the table of contents, and then choose \<emph\>Edit Index/Table\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_form.xhp	0	help	par_id3150738				0	bs	Click the \<emph\>Entries\</emph\> tab.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_form.xhp	0	help	par_id3148399				0	bs	Click the heading level that you want to assign hyperlinks to in the \<emph\>Level \</emph\>list.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_form.xhp	0	help	par_id3148424	53			0	bs	In the \<emph\>Structure \</emph\>area, click in the box in front of \<emph\>E#\</emph\>, and then click \<emph\>Hyperlink\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_form.xhp	0	help	par_id3153171				0	bs	Click in the box behind the \<emph\>E\</emph\>, and then click \<emph\>Hyperlink\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_form.xhp	0	help	par_id3147060				0	bs	Repeat for each heading level that you want to create hyperlinks for, or click the \<emph\>All levels\</emph\> button to apply the formatting to all levels.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
