helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\table_repeat_multiple_headers.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153406				0	bs	\<variable id=\"table_repeat_multiple_headers\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/table_repeat_multiple_headers.xhp\" name=\"Repeating a Table Header on a New Page\"\>Repeating a Table Heading on a New Page\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\table_repeat_multiple_headers.xhp	0	help	par_id3149636				0	bs	You can repeat a table heading on each new page that the table spans.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\table_repeat_multiple_headers.xhp	0	help	par_id3145098				0	bs	Choose \<emph\>Table - Insert - Table\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\table_repeat_multiple_headers.xhp	0	help	par_id3156240				0	bs	Select the \<emph\>Heading \</emph\>and the \<emph\>Repeat heading \</emph\>check boxes.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\table_repeat_multiple_headers.xhp	0	help	par_id3153376				0	bs	Select the number of rows and columns for the table.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\table_repeat_multiple_headers.xhp	0	help	par_id3153393				0	bs	Click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\header_with_line.xhp	0	help	tit				0	bs	Formatting Headers or Footers				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\header_with_line.xhp	0	help	bm_id3154866				0	bs	\<bookmark_value\>inserting; lines under headers\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>lines; under headers/above footers\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>headers;formatting\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>footers;formatting\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>shadows;headers/footers\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>borders;for headers/footers\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\header_with_line.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154866				0	bs	\<variable id=\"header_with_line\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/header_with_line.xhp\" name=\"Formatting Headers or Footers\"\>Formatting Headers or Footers\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\header_with_line.xhp	0	help	par_id3154243				0	bs	You can apply direct formatting to the text in a header or footer. You can also adjust the spacing of the text relative to the header or footer frame or apply a border to the header or footer.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\header_with_line.xhp	0	help	par_id3155873				0	bs	Choose \<emph\>Format - Page \</emph\>and select the \<emph\>Header \</emph\>or \<emph\>Footer \</emph\>tab.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\header_with_line.xhp	0	help	par_id3147109				0	bs	Set the spacing options that you want to use.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\header_with_line.xhp	0	help	par_id3147128				0	bs	To add a border or a shadow to the header or the footer, click \<emph\>More\</emph\>. The \<emph\>Border/Background \</emph\>dialog opens.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pageorientation.xhp	0	help	tit				0	bs	Changing Page Orientation (Landscape or Portrait)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pageorientation.xhp	0	help	bm_id9683828				0	bs	\<bookmark_value\>page styles;orientation\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>page formats; changing individual pages\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>formatting; changing individual pages\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>portrait and landscape\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>landscape and portrait\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>printing;portrait/landscape format\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>orientation of pages\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>paper orientation\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>page orientation\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>sideways orientation of pages\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pageorientation.xhp	0	help	par_idN106FF				0	bs	\<variable id=\"pageorientation\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/pageorientation.xhp\"\>Changing Page Orientation\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pageorientation.xhp	0	help	par_idN1071D				0	bs	$[officename] uses page styles to specify the orientation of the pages in a document. For example, to change the page orientation of one or more pages in a document from portrait to landscape in a document, you need to create a page style that uses the landscape orientation, and then apply the page style to the pages.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pageorientation.xhp	0	help	par_idN10727				0	bs	Choose \<emph\>Format - Styles and Formatting\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pageorientation.xhp	0	help	par_idN10741				0	bs	Click the \<emph\>Page Styles\</emph\> icon.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pageorientation.xhp	0	help	par_idN10749				0	bs	Right-click, and choose \<emph\>New\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pageorientation.xhp	0	help	par_idN10751				0	bs	On the \<emph\>Organizer\</emph\> tab page, type a name for the page style in the \<emph\>Name\</emph\> box.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pageorientation.xhp	0	help	par_idN1075D				0	bs	In the \<emph\>Next Style\</emph\> box, select the page style that you want to apply to the next page.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pageorientation.xhp	0	help	par_idN10775				0	bs	Click the \<emph\>Page\</emph\> tab.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pageorientation.xhp	0	help	par_idN1077D				0	bs	Under \<emph\>Paper format\</emph\>, select \<emph\>Portrait\</emph\> or \<emph\>Landscape\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pageorientation.xhp	0	help	par_idN108AE				0	bs	Click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\header_footer.xhp	0	help	tit				0	bs	About Headers and Footers				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\header_footer.xhp	0	help	bm_id3155863				0	bs	\<bookmark_value\>headers;about\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>footers;about\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>HTML documents; headers and footers\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\header_footer.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155863				0	bs	\<variable id=\"header_footer\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/header_footer.xhp\" name=\"About Headers and Footers\"\>About Headers and Footers\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\header_footer.xhp	0	help	par_id3154255				0	bs	Headers and footers are areas in the top and the bottom page margins, where you can add text or graphics. Headers and footers are added to the current page style. Any page that uses the same style automatically receives the header or footer that you add. You can insert \<link href=\"text/swriter/01/04090000.xhp\" name=\"Fields\"\>Fields\</link\>, such as page numbers and chapter headings, in headers and footers in a text document.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\header_footer.xhp	0	help	par_id3150511				0	bs	The page style for the current page is displayed in the \<emph\>Status Bar\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\header_footer.xhp	0	help	par_id3155896				0	bs	To add a header to a page, choose \<emph\>Insert - Header\</emph\>, and then select the page style for the current page from the submenu.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\header_footer.xhp	0	help	par_id3147119				0	bs	To add a footer to a page, choose \<emph\>Insert - Footer\</emph\>, and then select the page style for the current page from the submenu.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\header_footer.xhp	0	help	par_id3153726				0	bs	You can also choose \<emph\>Format - Page\</emph\>, click the \<emph\>Header\</emph\> or \<emph\>Footer \</emph\>tab, and then select \<emph\>Header on \</emph\>or \<emph\>Footer on\</emph\>. Clear the \<emph\>Same content left/right\</emph\> check box if you want to define different headers and footers for even and odd pages.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\header_footer.xhp	0	help	par_id3146876				0	bs	To use different headers or footers in your document, you must add them to different \<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/header_pagestyles.xhp\" name=\"Page Styles\"\>Page Styles\</link\>, and then apply the styles to the pages where you want the headers or footer to appear.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\header_footer.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150704				0	bs	Headers and Footers in HTML Documents				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\header_footer.xhp	0	help	par_id3150717	34			0	bs	Some of the header and footer options are also available for HTML documents. Headers and footers are not supported by HTML and instead are exported with special tags, so that they can be viewed in a browser. Headers and footers are only exported in HTML documents if they are enabled in Online Layout mode. When you reopen the document in $[officename], the headers and footers are displayed correctly, including any fields that you inserted. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\header_footer.xhp	0	help	par_id3153174				0	bs	\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/header_pagestyles.xhp\" name=\"Page Styles\"\>Page Styles\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\templates_styles.xhp	0	help	tit				0	bs	Templates and Styles				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\templates_styles.xhp	0	help	bm_id3153396				0	bs	\<bookmark_value\>formatting styles; styles and templates\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>styles; styles and templates\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>organizing; templates (guide)\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>templates; organizing (guide)\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\templates_styles.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153396				0	bs	\<variable id=\"templates_styles\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/templates_styles.xhp\" name=\"Templates and Styles\"\>Templates and Styles\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\templates_styles.xhp	0	help	par_id3149635				0	bs	A template is a document that contains specific formatting styles, graphics, tables, object, and other information. A template is used as the basis for creating other documents. For example, you can define paragraph and character styles in a document, save the document as a template, and then use the template to create a new document with the same styles.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\templates_styles.xhp	0	help	par_id3149957				0	bs	Unless you specify otherwise, every new $[officename] text document is based on the "Default" template.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\templates_styles.xhp	0	help	par_id3149974				0	bs	$[officename] has a number of \<link href=\"text/swriter/01/05130000.xhp\" name=\"predefined templates\"\>predefined templates\</link\> that you can use to create different types or text documents, such as business letters.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\templates_styles.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149613				0	bs	Viewing and Organizing Styles in Templates				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\templates_styles.xhp	0	help	par_idN106B0				0	bs	Use the \<link href=\"text/shared/01/01110100.xhp\" name=\"Template Management\"\>Template Management\</link\> dialog to copy styles from one document to another.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\templates_styles.xhp	0	help	par_id3153377				0	bs	To copy a style, drag it to another template or document.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_emphasize.xhp	0	help	tit				0	bs	Emphasizing Text				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_emphasize.xhp	0	help	bm_id3149820				0	bs	\<bookmark_value\>text; emphasizing\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>emphasizing text\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_emphasize.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149820				0	bs	\<variable id=\"text_emphasize\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/text_emphasize.xhp\" name=\"Emphasizing Text\"\>Emphasizing Text\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_emphasize.xhp	0	help	par_id3155922				0	bs	Here are a few examples of how to emphasize text in a document:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_emphasize.xhp	0	help	par_id3147412				0	bs	Select the text and apply a different font style or effect, such as \<emph\>bold\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_emphasize.xhp	0	help	par_id3149840	68			0	bs	Right-click in a paragraph, choose \<emph\>Paragraph, \</emph\>set the options that you want, for example, the background color, and then click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_emphasize.xhp	0	help	par_id3150084				0	bs	Select the text, and then choose \<emph\>Insert Frame\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_emphasize.xhp	0	help	par_id6924649				0	bs	Use the Text tool on the Drawing toolbar. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_emphasize.xhp	0	help	par_idN106E7				0	bs	Use Fontwork. To open the Fontwork window, click the Fontwork icon on the Drawing bar.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_centervert.xhp	0	help	tit				0	bs	Using a Frame to Center Text on a Page				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_centervert.xhp	0	help	bm_id3155177				0	bs	\<bookmark_value\>text frames; centering on pages\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>centering text frames on pages\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>title pages; centering text on\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_centervert.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155177				0	bs	\<variable id=\"text_centervert\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/text_centervert.xhp\" name=\"Using a Frame to Center Text on a Page\"\>Using a Frame to Center Text on a Page\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_centervert.xhp	0	help	par_id3155920				0	bs	Select the text that you want to center on the page.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_centervert.xhp	0	help	par_id3155868				0	bs	Choose \<emph\>Insert - Frame\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_centervert.xhp	0	help	par_id3152765				0	bs	In the \<emph\>Anchor \</emph\>area, select \<emph\>To page\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_centervert.xhp	0	help	par_id3149844				0	bs	In the \<emph\>Size \</emph\>area, set the dimensions of the frame.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_centervert.xhp	0	help	par_id3156114				0	bs	In the \<emph\>Position \</emph\>area, select "Center" in the \<emph\>Horizontal \</emph\>and \<emph\>Vertical \</emph\>boxes.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_centervert.xhp	0	help	par_id3153410				0	bs	Click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_centervert.xhp	0	help	par_id3149615				0	bs	To hide the borders of the frame, select the frame, and then choose \<emph\>Format - Frame\</emph\>. Click the \<emph\>Borders\</emph\> tab, and then click in the\<emph\> Set No Border\</emph\> box in the\<emph\> Line Arrangement\</emph\> area.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_centervert.xhp	0	help	par_id3145098				0	bs	To resize the frame, drag the edges of the frame.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\calculate_intext.xhp	0	help	tit				0	bs	Calculating Complex Formulas in Text Documents				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\calculate_intext.xhp	0	help	bm_id3147406				0	bs	\<bookmark_value\>calculating;complex formulas in text\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>formulas; complex formulas in text\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>calculating;mean values\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\calculate_intext.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147406				0	bs	\<variable id=\"calculate_intext\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/calculate_intext.xhp\" name=\"Calculating Complex Formulas in Text Documents\"\>Calculating Complex Formulas in Text Documents\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\calculate_intext.xhp	0	help	par_id3145245				0	bs	You can use predefined functions in a formula, and then insert the result of the calculation into a text document.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\calculate_intext.xhp	0	help	par_id3152901				0	bs	For example, to calculate the mean value of three numbers, do the following:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\calculate_intext.xhp	0	help	par_id3145078				0	bs	Click in the document where you want to insert the formula, and then press F2.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\calculate_intext.xhp	0	help	par_id3156382				0	bs	Click the \<emph\>Formula \</emph\>icon, and choose "Mean" from the Statistical Functions list.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\calculate_intext.xhp	0	help	par_id3149692				0	bs	Type the three numbers, separated by vertical slashes (|).				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\calculate_intext.xhp	0	help	par_id3149481				0	bs	Press \<emph\>Enter\</emph\>. The result is inserted as a field into the document.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\calculate_intext.xhp	0	help	par_id3149823				0	bs	To edit the formula, double-click the field in the document.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\calculate.xhp	0	help	tit				0	bs	Calculating in Text Documents				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\calculate.xhp	0	help	bm_id3149909				0	bs	\<bookmark_value\>calculating; in text\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>formulas; calculating directly in text\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>formula bar in text\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\calculate.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149909				0	bs	\<variable id=\"calculate\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/calculate.xhp\" name=\"Calculating in Text Documents\"\>Calculating in Text Documents\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\calculate.xhp	0	help	par_id3149949				0	bs	You can insert a calculation directly into a text document or into a text table.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\calculate.xhp	0	help	par_id3149972				0	bs	Click in the document where you want to insert the calculation, and then press F2. If you are in a table cell, type an equals sign =.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\calculate.xhp	0	help	par_id3155547				0	bs	Type the calculation that you want to insert, for example, "=10000/12", and then press Enter.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\calculate.xhp	0	help	par_id3155565				0	bs	You can also click the \<emph\>Formula \</emph\>icon on the \<emph\>Formula Bar\</emph\>, and then choose a function for your formula.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_frame.xhp	0	help	tit				0	bs	Inserting, Editing, and Linking Text Frames				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_frame.xhp	0	help	bm_id3149487				0	bs	\<bookmark_value\>text frames; inserting/editing/linking\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>editing;text frames\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>inserting;text frames\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>moving;text frames\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>resizing;text frames\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>scaling; text frames\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>changing; size of text frames\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>linking frames\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>text flow; from frame to frame\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>frames; linking\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>text frames; linking\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>text;not printing\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>printing;hiding text from printing\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_frame.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149487				0	bs	\<variable id=\"text_frame\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/text_frame.xhp\" name=\"Inserting, Editing, and Linking Text Frames\"\>Inserting, Editing, and Linking Text Frames\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_frame.xhp	0	help	par_id3149842				0	bs	A text frame is a container for text and graphics that you can place anywhere on a page. You can also use a frame to apply a column layout to text.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_frame.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156104				0	bs	Inserting Text Frames				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_frame.xhp	0	help	par_id3149961				0	bs	Select the text that you want to include in the frame.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_frame.xhp	0	help	par_id3149602				0	bs	Choose \<emph\>Insert - Frame\</emph\>, and click OK.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_frame.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145115				0	bs	Editing Text Frames				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_frame.xhp	0	help	par_id3149578				0	bs	To edit the contents of a text frame, click in the frame, and make the changes that you want.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_frame.xhp	0	help	par_id3156239				0	bs	To edit a frame, select the frame, right-click, and then choose a formatting option. You can also right-click the selected frame, and choose \<emph\>Frame\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_frame.xhp	0	help	par_id3156261				0	bs	To resize a text frame, click an edge of frame, and drag one of the edges or corners of the frame. Hold down Shift while you drag to maintain the proportion of the frame.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_frame.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153386				0	bs	Hiding Text From Printing				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_frame.xhp	0	help	par_id3154262				0	bs	Any text frame can be set to a mode which allows viewing the text on screen, but hides the text from printing.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_frame.xhp	0	help	par_id3154858				0	bs	Select the text frame (you see the eight handles).				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_frame.xhp	0	help	par_id3155875				0	bs	Choose \<emph\>Format - Frame - Options\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_frame.xhp	0	help	par_id3155899				0	bs	In the \<emph\>Properties\</emph\> area, unmark the \<emph\>Print\</emph\> check box and click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_frame.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148701				0	bs	Linking Text Frames				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_frame.xhp	0	help	par_id3149986				0	bs	You can link text frames so that their contents automatically flow from one frame to another.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_frame.xhp	0	help	par_id3153025				0	bs	Click the edge of a frame that you want to link. Selection handles appear on the edges of the frame.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_frame.xhp	0	help	par_id3150223	87			0	bs	On the \<emph\>Frame\</emph\> Bar, click the \<emph\>Link Frames\</emph\> icon \<image id=\"img_id3148968\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_chainframes.png\" width=\"5.64mm\" height=\"5.64mm\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3148968\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_frame.xhp	0	help	par_id3150930				0	bs	Click the frame that you want to link to.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_frame.xhp	0	help	par_id3150947				0	bs	You can only link frames if:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_frame.xhp	0	help	par_id3150969				0	bs	The target frame is empty.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_frame.xhp	0	help	par_id3154365				0	bs	The target frame is not linked to another frame.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_frame.xhp	0	help	par_id3154383				0	bs	The source and the target frames are in the same section. For example, you cannot link a header frame to a footer frame.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_frame.xhp	0	help	par_id3145559				0	bs	The source frame does not have a next link.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_frame.xhp	0	help	par_id3145577				0	bs	The target or the source frame are not contained in each other.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_frame.xhp	0	help	par_id3151083				0	bs	When you select a linked frame, a line is displayed that connects the linked frames.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\ruler.xhp	0	help	tit				0	bs	Using Rulers				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\ruler.xhp	0	help	bm_id8186284				0	bs	\<bookmark_value\>rulers;using rulers\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>horizontal rulers\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>vertical rulers\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>indent settings on rulers\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>changing;indents\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>page margins on rulers\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>table cells;adjusting the width on rulers\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>showing;rulers\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>hiding;rulers\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>adjusting page margins and cell widths\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
