helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\number_date_conv.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156383				0	bs	\<variable id=\"number_date_conv\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/number_date_conv.xhp\" name=\"Turning Number Recognition On or Off in Tables\"\>Turning Number Recognition On or Off in Tables\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\number_date_conv.xhp	0	help	par_id3155179				0	bs	$[officename] can automatically format dates that you have entered into a table, according to the regional settings specified in your operating system.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\number_date_conv.xhp	0	help	par_id3149966				0	bs	Do one of the following:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\number_date_conv.xhp	0	help	par_id3155919				0	bs	Right-click in a table cell and choose \<emph\>Number recognition\</emph\>. When this feature is on, a check mark is displayed in front of the \<emph\>Number recognition \</emph\>command.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\print_preview.xhp	0	help	tit				0	bs	Previewing a Page Before Printing				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\print_preview.xhp	0	help	bm_id3155179				0	bs	\<bookmark_value\>printing; previews\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>previews; print layouts\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>print layout checks\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>page views\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
