helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\stylist_fromselect.xhp	0	help	par_id3149829				0	bs	You can quickly create a new style from an existing style that you have applied manual formatting to.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\stylist_fromselect.xhp	0	help	par_id3156097				0	bs	Choose \<emph\>Format - Styles and Formatting\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\stylist_fromselect.xhp	0	help	par_id3153402				0	bs	Click the icon of the style category that you want to create.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\stylist_fromselect.xhp	0	help	par_id3153119				0	bs	Click in the document where you want to copy the style from, for example, in a paragraph that you applied manual formatting to.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\stylist_fromselect.xhp	0	help	par_id3156260				0	bs	Type a name in the \<emph\>Style Name \</emph\>box.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\stylist_fromselect.xhp	0	help	par_id3154411				0	bs	Click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\stylist_fromselect.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153373				0	bs	To create a new style by drag-and-drop:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\stylist_fromselect.xhp	0	help	par_id3154233				0	bs	Choose \<emph\>Format - Styles and Formatting\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\stylist_fromselect.xhp	0	help	par_id3154258				0	bs	Click the icon of the style category that you want to create.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\stylist_fromselect.xhp	0	help	par_id3154851				0	bs	Select at least one character, or object, in the style that you want to copy. For page and frame styles, select at least one character or object in the page or frame.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\stylist_fromselect.xhp	0	help	par_id3154871				0	bs	Drag the character or object to the Styles and Formatting window and release.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\stylist_fromselect.xhp	0	help	par_idN107B2				0	bs	For Paragraph and Character Styles, you can drag-and-drop onto the respective icon in the Styles and Formatting window. You do not need to open that style category in advance.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\stylist_fromselect.xhp	0	help	par_idN107B5				0	bs	You can also drag-and-drop a frame into the Styles and Formatting window to create a new frame style: Click the frame, wait a moment with the mouse button pressed down, but without moving the mouse, then drag to the Styles and Formatting window and drop the frame onto the Frame Styles icon.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
