helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\autotext.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155521				0	bs	\<variable id=\"autotext\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/autotext.xhp\" name=\"Using AutoText\"\>Using AutoText\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\autotext.xhp	0	help	par_id3150534				0	bs	In $[officename] Writer, you can store text - also containing graphics, tables, and fields - as AutoText, so that you can quickly insert the text later on. If you want, you can also store formatted text.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\autotext.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155539				0	bs	Creating an AutoText Entry				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\autotext.xhp	0	help	par_id3155560				0	bs	Select the text, text with graphics, table, or field that you want to save as an AutoText entry. A graphic can only be stored if it is anchored as a character and is preceded and followed by at least one text character.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\autotext.xhp	0	help	par_id3155581				0	bs	Choose\<emph\> Edit - AutoText\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\autotext.xhp	0	help	par_id3147761				0	bs	Select the category where you want to store the AutoText.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\autotext.xhp	0	help	par_id3147779				0	bs	Type a name that is longer than four characters. This allows you to use the \<emph\>Display remainder of name as suggestion while typing\</emph\> AutoText option. If you want, you can modify the proposed shortcut.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\autotext.xhp	0	help	par_id3147807	60			0	bs	Click the \<emph\>AutoText\</emph\> button, and then choose \<emph\>New\</emph\>. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\autotext.xhp	0	help	par_idN10732				0	bs	Click the \<emph\>Close\</emph\> button.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\autotext.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147282				0	bs	Inserting an AutoText Entry				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\autotext.xhp	0	help	par_id3145597				0	bs	Click in your document where you want to insert an AutoText entry.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\autotext.xhp	0	help	par_id3145615				0	bs	Choose \<link href=\"text/swriter/01/02120000.xhp\" name=\"Edit - AutoText\"\>\<emph\>Edit - AutoText\</emph\>\</link\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\autotext.xhp	0	help	par_id3145644				0	bs	Select the AutoText that you want to insert, and then click\<emph\> Insert\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\autotext.xhp	0	help	par_id3145668	30			0	bs	You can also type the shortcut for an AutoText entry, and then press F3, or click the arrow next to the \<emph\>AutoText \</emph\>icon on the \<emph\>Insert\</emph\> bar, and then choose an AutoText entry. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\autotext.xhp	0	help	par_id3155090	43			0	bs	To quickly enter a %PRODUCTNAME Math formula, type "FN", and then press F3. If you insert more than one formula, the formulae are sequentially numbered. To insert dummy text, type "DT", and then press F3. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\autotext.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155115				0	bs	To Print a List of AutoText Entries				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\autotext.xhp	0	help	par_id3155136				0	bs	Choose \<emph\>Tools - Macros - Organize Macros - %PRODUCTNAME Basic\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\autotext.xhp	0	help	par_id3155160				0	bs	In the \<emph\>Macro from\</emph\> list, double-click "%PRODUCTNAME Macros - Gimmicks".				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\autotext.xhp	0	help	par_id3151277				0	bs	Select "AutoText" and then click \<emph\>Run\</emph\>. A list of the current AutoText entries is generated in a separate text document.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\autotext.xhp	0	help	par_id3151304				0	bs	Choose \<emph\>File - Print\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\autotext.xhp	0	help	hd_id3151327				0	bs	Using AutoText in Network Installations				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\autotext.xhp	0	help	par_id3151355				0	bs	You can store AutoText entries in different directories on a network.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\autotext.xhp	0	help	par_id3151370				0	bs	For example, you can store "read-only" AutoText entries for your company on a central server, and user-defined AutoText entries in a local directory.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\autotext.xhp	0	help	par_id3151390				0	bs	To view the paths for the current AutoText directories, choose \<emph\>Tools - Options - $[officename] - Paths\</emph\>, select \<emph\>AutoText\</emph\>, and then click \<emph\>Edit\</emph\>. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\autotext.xhp	0	help	par_id3154960				0	bs	Two directories are listed here. The first entry is on the server installation and the second entry is in the user directory. If there are two AutoText entries with the same name in both directories, the entry from the user directory is used.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
