helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\insert_graphic_fromdraw.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155917				0	bs	\<variable id=\"insert_graphic_fromdraw\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/insert_graphic_fromdraw.xhp\" name=\"Inserting Graphics From $[officename] Draw or Impress\"\>Inserting Graphics From $[officename] Draw or Impress\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\insert_graphic_fromdraw.xhp	0	help	par_id3153414				0	bs	Open the document where you want to insert the object.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\insert_graphic_fromdraw.xhp	0	help	par_id3149640				0	bs	Open the Draw or Impress document containing the object that you want to copy.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\insert_graphic_fromdraw.xhp	0	help	par_id3156250				0	bs	Drag to the document where you want to insert the object.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_edit.xhp	0	help	tit				0	bs	Updating, Editing and Deleting Indexes and Tables of Contents				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_edit.xhp	0	help	bm_id3149695				0	bs	\<bookmark_value\>indexes; editing/updating/deleting\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>tables of contents; editing and deleting\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>updating;indexes/tables of contents\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>editing;indexes/tables of contents\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>deleting;indexes/tables of contents\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_edit.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149695				0	bs	\<variable id=\"indices_edit\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/indices_edit.xhp\" name=\"Updating, Editing and Deleting Indexes and Tables of Contents\"\>Updating, Editing and Deleting Indexes and Tables of Contents\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_edit.xhp	0	help	par_id3155856				0	bs	Place the cursor in the index or table of contents.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_edit.xhp	0	help	par_id3154248				0	bs	Right-click and choose an editing option from the menu.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_edit.xhp	0	help	par_id3155872				0	bs	You can also make changes directly to an index or table of contents. Right-click in the index or table of contents, choose \<emph\>Edit Index/Table\</emph\>, click \<emph\>Index/Table\</emph\> tab, and then clear the \<emph\>Protected from manual changes\</emph\> check box.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\chapter_numbering.xhp	0	help	tit				0	bs	Outline Numbering				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\chapter_numbering.xhp	0	help	bm_id3147682				0	bs	\<bookmark_value\>outline numbering\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>removing;heading numbers\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>chapter numbering\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>headings; numbering\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>numbering;headings\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>headings; own paragraph styles\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\chapter_numbering.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147682				0	bs	\<variable id=\"chapter_numbering\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/chapter_numbering.xhp\" name=\"Outline Numbering\"\>Outline Numbering\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\chapter_numbering.xhp	0	help	par_id3155605				0	bs	You can modify the heading hierarchy or assign a level in the hierarchy to a custom paragraph style. You can also add chapter and section numbering to heading paragraph styles. By default, the "Heading 1" paragraph style is at the top of the outline hierarchy.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\chapter_numbering.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155626				0	bs	To add automatic numbering to a heading style:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\chapter_numbering.xhp	0	help	par_id3154255				0	bs	Choose \<emph\>Tools - Outline Numbering\</emph\>, and then click the \<emph\>Numbering \</emph\>tab.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\chapter_numbering.xhp	0	help	par_id3155891				0	bs	In the \<emph\>Paragraph Style \</emph\>box, select the heading style that you want to add a chapter number to.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\chapter_numbering.xhp	0	help	par_id3150513				0	bs	In the\<emph\> Numbers\</emph\> box, select the numbering style that you want to use, and then click\<emph\> OK\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\chapter_numbering.xhp	0	help	par_idN107CE				0	bs	To remove automatic outline numbering from a heading paragraph:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\chapter_numbering.xhp	0	help	par_idN107D5				0	bs	Click at the beginning of the text in the heading paragraph, after the number.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\chapter_numbering.xhp	0	help	par_idN107D9				0	bs	Press the \<item type=\"keycode\"\>Backspace\</item\> key to delete the number.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\chapter_numbering.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155552				0	bs	To use a custom paragraph style as a heading:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\chapter_numbering.xhp	0	help	par_id3155571				0	bs	Choose \<emph\>Tools - Outline Numbering\</emph\>, and then click the \<emph\>Numbering \</emph\>tab.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\chapter_numbering.xhp	0	help	par_id3147758				0	bs	Select the custom style in the \<emph\>Paragraph Style\</emph\> box.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\chapter_numbering.xhp	0	help	par_id3147782	39			0	bs	Click the heading level that you want to assign to the custom paragraph style in the\<emph\> Level\</emph\> list. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\chapter_numbering.xhp	0	help	par_id3147808				0	bs	Click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\search_regexp.xhp	0	help	tit				0	bs	Using Wildcards in Text Searches				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\search_regexp.xhp	0	help	bm_id3150099				0	bs	\<bookmark_value\>searching; with wildcards\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>regular expressions;searching\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>wildcards; searching in text\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>examples for regular expressions\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\search_regexp.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150099				0	bs	\<variable id=\"search_regexp\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/search_regexp.xhp\"\>Using Wildcards in Text Searches\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\search_regexp.xhp	0	help	par_id3155182				0	bs	You can use wildcards when you find and replace text in a document. For example, "s.n" finds "sun" and "son".				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\search_regexp.xhp	0	help	par_id3155907				0	bs	Choose \<emph\>Edit - Find & Replace\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\search_regexp.xhp	0	help	par_id3155861				0	bs	Select the \<emph\>Regular expressions\</emph\> check box.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\search_regexp.xhp	0	help	par_id3149843				0	bs	In the \<emph\>Search for \</emph\>box, type the search term and the wildcard(s) that you want to use in your search.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\search_regexp.xhp	0	help	par_id3156113				0	bs	Click \<emph\>Find \</emph\>or\<emph\> Find All\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\search_regexp.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153401				0	bs	Regular Expression Examples				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\search_regexp.xhp	0	help	par_id3149641				0	bs	The wildcard for a single character is a period (.).				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\search_regexp.xhp	0	help	par_id3153136				0	bs	The wildcard for zero or more occurrences of the previous character is an asterisk. For example: "123*" finds "12" "123", and "1233".				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\search_regexp.xhp	0	help	par_id3149609				0	bs	The wildcard combination to search for zero or more occurrences of any character is a period and asterisk (.*).				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\search_regexp.xhp	0	help	par_id3149854				0	bs	The wildcard for the end of a paragraph is a dollar sign ($). The wildcard character combination for the start of a paragraph is a caret and a period (^.).				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\search_regexp.xhp	0	help	par_id3153414				0	bs	You can only search for regular expressions within the same paragraph. That is, you cannot search for one term in a paragraph and a different term in the next paragraph.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\search_regexp.xhp	0	help	par_id3149875				0	bs	\<link href=\"text/shared/01/02100001.xhp\" name=\"List of Wildcards\"\>List of Wildcards\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\table_cells.xhp	0	help	tit				0	bs	Adding or Deleting a Row or Column to a Table Using the Keyboard				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\table_cells.xhp	0	help	bm_id3156377				0	bs	\<bookmark_value\>rows; inserting/deleting in tables by keyboard\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>columns; inserting/deleting in tables by keyboard\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>text tables; editing by keyboard\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>keyboard;editing text tables\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>splitting cells by keyboard\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>merging;cells, by keyboard\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>deleting;rows/columns, by keyboard\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>adding;rows/columns, by keyboard\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\table_cells.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156377				0	bs	\<variable id=\"table_cells\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/table_cells.xhp\" name=\"Adding or Deleting a Row or Column to a Table Using the Keyboard\"\>Adding or Deleting a Row or Column to a Table Using the Keyboard\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\table_cells.xhp	0	help	par_id3149487				0	bs	You can add or delete rows or columns in table as well as split or merge table cells using the keyboard.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\table_cells.xhp	0	help	par_id3155906				0	bs	To insert a new row in a table, place the cursor in a table cell, press \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Option \</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Alt\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+Ins, and then press the up or down arrow key. You can also move the cursor to the last cell in the table, and then press Tab.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\table_cells.xhp	0	help	par_id3147412				0	bs	To insert a new column, place the cursor in a table cell, press \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Option \</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Alt\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+Ins, and then press the left or right arrow key.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\table_cells.xhp	0	help	par_id3156096				0	bs	To split a table cell instead of adding a column, press \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Option \</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Alt\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+Ins, and then hold down \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command \</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> while you press the left or right arrow key.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\table_cells.xhp	0	help	par_id3153408				0	bs	To delete a row, place the cursor in a table cell, press \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Option \</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Alt\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+Del, and then press the up or down arrow key.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\table_cells.xhp	0	help	par_id3149626				0	bs	To delete a column, place the cursor in a table cell, press \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Option \</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Alt\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+Del, and then press the left or the right arrow key.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\table_cells.xhp	0	help	par_id3149612				0	bs	To merge a table into an adjacent cell, place the cursor in the cell, press \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Option \</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Alt\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+Del, hold down \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command \</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>, and then press the left or the right arrow key.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\section_edit.xhp	0	help	tit				0	bs	Editing Sections				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\section_edit.xhp	0	help	par_id3155858				0	bs	You can protect, hide, and convert sections to normal text in your document.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\section_edit.xhp	0	help	par_id3154224				0	bs	Choose \<link href=\"text/swriter/01/02170000.xhp\" name=\"Format - Sections\"\>\<emph\>Format - Sections\</emph\>\</link\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\section_edit.xhp	0	help	par_id3153397				0	bs	Do one of the following:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\section_edit.xhp	0	help	par_id3156255				0	bs	\<link href=\"text/swriter/01/02170000.xhp\" name=\"Format - Sections\"\>Format - Sections\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\anchor_object.xhp	0	help	tit				0	bs	Positioning Objects				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\anchor_object.xhp	0	help	bm_id3147828				0	bs	\<bookmark_value\>objects;anchoring options\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>positioning;objects (guide)\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>anchoring;objects\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>frames;anchoring options\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>pictures;anchoring options\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>centering;images on HTML pages\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\anchor_object.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147828				0	bs	\<variable id=\"anchor_object\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/anchor_object.xhp\" name=\"Positioning Objects\"\>Positioning Objects\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\anchor_object.xhp	0	help	par_id3147251				0	bs	You can use anchors to position an object, graphic, or frame in a document. An anchored item remains in place, or moves when you modify the document. The following anchoring options are available:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\anchor_object.xhp	0	help	par_id3145599				0	bs	Anchoring				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\anchor_object.xhp	0	help	par_id3145622				0	bs	Effect				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\anchor_object.xhp	0	help	par_id3145650				0	bs	As character				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\anchor_object.xhp	0	help	par_id3151181				0	bs	Anchors the selected item as a character in the current text. If the height of the selected item is greater than the current font size, the height of the line containing the item is increased.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\anchor_object.xhp	0	help	par_idN10674				0	bs	To center an image on an HTML page, insert the image, anchor it "as character", then center the paragraph.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\anchor_object.xhp	0	help	par_id3151212				0	bs	To character				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\anchor_object.xhp	0	help	par_id3151235				0	bs	Anchors the selected item to a character.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\anchor_object.xhp	0	help	par_id3155071				0	bs	To paragraph				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\anchor_object.xhp	0	help	par_id3155094				0	bs	Anchors the selected item to the current paragraph.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\anchor_object.xhp	0	help	par_id3155122				0	bs	To page				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\anchor_object.xhp	0	help	par_id3155144				0	bs	Anchors the selected item to the current page.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\anchor_object.xhp	0	help	par_id3145674				0	bs	To frame				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\anchor_object.xhp	0	help	par_id3145697				0	bs	Anchors the selected item to the surrounding frame.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\anchor_object.xhp	0	help	par_id3145715				0	bs	When you insert an object, graphic, or frame, an anchor icon appears where the item is anchored. You can position an anchored item by dragging the item to another location. To change the anchoring options of an item, right-click the item, and then choose an option from the \<emph\>Anchor \</emph\>submenu.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
