helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_animation.xhp	0	help	hd_id3151182				0	bs	\<variable id=\"text_animation\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/text_animation.xhp\" name=\"Animating Text\"\>Animating Text\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_animation.xhp	0	help	par_id3145080				0	bs	You can only animate text that is contained in a drawing object, such as rectangles, lines, or text objects. For example, draw a rectangle, then double-click the rectangle and enter your text.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_animation.xhp	0	help	par_id3149811				0	bs	Select the drawing object containing the text that you want to animate.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_animation.xhp	0	help	par_id3155178				0	bs	Choose \<emph\>Format - Text\</emph\>, and then click the\<emph\> Text Animation\</emph\> tab.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_animation.xhp	0	help	par_id3149819				0	bs	In the \<emph\>Effect \</emph\>box, select the animation that you want.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_animation.xhp	0	help	par_id3145786				0	bs	Set the properties of the effect, and then click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\table_select.xhp	0	help	tit				0	bs	Selecting Tables, Rows, and Columns				2002-02-02 02:02:02
