helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\table_select.xhp	0	help	par_idN105F0				0	bs	\<variable id=\"table_select\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/table_select.xhp\"\>Selecting Tables, Rows, and Columns\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\table_select.xhp	0	help	par_idN1060E				0	bs	You can select a table in a text document with a keyboard or with a mouse.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\table_select.xhp	0	help	par_idN10614				0	bs	To select a table with the keyboard, move the cursor into the table, and then press \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command \</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+A until all the cells are selected.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\table_select.xhp	0	help	par_idN10633				0	bs	To select a table with the mouse, move the mouse pointer to a position just above and left of the table. The mouse pointer becomes a diagonal arrow. Click to select the table.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\table_select.xhp	0	help	par_idN10637				0	bs	To select a row or column with the mouse, point to a position just left of the row or above the column. The mouse pointer becomes an arrow. Click to select the row or column.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\calculate_multitable.xhp	0	help	tit				0	bs	Calculating Across Tables				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\calculate_multitable.xhp	0	help	bm_id3154248				0	bs	\<bookmark_value\>calculating; across multiple text tables\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>text tables;calculating across\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\calculate_multitable.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154248				0	bs	\<variable id=\"calculate_multitable\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/calculate_multitable.xhp\" name=\"Calculating Across Tables\"\>Calculating Across Tables\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\calculate_multitable.xhp	0	help	par_id3147773				0	bs	You can perform calculations that span across more than one table in a text document.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\calculate_multitable.xhp	0	help	par_id3147795				0	bs	Open a text document, insert two tables, and type numbers in a few cells in both tables.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\calculate_multitable.xhp	0	help	par_id3147815				0	bs	Place your cursor in an empty cell in one of the tables.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\calculate_multitable.xhp	0	help	par_id3147833				0	bs	Press F2.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\calculate_multitable.xhp	0	help	par_id3147228				0	bs	In the \<emph\>Formula Bar\</emph\>, enter the function that you want to perform, for example, "=SUM".				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\calculate_multitable.xhp	0	help	par_id3147254				0	bs	Click in a cell containing a number, press the plus sign (+), and then click in a different cell containing a number.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\calculate_multitable.xhp	0	help	par_id3147274				0	bs	Press \<emph\>Enter\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
