helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\auto_off.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147812				0	bs	\<variable id=\"auto_off\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/auto_off.xhp\" name=\"Turning Off AutoFormat and AutoCorrect\"\>Turning Off AutoFormat and AutoCorrect\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\auto_off.xhp	0	help	par_id3147833	2			0	bs	By default, $[officename] automatically corrects many common typing errors and applies formatting while you type. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\auto_off.xhp	0	help	par_idN1081B				0	bs	To quickly undo an automatic correction or completion, press \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command \</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+Z. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\auto_off.xhp	0	help	par_idN10846				0	bs	To turn off most AutoFormat features, remove the check mark from the menu \<emph\>Format - AutoFormat - While Typing\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\auto_off.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147251				0	bs	To remove a word from the AutoCorrect list:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
