helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\fields_userdata.xhp	0	help	par_id3153167				0	bs	If you want, you can use a condition to hide specific text in your document from a specific user.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\fields_userdata.xhp	0	help	par_id3153190				0	bs	Select the text in the document that you want to hide.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\fields_userdata.xhp	0	help	par_id3145273				0	bs	Choose \<emph\>Insert - Section\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\fields_userdata.xhp	0	help	par_id3145297				0	bs	In the \<emph\>Hide \</emph\>area, select the \<emph\>Hide\</emph\> check box.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\fields_userdata.xhp	0	help	par_id3155533	105			0	bs	In the \<emph\>With Condition\</emph\> box, type \<emph\>user_lastname == "Doe"\</emph\>, where "Doe" is the last name of the user that you want to hide the text from. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\fields_userdata.xhp	0	help	par_id3155573				0	bs	Click \<emph\>Insert\</emph\> and then save the document.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
