helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\dragdroptext.xhp	0	help	par_id3155606				0	bs	Do one of the following:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\fields.xhp	0	help	tit				0	bs	About Fields				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\fields.xhp	0	help	bm_id3145576				0	bs	\<bookmark_value\>fields; using\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>updating;fields\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>Help tips;fields\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>properties;fields\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>disabling field highlighting\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>changing;field shadings\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>viewing;fields\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\fields.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145576				0	bs	\<variable id=\"fields\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/fields.xhp\" name=\"About Fields\"\>About Fields\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\fields.xhp	0	help	par_id3154246				0	bs	Fields are used for data that changes in a document, such as the current date or the total number of pages in a document.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\fields.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154262				0	bs	Viewing Fields				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\fields.xhp	0	help	par_id3150509				0	bs	Fields consist of a field name and the field content. To switch the field display between the field name or the field content, choose \<link href=\"text/swriter/01/03090000.xhp\" name=\"View - Fields\"\>\<emph\>View - Field Names\</emph\>\</link\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\fields.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153166				0	bs	Field Properties				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\fields.xhp	0	help	par_id3153180				0	bs	Most field types in a document, including database fields, store and display variable values.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\fields.xhp	0	help	par_id3155533				0	bs	The following field types execute an action when you click the field:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\fields.xhp	0	help	par_id3155582				0	bs	Field Type				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\fields.xhp	0	help	par_id3147760				0	bs	Property				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\fields.xhp	0	help	par_id3147789				0	bs	Placeholder				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\fields.xhp	0	help	par_id3147812				0	bs	Opens a dialog to insert the object for which the placeholder was set.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\fields.xhp	0	help	par_id3147216				0	bs	Insert Reference				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\fields.xhp	0	help	par_id3147239				0	bs	Moves the mouse pointer to the reference.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\fields.xhp	0	help	par_id3147267				0	bs	Run macro				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\fields.xhp	0	help	par_id3147290				0	bs	Runs a macro.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\fields.xhp	0	help	par_id3145614				0	bs	Input Field				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\fields.xhp	0	help	par_id3145637				0	bs	Opens a dialog to edit the contents of the field.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\fields.xhp	0	help	par_id3151244				0	bs	Placeholder, hidden text, insert reference, variable, database, and user-defined fields display a help tip when you rest the mouse pointer over the field in a document. To enable this feature, ensure that the \<emph\>Extended Tips \</emph\>option is selected in the \<emph\>Help\</emph\> menu.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\fields.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155937				0	bs	Updating Fields				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\fields.xhp	0	help	par_id3155963				0	bs	To update all of the fields in a document, press F9, or choose \<emph\>Edit - Select All\</emph\>, and then press F9.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\fields.xhp	0	help	par_id3155984				0	bs	To update a field that was inserted from a database, select the field, and then press F9.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\hyperlinks.xhp	0	help	tit				0	bs	Inserting Hyperlinks With the Navigator				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\hyperlinks.xhp	0	help	bm_id3155845				0	bs	\<bookmark_value\>hyperlinks; inserting from Navigator\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>inserting; hyperlinks from Navigator\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>cross-references; inserting with Navigator\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>adding;hyperlinks\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>Navigator;inserting hyperlinks\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\hyperlinks.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155845				0	bs	\<variable id=\"hyperlinks\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/hyperlinks.xhp\" name=\"Inserting Hyperlinks With the Navigator\"\>Inserting Hyperlinks With the Navigator\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\hyperlinks.xhp	0	help	par_id3155858				0	bs	You can insert a cross-reference as a hyperlink in your document using the Navigator. You can even cross-reference items from other \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> documents. If you click the hyperlink when the document is opened in \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\>, you are taken to the cross-referenced item.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\hyperlinks.xhp	0	help	par_id3149833				0	bs	Open the document(s) containing the items you want to cross-reference.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\hyperlinks.xhp	0	help	par_id3148846				0	bs	On the Standard bar, click the \<emph\>Navigator\</emph\> icon.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\hyperlinks.xhp	0	help	par_id3156108				0	bs	Click the arrow next to the \<emph\>Drag Mode\</emph\> icon, and ensure that \<emph\>Insert as Hyperlink \</emph\>is selected.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\hyperlinks.xhp	0	help	par_id3153396				0	bs	In the list at the bottom of the Navigator, select the document containing the item that you want to cross-reference.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\hyperlinks.xhp	0	help	par_id3153416				0	bs	In the Navigator list, click the plus sign next to the item that you want to insert as a hyperlink.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\hyperlinks.xhp	0	help	par_id3153133				0	bs	Drag the item to where you want to insert the hyperlink in the document.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\hyperlinks.xhp	0	help	par_id3149635				0	bs	The name of the item is inserted in the document as an underlined hyperlink.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\stylist_update.xhp	0	help	tit				0	bs	Updating Styles From Selections				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\stylist_update.xhp	0	help	bm_id3155915				0	bs	\<bookmark_value\>Stylist, see Styles and Formatting window\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>styles; updating from selections\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>templates; updating from selections\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>Styles and Formatting window; updating from selections\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>updating; styles, from selections\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\stylist_update.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155915				0	bs	\<variable id=\"stylist_update\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/stylist_update.xhp\" name=\"Updating Styles From Selections\"\>Updating Styles From Selections\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\stylist_update.xhp	0	help	par_id3149838				0	bs	Choose \<emph\>Format - Styles and Formatting\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\stylist_update.xhp	0	help	par_id3156107				0	bs	Click the icon of the style category that you want to update.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\stylist_update.xhp	0	help	par_id3149283				0	bs	Click in the document where you want to copy the updated style from, for example, in a paragraph that you applied manual formatting to.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\stylist_update.xhp	0	help	par_id3153402				0	bs	In the Styles and Formatting windows, click the style that you want to update.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\stylist_update.xhp	0	help	par_id3155498				0	bs	\<link href=\"text/swriter/01/05140000.xhp\" name=\"Styles and Formatting\"\>Styles and Formatting\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\tablemode.xhp	0	help	tit				0	bs	Modifying Rows and Columns by Keyboard				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\tablemode.xhp	0	help	bm_id3155856				0	bs	\<bookmark_value\>table mode selection\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>proportional distribution of tables\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>relative distribution of table cells\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>tables; adapting the width by keyboard\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>cells; adapting the width by keyboard\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>keyboard;modifying rows/columns\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\tablemode.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155856				0	bs	\<variable id=\"tablemode\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/tablemode.xhp\" name=\"Modifying the Behavior of Rows and Columns for Table\"\>Modifying Rows and Columns by Keyboard\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\tablemode.xhp	0	help	par_id3149835				0	bs	When you insert or delete cells, rows or columns in a table, the \<emph\>Behavior of rows/columns\</emph\> options determine how the neighboring elements are affected. For example, you can only insert new rows and columns into a table with \<emph\>Fixed\</emph\> row and column dimensions if space permits.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\tablemode.xhp	0	help	par_id7344279				0	bs	Note that these properties are valid only for changes to the column width that are made using the keyboard. Using the mouse, you are free to make any column width changes.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\tablemode.xhp	0	help	par_id3149638				0	bs	\<emph\>Fixed\</emph\> - changes only affect the adjacent cell, and not the entire table. For example, when you widen a cell, the adjacent cell becomes narrower, but the width of the table remains constant.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\tablemode.xhp	0	help	par_id3149613				0	bs	\<emph\>Fixed, proportional\</emph\> - changes affect the entire table, and wide cells shrink more than narrow cells. For example, when you widen a cell, the adjacent cells become proportionally narrower, but the width of the table remains constant.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\tablemode.xhp	0	help	par_id3149864				0	bs	\<emph\>Variable\</emph\> - changes affect the table size. For example, when you widen a cell, the width of the table increases.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\insert_graphic_dialog.xhp	0	help	tit				0	bs	Inserting a Graphic From a File				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\insert_graphic_dialog.xhp	0	help	bm_id3154896				0	bs	\<bookmark_value\>pictures; inserting by dialog\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>inserting; pictures by dialog\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\insert_graphic_dialog.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154896				0	bs	\<variable id=\"insert_graphic_dialog\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/insert_graphic_dialog.xhp\" name=\"Inserting a Graphic From a File\"\>Inserting a Graphic From a File\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\insert_graphic_dialog.xhp	0	help	par_id3155914				0	bs	Click in the document where you want to insert the graphic.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\insert_graphic_dialog.xhp	0	help	par_id3155864				0	bs	Choose \<link href=\"text/shared/01/04140000.xhp\" name=\"Insert - Picture - From File\"\>\<emph\>Insert - Picture - From File\</emph\>\</link\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\insert_graphic_dialog.xhp	0	help	par_id3156021				0	bs	Locate the graphic file that you want to insert, and then click \<emph\>Open\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\insert_graphic_dialog.xhp	0	help	par_id3153396				0	bs	By default, the inserted graphic is centered above the paragraph that you clicked in.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
