helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\printer_tray.xhp	0	help	bm_id6609088				0	bs	\<bookmark_value\>selecting;paper trays\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>paper trays;selecting\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\printer_tray.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155909				0	bs	\<variable id=\"printer_tray\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/printer_tray.xhp\" name=\"Selecting printer paper trays\"\>Selecting Printer Paper Trays\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\printer_tray.xhp	0	help	par_id3155858				0	bs	Use page styles to specify different paper sources for different pages in your document.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\printer_tray.xhp	0	help	par_id3149841				0	bs	Choose \<emph\>Format - Styles and Formatting\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\printer_tray.xhp	0	help	par_id3156108				0	bs	Click the \<emph\>Page Styles \</emph\>icon.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\printer_tray.xhp	0	help	par_id3155066				0	bs	Right-click the page style in the list that you want to specify the paper source for, and then choose \<emph\>Modify\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\printer_tray.xhp	0	help	par_id3153416				0	bs	In the \<emph\>Paper tray \</emph\>box, select the paper tray that you want to use.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\printer_tray.xhp	0	help	par_id3153140				0	bs	Click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\printer_tray.xhp	0	help	par_id3149649				0	bs	Repeat steps 1-5 for each page style that you want to specify the paper for.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\printer_tray.xhp	0	help	par_id3149616				0	bs	Apply the page style to the pages that you want.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
