helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\footnote_with_line.xhp	0	help	tit				0	bs	Spacing Between Footnotes				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\footnote_with_line.xhp	0	help	bm_id3147683				0	bs	\<bookmark_value\>spacing; endnotes/footnotes\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>endnotes; spacing\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>footnotes; spacing\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>borders;footnotes/endnotes\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>lines;footnotes/endnotes\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\footnote_with_line.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147683				0	bs	\<variable id=\"footnote_with_line\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/footnote_with_line.xhp\" name=\"Spacing Between Footnotes\"\>Spacing Between Footnotes\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\footnote_with_line.xhp	0	help	par_id3145808				0	bs	If you want to increase the spacing between footnote or endnote texts, you can add a top and bottom border to the corresponding paragraph style.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\footnote_with_line.xhp	0	help	par_id3155603				0	bs	Click in a footnote or endnote.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\footnote_with_line.xhp	0	help	par_id3155620				0	bs	Choose \<emph\>Format - Styles and Formatting\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\footnote_with_line.xhp	0	help	par_id3154251				0	bs	Right-click the Paragraph Style that you want to modify, for example, "Footnote", and choose \<emph\>Modify\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\footnote_with_line.xhp	0	help	par_id3155884				0	bs	Click the \<link href=\"text/shared/01/05030500.xhp\" name=\"Borders\"\>\<emph\>Borders\</emph\>\</link\> tab.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\footnote_with_line.xhp	0	help	par_id3147110				0	bs	In the \<emph\>Default \</emph\>area, click the \<emph\>Set Top and Bottom Borders Only\</emph\> icon.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\footnote_with_line.xhp	0	help	par_id3150931				0	bs	In the \<emph\>Line\</emph\> area, click a line in the \<emph\>Style \</emph\>list.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\footnote_with_line.xhp	0	help	par_id3150961				0	bs	Select "White" in the \<emph\>Color \</emph\>box. If the background of the page is not white, select the color that best matches the background color.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\footnote_with_line.xhp	0	help	par_id3150519				0	bs	In the \<emph\>Spacing to contents\</emph\> area, clear the \<emph\>Synchronize\</emph\> check box.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\footnote_with_line.xhp	0	help	par_id3150709				0	bs	Enter a value in the \<emph\>Top \</emph\>and \<emph\>Bottom \</emph\>boxes.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\footnote_with_line.xhp	0	help	par_id3150740				0	bs	Click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\footnote_with_line.xhp	0	help	par_id3148846				0	bs	\<link href=\"text/shared/01/05030500.xhp\" name=\"Format - Paragraph - Borders\"\>Format - Paragraph - Borders\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\removing_line_breaks.xhp	0	help	tit				0	bs	Removing Line Breaks				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\removing_line_breaks.xhp	0	help	bm_id3149687				0	bs	\<bookmark_value\>hard returns;finding & replacing\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>paragraph marks;finding & replacing\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>line breaks;removing\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>removing; line breaks\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>copies;removing line breaks\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\removing_line_breaks.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155916				0	bs	\<variable id=\"removing_line_breaks\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/removing_line_breaks.xhp\"\>Removing Line Breaks\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\removing_line_breaks.xhp	0	help	par_id3155858				0	bs	Use the AutoFormat feature to remove line breaks that occur within sentences. Unwanted line breaks can occur when you copy text from another source and paste it into a text document.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\removing_line_breaks.xhp	0	help	par_id3153413	3			0	bs	This AutoFormat feature only works on text that is formatted with the "Default" paragraph style. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\removing_line_breaks.xhp	0	help	par_id3153138	5			0	bs	Choose \<emph\>Tools - AutoCorrect.\</emph\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\removing_line_breaks.xhp	0	help	par_id3149645				0	bs	On the \<emph\>Options\</emph\> tab, ensure that \<emph\>Combine single line paragraphs if length greater than 50%\</emph\> is selected. To change the minimum percentage for the line length, double-click the option in the list, and then enter a new percentage.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\removing_line_breaks.xhp	0	help	par_id3145093				0	bs	Click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\removing_line_breaks.xhp	0	help	par_id3145118				0	bs	Select the text containing the line breaks that you want to remove.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\removing_line_breaks.xhp	0	help	par_id3156253				0	bs	In the \<emph\>Apply Style \</emph\>box on the \<emph\>Formatting\</emph\> bar, choose \<emph\>Default\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
