helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01020400.xhp	0	help	tit				0	bs	Mozilla Plug-in				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01020400.xhp	0	help	par_idN105D5				0	bs	Specifies to use the Mozilla plug-in to show %PRODUCTNAME documents.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01020400.xhp	0	help	par_idN105D8				0	bs	When you click a hyperlink to a %PRODUCTNAME document in your Mozilla or Netscape browser, one of the following can happen:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01020400.xhp	0	help	par_idN105DE				0	bs	The browser asks you whether you want to save the document on your disk, or whether you want to use an application to open the document. This request dialog appears by default when you click a hyperlink to a %PRODUCTNAME document the first time and you did not enable the Mozilla plug-in.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01020400.xhp	0	help	par_idN105E2				0	bs	The browser downloads the document to a temporary folder, then tells your system to run %PRODUCTNAME and open the document in %PRODUCTNAME. This is the default when you did not enable the Mozilla plug-in and chose to open the document with %PRODUCTNAME when you were first asked.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01020400.xhp	0	help	par_idN105E6				0	bs	The browser opens a new browser window that shows some of the %PRODUCTNAME icons, and displays the document in the browser window. This is the default when you enable the Mozilla plug-in. When you click the \<emph\>Edit File\</emph\> icon, a copy of the document is downloaded to a temporary folder on your disk, then %PRODUCTNAME starts and loads the copy for editing.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01020400.xhp	0	help	par_idN105F5				0	bs	Viewing of %PRODUCTNAME and MS Office documents in Mozilla/Netscape enabled				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01020400.xhp	0	help	par_idN105F9				0	bs	\<ahelp hid=\"736117762\"\>Enables the Mozilla plug-in to show %PRODUCTNAME documents in a browser window. Select, click OK, then restart your browser. Then in the browser window, click a link to a %PRODUCTNAME document.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01020400.xhp	0	help	par_idN10655				0	bs	The plug-in needs a version of Mozilla 1.x, Netscape 6.x, or Netscape 7.x installed on your system.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01012000.xhp	0	help	tit				0	bs	Appearance				2002-02-02 02:02:02
