helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01070300.xhp	0	help	par_id3145271				0	bs	\<variable id=\"opunkte\"\>\<ahelp hid=\"SVX_CHECKBOX_RID_SVXPAGE_GRID_CBX_SNAP_POINTS\"\>Specifies whether to align the contour of the graphic object to the points of the nearest graphic object.\</ahelp\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01070300.xhp	0	help	par_id3146146				0	bs	In a presentation or drawing document, this function can also be accessed with the \<switchinline select=\"appl\"\>\<caseinline select=\"IMPRESS\"\>\<link href=\"text/simpress/02/13170000.xhp\" name=\"Snap to Object Points\"\>Snap to Object Points\</link\>\</caseinline\>\<caseinline select=\"DRAW\"\>\<link href=\"text/simpress/02/13170000.xhp\" name=\"Snap to Object Points\"\>Snap to Object Points\</link\>\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>\<emph\>Snap to Object Points\</emph\>\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> icon in the option bar.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01070300.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148645				0	bs	Snap range				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01070300.xhp	0	help	par_id3154145				0	bs	\<ahelp hid=\"SVX_METRICFIELD_RID_SVXPAGE_GRID_MTR_FLD_SNAP_AREA\"\>Defines the snap distance between the mouse pointer and the object contour. $[officename] Impress snaps to a snap point if the mouse pointer is nearer than the distance selected in the \<emph\>Snap range \</emph\>spin box.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01070300.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150872				0	bs	Snap position				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01070300.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154639				0	bs	When creating or moving objects				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01070300.xhp	0	help	par_id3150417				0	bs	\<ahelp hid=\"SVX_CHECKBOX_RID_SVXPAGE_GRID_CBX_ORTHO\"\>Specifies that graphic objects are restricted vertically, horizontally or diagonally (45°) when creating or moving them.\</ahelp\> You can temporarily deactivate this setting by pressing the Shift key.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01070300.xhp	0	help	hd_id3159345				0	bs	Extend edges				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01070300.xhp	0	help	par_id3154942	24			0	bs	\<ahelp hid=\"SVX_CHECKBOX_RID_SVXPAGE_GRID_CBX_BIGORTHO\"\>Specifies that a square is created based on the longer side of a rectangle when the Shift key is pressed before you release the mouse button. This also applies to an ellipse (a circle will be created based on the longest diameter of the ellipse). When the\<emph\> Extend edges \</emph\>box is not marked, a square or a circle will be created based on the shorter side or diameter.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01070300.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149413				0	bs	When rotating				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01070300.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154163				0	bs	Point reduction				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01070300.xhp	0	help	par_id3156275				0	bs	\<ahelp hid=\"SVX_METRICFIELD_RID_SVXPAGE_GRID_MTR_FLD_BEZ_ANGLE\"\>Defines the angle for point reduction.\</ahelp\> When working with polygons, you might find it useful to reduce their editing points.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
