helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\06040200.xhp	0	help	par_id3149999	17			0	bs	\<switchinline select=\"appl\"\>\<caseinline select=\"WRITER\"\>To enable the replacement table, choose \<emph\>Tools - AutoCorrect/AutoFormat\</emph\>, click the\<emph\> Options\</emph\> tab, and then select\<emph\> Use replacement table\</emph\>. To use the replacement table while you type, choose \<emph\>Format - AutoFormat - While Typing\</emph\>. \</caseinline\>\</switchinline\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\06040200.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155321				0	bs	Replacement table				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\06040200.xhp	0	help	par_id3152945	4			0	bs	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_OFACTL_AUTOCORR_REPLACE\"\>Lists the entries for automatically replacing words or abbreviations while you type. To add an entry, enter text in the \<emph\>Replace \</emph\>and \<emph\>With \</emph\>boxes, and then click \<emph\>New\</emph\>. To edit an entry, select it, change the text in the \<emph\>With\</emph\> box, and then click \<emph\>Replace\</emph\>. To delete an entry, select it, and then click \<emph\>Delete\</emph\>.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\06040200.xhp	0	help	par_id3153349	14			0	bs	You can use the AutoCorrect feature to apply a specific character format to a word or abbreviation. Select the formatted text in your document, open this dialog, clear the \<emph\>Text only\</emph\> box, and then enter the text that you want to replace in the\<emph\> Replace\</emph\> box.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\06040200.xhp	0	help	par_id3154173	16			0	bs	\<switchinline select=\"appl\"\>\<caseinline select=\"WRITER\"\>You can also include frames, graphics, and OLE objects in an AutoCorrect entry, so long as they are anchored \<emph\>as characters\</emph\> in the text. Select the frame, graphic or OLE object and at least one text character in front of and behind the object. Open this dialog, type a name for this AutoCorrect entry in the \<emph\>Replace \</emph\>box, and then click \<emph\>New\</emph\>. \</caseinline\>\</switchinline\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\06040200.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148943				0	bs	Replace				2002-02-02 02:02:02
