helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\password_main.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154183				0	bs	\<variable id=\"password_maintitle\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/01/password_main.xhp\" name=\"Enter Master Password\"\>Enter Master Password\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\password_main.xhp	0	help	par_id3154841				0	bs	\<ahelp hid=\"\" visibility=\"visible\"\>Assign a master password to protect the access to a saved password.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\password_main.xhp	0	help	par_id3146857				0	bs	You can save some passwords for the duration of a session, or permanently to a file protected by a master password. For example, passwords for accessing WebDAV or FTP servers are stored permanently if you enter a master password when prompted. Otherwise, they are only stored for the current session.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\password_main.xhp	0	help	par_id3147000				0	bs	You must enter the master password to access a file or service that is protected by a saved password. You only need to enter the master password once during a session.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\password_main.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147588				0	bs	Master password				2002-02-02 02:02:02
