helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\06040300.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150278				0	bs	\<link href=\"text/shared/01/06040300.xhp\" name=\"Exceptions\"\>Exceptions\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\06040300.xhp	0	help	par_id3152876				0	bs	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_OFAPAGE_AUTOCORR_EXCEPT\"\>Specify the abbreviations or letter combinations that you do not want $[officename] to correct automatically.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\06040300.xhp	0	help	par_id3154926				0	bs	The exceptions that you define depend on the current language setting. If you want, you can change the language setting by selecting a different language in the \<emph\>Replacements and exceptions for language\</emph\> box.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\06040300.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149205				0	bs	Replacements and exceptions for language:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\06040300.xhp	0	help	par_id3156027				0	bs	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_AUTOCORR_LANGUAGE\"\>Select the language for which you want to create or edit the replacement rules.\</ahelp\> $[officename] first searches for exceptions that are defined for the language at the current cursor position in the document, and then searches the remaining languages.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\06040300.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153681				0	bs	Abbreviations (no subsequent capital)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\06040300.xhp	0	help	par_id3156410				0	bs	\<ahelp hid=\"OFFMGR:EDIT:RID_OFAPAGE_AUTOCORR_EXCEPT:ED_ABBREV\"\>Type an abbreviation followed by a period, and then click \<emph\>New\</emph\>. This prevents $[officename] from automatically capitalizing the first letter of the word that comes after the period at the end of the abbreviation.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\06040300.xhp	0	help	par_id3149751				0	bs	\<ahelp hid=\"OFFMGR:LISTBOX:RID_OFAPAGE_AUTOCORR_EXCEPT:LB_ABBREV\"\>Lists the abbreviations that are not automatically corrected.\</ahelp\> To remove an item from the list, select the item, and then click \<emph\>Delete\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\06040300.xhp	0	help	hd_id3151110				0	bs	Words with TWo INitial CApitals				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\06040300.xhp	0	help	par_id3154749				0	bs	\<ahelp hid=\"OFFMGR:EDIT:RID_OFAPAGE_AUTOCORR_EXCEPT:ED_DOUBLE_CAPS\"\>Type the word or abbreviation that starts with two capital letters that you do not want $[officename] to change to one initial capital. For example, enter PC to prevent $[officename] from changing PC to Pc.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\06040300.xhp	0	help	par_id3143271				0	bs	\<ahelp hid=\"OFFMGR:LISTBOX:RID_OFAPAGE_AUTOCORR_EXCEPT:LB_DOUBLE_CAPS\"\>Lists the words or abbreviations that start with two initial capitals that are not automatically corrected. All words which start with two capital letters are listed in the field.\</ahelp\> To remove an item from the list, select the item, and then click \<emph\>Delete\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\06040300.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155503				0	bs	New				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\06040300.xhp	0	help	par_id3147573				0	bs	\<ahelp hid=\"OFFMGR:PUSHBUTTON:RID_OFAPAGE_AUTOCORR_EXCEPT:PB_NEWDOUBLECAPS\"\>Adds the current entry to the list of exceptions.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\06040300.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149762				0	bs	AutoInclude				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\06040300.xhp	0	help	par_id3155829	11			0	bs	\<ahelp hid=\"OFFMGR:CHECKBOX:RID_OFAPAGE_AUTOCORR_EXCEPT:CB_AUTOCAPS\"\>Automatically adds abbreviations or words that start with two capital letters to the corresponding list of exceptions. This feature only works if the \<emph\>Correct TWo INitial CApitals\</emph\> option or the Capitalize\<emph\> first letter of every sentence\</emph\> option are selected in the \<emph\>[T]\</emph\> column on\<link href=\"text/shared/01/06040100.xhp\" name=\"Options\"\>\<emph\>Options\</emph\>\</link\> tab of this dialog. \</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\06010000.xhp	0	help	tit				0	bs	Spellcheck				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\06010000.xhp	0	help	bm_id3149047				0	bs	\<bookmark_value\>dictionaries; spellcheck\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>spellcheck; dictionaries\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>spellcheck; languages\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>languages; spellcheck\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\06010000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153882				0	bs	\<link href=\"text/shared/01/06010000.xhp\" name=\"Spellcheck\"\>Spellcheck\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\06010000.xhp	0	help	par_id3154682				0	bs	\<variable id=\"recht\"\>\<ahelp hid=\".uno:Spelling\"\>Checks the document or the current selection for spelling errors.\</ahelp\> $[officename] includes headers, footers, index entries, and footnotes in the spellcheck. \</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\06010000.xhp	0	help	par_idN1064B				0	bs	The spellcheck starts at the current cursor position and advances to the end of the document or selection. You can then choose to continue the spellcheck from the beginning of the document.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\06010000.xhp	0	help	par_id3166445				0	bs	Spellcheck looks for misspelled words and gives you the option of adding an unknown word to a user dictionary. When the first misspelled word is found, the \<emph\>Spellcheck\</emph\> dialog opens.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\06010000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149511				0	bs	Not in dictionary				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\06010000.xhp	0	help	par_id3149798				0	bs	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>Displays the sentence with the misspelled word highlighted. Edit the word or the sentence, or click one of the suggestions in the text box below.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\06010000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149885				0	bs	Suggestions				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\06010000.xhp	0	help	par_id3155628				0	bs	\<ahelp hid=\"SVX_LISTBOX_RID_SVXDLG_SPELLCHECK_LB_NEWWORD\"\>Lists suggested words to replace the misspelled word. Select the word that you want to use, and then click \<emph\>Change\</emph\> or \<emph\>Change All\</emph\>.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\06010000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145087				0	bs	Dictionary Language				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\06010000.xhp	0	help	par_id3144422				0	bs	\<ahelp hid=\"SVX_LISTBOX_RID_SVXDLG_SPELLCHECK_LB_LANGUAGE\"\>Specifies the language to use to check the spelling.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\06010000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154071				0	bs	\<switchinline select=\"appl\"\>\<caseinline select=\"WRITER\"\>AutoCorrect \</caseinline\>\</switchinline\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\06010000.xhp	0	help	par_id3153798				0	bs	\<switchinline select=\"appl\"\>\<caseinline select=\"WRITER\"\>\<ahelp hid=\"SVX_PUSHBUTTON_RID_SVXDLG_SPELLCHECK_BTN_AUTOCORR\"\>Adds the current combination of the incorrect word and the replacement word to the AutoCorrect replacements table.\</ahelp\>\</caseinline\>\</switchinline\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\06010000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3151382				0	bs	Options				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\06010000.xhp	0	help	par_id3154123				0	bs	\<ahelp hid=\"SVX_PUSHBUTTON_RID_SVXDLG_SPELLCHECK_BTN_OPTIONS\"\>Opens a dialog, where you can select the user-defined dictionaries, and set the rules for the spellchecking.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\06010000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153353				0	bs	Add				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\06010000.xhp	0	help	par_id3144432				0	bs	\<ahelp hid=\"SVX_PUSHBUTTON_RID_SVXDLG_SPELLCHECK_BTN_ADD\"\>Adds the unknown word to a user-defined dictionary.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\06010000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155994				0	bs	Ignore Once				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\06010000.xhp	0	help	par_id3148920				0	bs	\<ahelp hid=\"SVX:PUSHBUTTON:RID_SVXDLG_SPELLCHECK:BTN_IGNORE\"\>Skips the unknown word and continues with the spellcheck.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\06010000.xhp	0	help	par_idN107CB				0	bs	This label of this button changes to \<emph\>Resume\</emph\> if you leave the Spellcheck dialog open when you return to your document. To continue the spellcheck from the current position of the cursor, click \<emph\>Resume\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\06010000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150740				0	bs	Ignore All				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\06010000.xhp	0	help	par_id3145318				0	bs	\<ahelp hid=\"SVX:PUSHBUTTON:RID_SVXDLG_SPELLCHECK:BTN_IGNOREALL\"\>Skips all occurrences of the unknown word in the entire document and continues with the spellcheck.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\06010000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153056				0	bs	Change				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\06010000.xhp	0	help	par_id3148559				0	bs	\<ahelp hid=\"SVX:PUSHBUTTON:RID_SVXDLG_SPELLCHECK:BTN_CHANGE\"\>Replaces the unknown word with the current suggestion. If you changed more than just the misspelled word, the entire sentence is replaced.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\06010000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145787				0	bs	Change All				2002-02-02 02:02:02
