helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05030500.xhp	0	help	par_id3151097				0	bs	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_BORDER\"\>Sets the border options for the selected objects in Writer or Calc.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05030500.xhp	0	help	par_id3155351	44			0	bs	You can specify the border position, size, and style in Writer or Calc. \<switchinline select=\"appl\"\>\<caseinline select=\"WRITER\"\>In $[officename] Writer, you can add borders to pages, frames, graphics, tables, paragraphs, and to embedded objects. \</caseinline\>\</switchinline\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05030500.xhp	0	help	par_id3152997				0	bs	To modify the border of an entire table, place the cursor in a table cell, right-click, choose \<emph\>Table\</emph\>, and then click the \<emph\>Borders\</emph\> tab. To modify the border of a table cell, select the cell, right-click, choose \<emph\>Table\</emph\>, and then click the \<emph\>Borders\</emph\> tab.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05030500.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145417				0	bs	Line arrangement				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05030500.xhp	0	help	par_id3153332				0	bs	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_BORDER_CTL_PRESETS\"\>Select a predefined border style to apply.\</ahelp\> A preview of the border style is shown in the \<emph\>User-defined \</emph\>area of this dialog.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05030500.xhp	0	help	par_id3148643				0	bs	If you are in a table or spreadsheet, you can also add or remove predefined borders. Use the \<emph\>Borders\</emph\> icon on the \<emph\>Table Bar\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05030500.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149575				0	bs	Line				2002-02-02 02:02:02
