helpcontent2	source\text\shared\autopi\webwizard07.xhp	0	help	par_idN1055B				0	bs	\<ahelp hid=\"34260\"\>Opens your web page in the default web browser of your operating system.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\autopi\webwizard07.xhp	0	help	par_idN1055E				0	bs	Local directory				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\autopi\webwizard07.xhp	0	help	par_idN10562				0	bs	\<ahelp hid=\"34261\"\>Uploads your index page and files to a local directory. The index page is saved to the location that you specified. All other files are saved to the "myWebsite" directory in the directory that contains the index page.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\autopi\webwizard07.xhp	0	help	par_idN10569				0	bs	\<ahelp hid=\"34263\"\>Opens a dialog to select a folder.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\autopi\webwizard07.xhp	0	help	par_idN1056C				0	bs	Archive file				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\autopi\webwizard07.xhp	0	help	par_idN10570				0	bs	\<ahelp hid=\"34265\"\>Adds your index page and files to a compressed archive file and uploads the file to your web site. The index page is saved to the location that you specified. All other files are saved to the "myWebsite" directory in the directory that contains the index page.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\autopi\webwizard07.xhp	0	help	par_idN10573				0	bs	Depending on your operating system, the available archive file formats are zip, gzip, and war.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\autopi\webwizard07.xhp	0	help	par_idN1057A				0	bs	\<ahelp hid=\"34266\"\>Opens a dialog where you can specify the location of the archive file.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
