helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12070200.xhp	0	help	tit				0	bs	Fields				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12070200.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149991				0	bs	Fields				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12070200.xhp	0	help	bm_id3149987				0	bs	\<bookmark_value\>database contents; inserting as fields\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12070200.xhp	0	help	par_id3149987	8			0	bs	\<ahelp hid=\"SW_RADIOBUTTON_DLG_AP_INSERT_DB_SEL_RB_AS_FIELD\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Inserts data selected from the data source browser into the document as fields.\</ahelp\>In the \<emph\>Insert Database Columns\</emph\> dialog, select the \<link href=\"text/swriter/01/04090000.xhp\" name=\"Fields\"\>Fields\</link\> to insert the selected data into the document as fields. These \<link href=\"text/swriter/01/04090006.xhp\" name=\"database fields\"\>database fields\</link\> work as wildcards for the individual database columns and can be used for form letters. Click the \<link href=\"text/shared/02/12080000.xhp\" name=\"Data to Fields\"\>\<emph\>Data to Fields\</emph\>\</link\> icon to match the contents of the fields to the currently selected record.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12070200.xhp	0	help	par_id3153114				0	bs	If several records are selected when you choose the \<emph\>Data to Text\</emph\> function, the mail merge fields will be inserted according to the number of records. Also, a field command such as "Next record" will be inserted automatically between individual field command blocks.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12070200.xhp	0	help	par_id3145090				0	bs	The \<emph\>Insert Database Columns\</emph\> dialog lets you define which database fields to insert into the document and how to format the paragraphs.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12070200.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156136				0	bs	Fields				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12070200.xhp	0	help	par_id3147571				0	bs	In the \<emph\>Fields\</emph\> area, use the arrow button to select the database table columns into which you want to insert field contents.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12070200.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153345				0	bs	Database columns				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12070200.xhp	0	help	par_id3155535				0	bs	Lists all columns of the database table, which can be accepted in the selection list box to insert them into the document. \<ahelp hid=\"SW_LISTBOX_DLG_AP_INSERT_DB_SEL_LB_TXT_DB_COLUMN\" visibility=\"visible\"\>Select the database columns that you want to insert it in the document.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12070200.xhp	0	help	par_id3145345				0	bs	\<ahelp visibility=\"visible\" hid=\"SW_IMAGEBUTTON_DLG_AP_INSERT_DB_SEL_IB_DBCOL_TOEDIT\"\>Moves the fields that you selected in the \<emph\>Database columns\</emph\> list box into the selection field.\</ahelp\> You can also double-click the entry to select it.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12070200.xhp	0	help	hd_id3166411				0	bs	Select				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12070200.xhp	0	help	par_id3163802				0	bs	\<ahelp hid=\"SW_MULTILINEEDIT_DLG_AP_INSERT_DB_SEL_ED_DB_TEXT\" visibility=\"visible\"\>Lists the database columns that you selected to be inserted into the document. You can also enter text here. This text will be also inserted into the document.\</ahelp\> The entries' order in the selection field corresponds to the data order in the document.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12070200.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153257				0	bs	Paragraph Style				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12070200.xhp	0	help	par_id3158430				0	bs	By default, the inserted paragraphs are formatted with the current Paragraph Styles. This format corresponds to the "none" entry in the \<emph\>Paragraph Style\</emph\> list box. \<ahelp hid=\"SW_LISTBOX_DLG_AP_INSERT_DB_SEL_LB_DB_PARA_COLL\" visibility=\"visible\"\>This is where you can select other Paragraph Styles to apply to the paragraph you want to insert into the document.\</ahelp\> The list box displays the available Paragraph Styles defined in \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> and managed in the \<link href=\"text/swriter/01/05130000.xhp\" name=\"Style Catalog\"\>Style Catalog\</link\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170004.xhp	0	help	tit				0	bs	Special Tips for Table Controls				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170004.xhp	0	help	bm_id3109850				0	bs	\<bookmark_value\>table controls; properties\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>controls; table control properties\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>table controls;keyboard-only edit mode\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170004.xhp	0	help	hd_id3109850				0	bs	Special Tips for Table Controls				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170004.xhp	0	help	par_id3153539				0	bs	You can define a table control to display the records as you like. In other words you can define data fields for displaying or editing data like in a database form.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170004.xhp	0	help	par_id3152372				0	bs	The following fields are possible in a table control: text, date, time and currency field, numeric field, pattern field, check box and combo box. In the case of combined data/time fields, two columns are created automatically.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170004.xhp	0	help	par_id3159194				0	bs	The number of selected lines, if any are selected, is in parentheses after the total number of records.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170004.xhp	0	help	par_id3155616				0	bs	To insert columns into the table control, click in the column heads and bring up the context menu. The following commands are available:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170004.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150789				0	bs	Insert Column				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170004.xhp	0	help	par_id3153750				0	bs	\<ahelp hid=\"SID_FM_INSERTCOL\"\>Calls a submenu to select a data field to adopt it in the table control.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170004.xhp	0	help	par_id3155552				0	bs	Configure the table control using drag and drop: Open the data source browser and drag the desired fields out of the data source browser and on to the column heads of the table control. A pre-configured column is created.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170004.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149827				0	bs	Replace with				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170004.xhp	0	help	par_id3153345				0	bs	\<ahelp hid=\"SID_FM_CHANGECOL\"\>Opens a submenu to select a data field to replace the data field selected in the table control.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170004.xhp	0	help	hd_id3143267				0	bs	Delete Column				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170004.xhp	0	help	par_id3157958				0	bs	\<ahelp hid=\"SID_FM_DELETECOL\"\>Deletes the currently selected column.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170004.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147275				0	bs	Column				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170004.xhp	0	help	par_id3152996				0	bs	Opens the properties dialog of the selected column.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170004.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148539				0	bs	Hide Columns				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170004.xhp	0	help	par_id3159157				0	bs	\<ahelp hid=\"SID_FM_HIDECOL\"\>Hides the selected column.\</ahelp\> Its properties are not changed.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170004.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150771				0	bs	Show columns				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170004.xhp	0	help	par_id3159400				0	bs	\<ahelp hid=\"SID_FM_SHOWCOLS\"\>Calls a submenu where you can select the columns to show again.\</ahelp\> To show only one column, click the column name. You see only the first 16 hidden columns. If there are more hidden columns, choose the \<emph\>More\</emph\> command to call the \<emph\>Show Columns\</emph\> dialog.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170004.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156193				0	bs	More				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170004.xhp	0	help	par_id3159269				0	bs	\<ahelp hid=\"SID_FM_SHOWCOLS_MORE\"\>Calls the \<emph\>Show Columns\</emph\> dialog.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170004.xhp	0	help	par_id3149763				0	bs	\<ahelp hid=\"SVX:LISTBOX:RID_SVX_DLG_SHOWGRIDCOLUMNS:1\"\>In the \<emph\>Show Columns\</emph\> dialog you can select the columns to be shown. Hold down the Shift or Ctrl key to select multiple entries.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170004.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153561				0	bs	All				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170004.xhp	0	help	par_id3150504	87			0	bs	\<ahelp hid=\"SID_FM_SHOWALLCOLS\"\>Click \<emph\>All \</emph\>if you want to show all columns.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170004.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153349				0	bs	Keyboard-only control of Table Controls				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170004.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153062				0	bs	To enter the special keyboard-only edit mode for Table Controls:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170004.xhp	0	help	par_id3144510				0	bs	The form document must be in \<link href=\"text/shared/02/01170500.xhp\" name=\"design mode\"\>design mode\</link\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170004.xhp	0	help	par_id3161657				0	bs	Press Shift+F5 to select the first control. If the Table Control is not the first control, press Tab until it is selected.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170004.xhp	0	help	par_id3151056				0	bs	Press Enter to enter the edit mode. The handles are shown farther out from the control border.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170004.xhp	0	help	par_id3154938				0	bs	In the edit mode, you can open the edit mode context menu by pressing Shift+F10.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170004.xhp	0	help	par_id3145419				0	bs	Press the Escape key to exit the edit mode.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170003.xhp	0	help	tit				0	bs	Special Tips for Date Fields				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170003.xhp	0	help	bm_id3150445				0	bs	\<bookmark_value\>date fields; properties\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170003.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150445				0	bs	Special Tips for Date Fields				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170003.xhp	0	help	par_id3149205				0	bs	The pre-set limit value will be saved for each document. If you want to open a document in an older version of StarOffice, in which the limit of 1930 could not be changed, then you must also select the limit value 1930 in your current version of $[officename].				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\02040000.xhp	0	help	tit				0	bs	Text running from left to right				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\02040000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153255				0	bs	\<link href=\"text/shared/02/02040000.xhp\" name=\"Text running from left to right\"\>Text running from left to right\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\02040000.xhp	0	help	par_id3153539				0	bs	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:TextdirectionLeftToRigh\" visibility=\"visible\"\>Specifies the horizontal direction of the text.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
