helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\07070100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149388				0	bs	Editing Databases in Networks				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\07070100.xhp	0	help	par_id3147576				0	bs	To make changes in a database used by more than one person, you must have the appropriate access rights. When you edit an external database, there is no intermediate storage by $[officename] of the changes made. They are sent directly to the database.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
