helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\doc_open.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147653				0	bs	Opening an existing document				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\doc_open.xhp	0	help	par_id3149398				0	bs	Do one of the following:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\doc_open.xhp	0	help	par_idN107A9				0	bs	Choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>File - Open\</item\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\doc_open.xhp	0	help	par_idN107AF				0	bs	Click the Open File icon				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\doc_open.xhp	0	help	par_id3150275				0	bs	The \<link href=\"text/shared/01/01020000.xhp\" name=\"Open\"\>Open\</link\> dialog appears.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\doc_open.xhp	0	help	par_id3149164				0	bs	Select the file you want to open and click \<emph\>Open\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\doc_open.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149234				0	bs	Restrict Files to Display				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\doc_open.xhp	0	help	par_id3150985				0	bs	To restrict the display of files in the \<emph\>Open\</emph\> dialog to a certain type select the corresponding \<emph\>File type\</emph\> from the list. Select \<emph\>All Files (*.*)\</emph\> to display all files.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\doc_open.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148453				0	bs	Opening an Empty Document				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\doc_open.xhp	0	help	par_id3153092				0	bs	If you click the arrow next to the \<emph\>New\</emph\> icon, a submenu opens in which you can select another document type.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\doc_open.xhp	0	help	par_id3153126	9			0	bs	You can also enter a URL in the \<emph\>File name\</emph\> box of the \<emph\>Open\</emph\> dialog. This must start with the fully extended form with file:/// or ftp:// or http://.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\doc_open.xhp	0	help	par_idN107C4				0	bs	When you open a file by an URL from the Windows file dialog, Windows will open a local copy of the file, located in the Internet Explorer cache. The %PRODUCTNAME file dialog opens the remote file.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\doc_open.xhp	0	help	par_id3148616				0	bs	\<link href=\"text/shared/01/01020000.xhp\" name=\"File - Open\"\>File - Open\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining.xhp	0	help	tit				0	bs	Recording and Displaying Changes				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining.xhp	0	help	bm_id3150499				0	bs	\<bookmark_value\>marking changes\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>changes; review function\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>review function; recording changes\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150499				0	bs	\<variable id=\"redlining\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/redlining.xhp\" name=\"Recording and Displaying Changes\"\>Recording and Displaying Changes\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining.xhp	0	help	par_id3153681				0	bs	When several authors are working on the same text or spreadsheet, the review function records and displays who made the various changes. On the final edit of the document, it is then possible to look at each individual change and decide whether it should be accepted or rejected.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining.xhp	0	help	par_id3147008				0	bs	For example: You are an editor and are delivering your latest report. But before publication the report must be read by the senior editor and the proofreader, and both will add their changes. The senior editor writes "clarify" after one paragraph and crosses out another entirely. The proofreader corrects the spelling of your document.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining.xhp	0	help	par_id3150774				0	bs	The edited document comes back to you, and you can incorporate or ignore the suggestions of the two reviewers.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining.xhp	0	help	par_id3146957				0	bs	Let's say you also e-mailed a copy of the report to a good friend and colleague who has done research on a similar topic in the past. You asked for a few suggestions, and the document is now returned by e-mail with your colleague's suggestions.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining.xhp	0	help	par_id3147088				0	bs	As all your colleagues and the managers in your company work with $[officename], you can produce a final version of the document from the results you get back.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\email.xhp	0	help	tit				0	bs	Sending Documents as E-mail				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\email.xhp	0	help	bm_id3153345				0	bs	\<bookmark_value\>documents; sending as e-mail\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>sending; documents as e-mail\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>e-mail attachments\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>files; sending as e-mail\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>text;sending as e-mail\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>tables; sending as e-mail\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>drawings; sending as e-mail\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>presentations; sending as e-mail\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>attachments in e-mails\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\email.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153345				0	bs	\<variable id=\"email\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/email.xhp\" name=\"Sending Documents as E-mail\"\>Sending Documents as E-mail\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\email.xhp	0	help	par_id3154897				0	bs	Working in $[officename], you can send the current document as an e-mail attachment.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\email.xhp	0	help	par_id3147335				0	bs	Choose \<emph\>File - Send - Document as E-mail\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\email.xhp	0	help	par_id3153127				0	bs	$[officename] opens your default e-mail program.\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"UNIX\"\> If you want to send the current document with another e-mail program, you can select the program to use with \<emph\>Tools - Options - Internet - E-mail\</emph\>.\</caseinline\>\</switchinline\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\email.xhp	0	help	par_id3150986				0	bs	In your e-mail program, enter the recipient, subject and any text you want to add, then send the e-mail.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
