helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\scripting.xhp	0	help	par_idN10728				0	bs	You can assign custom scripts (macros) to menu items, icons, dialog controls, and events in %PRODUCTNAME.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\scripting.xhp	0	help	par_idN1072B				0	bs	%PRODUCTNAME internally supports the following scripting languages:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\scripting.xhp	0	help	par_idN10731				0	bs	%PRODUCTNAME Basic				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\scripting.xhp	0	help	par_idN10739				0	bs	JavaScript				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\scripting.xhp	0	help	par_idN1073D				0	bs	BeanShell				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\scripting.xhp	0	help	par_idN1091F				0	bs	In addition, developers can use high-level languages, for example Java programming language, to control %PRODUCTNAME externally. See the API project at OpenOffice.org.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\scripting.xhp	0	help	par_idN10751				0	bs	To assign a script to a new menu entry				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\scripting.xhp	0	help	par_idN10758				0	bs	Choose \<emph\>Tools - Customize\</emph\>, and click the \<emph\>Menus\</emph\> tab.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\scripting.xhp	0	help	par_idN1093D				0	bs	Click \<emph\>Add\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\scripting.xhp	0	help	par_idN10760				0	bs	In the \<emph\>Category\</emph\> list box, scroll down and open the "%PRODUCTNAME Macros" entry.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\scripting.xhp	0	help	par_idN10768				0	bs	You see entries for "%PRODUCTNAME Macros" (scripts in the share directory of your %PRODUCTNAME installation), "My Macros" (scripts in the user directory), and the current document. Open any one of them to see the supported scripting languages.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\scripting.xhp	0	help	par_idN1076C				0	bs	Open any scripting language entry to see the available scripts. Select a script.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\scripting.xhp	0	help	par_idN10770				0	bs	A list of the script functions appears in the \<emph\>Functions\</emph\> list box. Select a function.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\scripting.xhp	0	help	par_idN10778				0	bs	Click \<emph\>New\</emph\> to create a new menu assignment. The new menu entry appears in the \<emph\>Menu entries\</emph\> list box. Click the menu entry and enter text to rename the entry.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\scripting.xhp	0	help	par_idN10783				0	bs	To assign a script to a key combination				2002-02-02 02:02:02
