helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	par_id3153394				0	bs	The following is an overview of the different ways of protecting contents in \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> from being modified, deleted or viewed.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	hd_id3146957				0	bs	Protecting All Documents When Saving				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	par_id3150775				0	bs	All documents that are saved in \<link href=\"text/shared/00/00000021.xhp\" name=\"XML format\"\>XML format\</link\> can be saved with a password. Documents that are saved with a password cannot be opened without the password. The content is secured so that it cannot be read with an external editor. This applies to content, graphics and OLE objects.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	par_id3166410				0	bs	Turning on protection				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	par_id3145121				0	bs	Choose \<emph\>File - Save As\</emph\> and mark the \<emph\>Save with password\</emph\> check box. Save the document.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	par_id3154286				0	bs	Turning off protection				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	par_id3148492				0	bs	Open the document, entering the correct password. Choose \<emph\>File - Save As\</emph\> and clear the \<emph\>Save with password\</emph\> check box.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	par_id3145068				0	bs	Information entered in \<emph\>File - Properties\</emph\> is not encrypted. This includes the name of the author, creation date, word and character counts.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149294				0	bs	Protecting Revision Marking				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	par_id3161646				0	bs	With every change made in \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> Calc and \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> Writer, the review function records who made the change. This function can be turned on with protection, so that it can only be turned off when the correct password is entered. Until then, all changes will continue to be recorded. Acceptance or rejection of changes is not possible.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	par_id3154684				0	bs	Turning on protection				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	par_id3153104				0	bs	Choose \<emph\>Edit - Changes - Protect Records\</emph\>. Enter and confirm a password of at least 5 characters.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	par_id3144760				0	bs	Turning off protection				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	par_id3152920				0	bs	Choose \<emph\>Edit - Changes - Protect Records\</emph\>. Enter the correct password.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155113				0	bs	Protecting Frames, Graphics, and OLE Objects				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	par_id3153703				0	bs	You can protect the content, position and size of inserted graphics. The same applies to frames (in Writer) and OLE objects.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	par_id3147131				0	bs	Turning on protection				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	par_id3150088				0	bs	For example, for graphics inserted in Writer: Choose \<emph\>Format - Graphics - Options\</emph\> tab. Under \<emph\>Protect\</emph\>, mark \<emph\>Contents\</emph\>, \<emph\>Position\</emph\> and/or \<emph\>Size\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	par_id3147510				0	bs	Turning off protection				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	par_id3153657				0	bs	For example, for graphics inserted in Writer: Choose \<emph\>Format - Graphics - Options\</emph\> tab. Under \<emph\>Protect\</emph\>, unmark as appropriate.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	hd_id3152992				0	bs	Protecting Drawing Objects and Form Objects				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	par_id3166429	59			0	bs	The draw objects that you insert into your documents with the \<emph\>Drawing \</emph\>toolbar can be protected from being accidentally moved or changed in size. You can do the same with form objects inserted with the \<emph\>Form Controls\</emph\> toolbar.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	par_id3153226				0	bs	Turning on protection				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	par_id3148815	61			0	bs	Choose \<emph\>Format - Object - Position and Size \</emph\>- \<emph\>Position and Size\</emph\> tab. Mark the \<emph\>Position\</emph\> or \<emph\>Size\</emph\> check box.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	par_id3156289				0	bs	Turning off protection				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	par_id3154991	63			0	bs	Choose \<emph\>Format - Object - Position and Size \</emph\>- \<emph\>Position and Size\</emph\> tab. Unmark the \<emph\>Position\</emph\> or \<emph\>Size\</emph\> check box.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_table.xhp	0	help	tit				0	bs	Copying Spreadsheet Areas to Text Documents				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_table.xhp	0	help	bm_id3154927				0	bs	\<bookmark_value\>spreadsheets; copying areas to text documents\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>copying; sheet areas, to text documents\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_table.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154927				0	bs	\<variable id=\"dragdrop_table\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/dragdrop_table.xhp\" name=\"Copying Spreadsheet Areas to Text Documents\"\>Copying Spreadsheet Areas to Text Documents\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_table.xhp	0	help	par_id3155892				0	bs	Open both the text document and the spreadsheet.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_table.xhp	0	help	par_id3147088				0	bs	Select the sheet area you want to copy.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_table.xhp	0	help	par_id3149827				0	bs	Point to the selected area and press the mouse button. Keep the mouse button pressed for a moment, then drag the area into the text document.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_table.xhp	0	help	par_id3152780	32			0	bs	\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"WIN\"\>If the documents are not visible next to each other, first drag the mouse pointer to the destination document button. Continue to hold down the mouse button. The document is displayed, and you can move the mouse pointer within the document.\</caseinline\>\</switchinline\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_table.xhp	0	help	par_id3156346				0	bs	Once the cursor is located in the place where you want to insert the sheet area, release the mouse button. The sheet area is inserted as an OLE object.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_table.xhp	0	help	par_id3154047				0	bs	You can select and edit the OLE object at any time.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_table.xhp	0	help	par_id3149164				0	bs	To edit the OLE object, double-click on it.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_table.xhp	0	help	par_id3155389				0	bs	Alternatively, select the object and choose \<emph\>Edit - Object - Edit\</emph\> or choose \<emph\>Edit\</emph\> from the context menu. You edit the object in its own frame within the text document, but you see the icons and menu commands needed for spreadsheets.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_table.xhp	0	help	par_id3154860				0	bs	Choose \<emph\>Open\</emph\> to open the source document of the OLE object.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\workfolder.xhp	0	help	tit				0	bs	Changing Your Work Directory				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\workfolder.xhp	0	help	bm_id3150789				0	bs	\<bookmark_value\>work directory change\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>My Documents folder; work directory\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>paths; changing work directory\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>pictures; changing paths\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>changing;work directory\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\workfolder.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149346				0	bs	\<variable id=\"workfolder\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/workfolder.xhp\" name=\"Changing Your Work Directory\"\>Changing Your Work Directory\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\workfolder.xhp	0	help	par_id3150774				0	bs	When you start a dialog to open or save a document, $[officename] initially displays your work directory. To change this directory:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\workfolder.xhp	0	help	par_id3163802	5			0	bs	Click \<emph\>My Documents \</emph\>and click the\<emph\> Edit button, or \</emph\>double-click on \<emph\>My Documents\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\workfolder.xhp	0	help	par_id3153880				0	bs	In the \<emph\>Select Path\</emph\> dialog, choose the work directory you want and click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\workfolder.xhp	0	help	par_id3154286				0	bs	\<link href=\"text/shared/optionen/01010300.xhp\" name=\"Paths\"\>Paths\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\print_faster.xhp	0	help	tit				0	bs	Printing with Reduced Data				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\print_faster.xhp	0	help	bm_id5201574				0	bs	\<bookmark_value\>gradients;off for faster printing\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>bitmaps;off for faster printing\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>resolution when printing bitmaps \</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>transparency;off for faster printing\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>reduced printing;faster printing\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>speed of printing;faster printing\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>printing speed\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>printing;transparencies\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>printing;faster\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>faster printing\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\print_faster.xhp	0	help	par_idN106AA				0	bs	\<variable id=\"print_faster\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/print_faster.xhp\"\>Printing faster with Reduced Data\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\print_faster.xhp	0	help	par_idN106C8				0	bs	You can decide to reduce the data necessary to print your document. The settings can be defined differently for printing directly to the printer or for printing to a file.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\print_faster.xhp	0	help	par_idN106D6				0	bs	Click one of the following settings options: 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\print_faster.xhp	0	help	par_idN106D9				0	bs	\<emph\>Printer\</emph\>\<emph\>- \</emph\>to define options for reducing data while printing directly to a printer				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\print_faster.xhp	0	help	par_idN106E2				0	bs	\<emph\>Print to file\</emph\>\<emph\>-\</emph\> to define options for reducing data while printing to a file				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\print_faster.xhp	0	help	par_idN106EC				0	bs	Select any combination of the four options, then click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\print_faster.xhp	0	help	par_idN106EF				0	bs	All documents that you print from now on will use the changed options.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\print_faster.xhp	0	help	par_idN106F3				0	bs	Print your document.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\print_faster.xhp	0	help	par_idN106F6				0	bs	You can reduce data for transparency, for gradients, or for bitmaps. When you reduce the data, on many printers you will not see a reduction of printing quality. But the printing time is substantially shorter, and when you print to a file, the file size is much smaller.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\print_faster.xhp	0	help	par_idN10704				0	bs	\<link href=\"text/shared/optionen/01010900.xhp\"\>Print options\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_queries.xhp	0	help	tit				0	bs	Working with Queries				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_queries.xhp	0	help	bm_id840784				0	bs	\<bookmark_value\>databases;creating queries\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>filtering;data in databases\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>queries;defining\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>defining;queries\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_queries.xhp	0	help	par_idN105F9				0	bs	\<variable id=\"data_queries\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/data_queries.xhp\"\>Working with Queries\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_queries.xhp	0	help	par_idN10617				0	bs	If you often want to access only a subset of your data that can be well defined by a filter condition, you can define a query. This is basically a name for the new view at the filtered data. You open the query and see the current data in the table layout that you defined.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_queries.xhp	0	help	par_idN1061A				0	bs	Creating a New Query With the Query Wizard				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_queries.xhp	0	help	par_idN1061E				0	bs	In %PRODUCTNAME you can create a new query using the \<link href=\"text/shared/explorer/database/querywizard00.xhp\"\>Query Wizard\</link\>:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_queries.xhp	0	help	par_idN10632				0	bs	Open the database file where you want to create the new query.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_queries.xhp	0	help	par_idN10636				0	bs	In the left pane of the database window, click the \<emph\>Queries\</emph\> icon.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_queries.xhp	0	help	par_idN1063E				0	bs	Click \<emph\>Use Wizard to Create Query\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_queries.xhp	0	help	par_idN10645				0	bs	Creating a New Query With the Design View				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_queries.xhp	0	help	par_idN1064C				0	bs	Open the database file where you want to create the new query.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_queries.xhp	0	help	par_idN10650				0	bs	In the left pane of the database window, click the \<emph\>Queries\</emph\> icon.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_queries.xhp	0	help	par_idN10658				0	bs	Click \<emph\>Create Query in Design View\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_queries.xhp	0	help	par_idN1065F				0	bs	You see the \<link href=\"text/shared/explorer/database/02010100.xhp\"\>Query Design window\</link\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
