helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\measurement_units.xhp	0	help	par_id3146957				0	bs	You can select separate measurement units for $[officename] Writer, $[officename] Writer/Web, $[officename] Calc, $[officename] Impress and $[officename] Draw documents.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\measurement_units.xhp	0	help	par_idN10674				0	bs	Open a document of the type for which you want to change the measurement units.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\measurement_units.xhp	0	help	par_id3154749				0	bs	In the left pane of the dialog, double-click the application for which you want to select the measurement unit.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\measurement_units.xhp	0	help	par_id3147653				0	bs	Double-click \<emph\>%PRODUCTNAME Writer\</emph\> if you want to select the measurement units for text documents.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\measurement_units.xhp	0	help	par_id3150443				0	bs	Click on \<emph\>General\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\measurement_units.xhp	0	help	par_id3147335				0	bs	On the \<emph\>General\</emph\> tab page, select the measurement unit. Close the dialog with \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
