helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\chart_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id3155066	32			0	bs	In $[officename] Writer documents, you can insert a chart obtained from the data of a Writer table. If you have not selected any data in a Writer table, choosing \<emph\>Insert - Object - Chart\</emph\> inserts a chart containing sample data.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\chart_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id3152960				0	bs	You can change the sample data values by double-clicking on the chart and then choosing \<link href=\"text/schart/01/03010000.xhp\" name=\"Edit - Chart Data\"\>\<emph\>Edit - Chart Data\</emph\>\</link\>. If you want to change the values of a chart obtained from selected cells, you have to change the values in the table cells. If the chart is in a text document, press F9 to update the chart.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
