helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\standard_template.xhp	0	help	par_id3152811				0	bs	When you open a new document with \<emph\>File - New\</emph\>, a blank document appears based on a $[officename] template. You can edit, modify, or replace this template so that the new document contains your customized Styles or other contents.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\standard_template.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150792				0	bs	Modifying Default Templates				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\standard_template.xhp	0	help	par_id3154365				0	bs	First, open either an existing $[officename] template and modify it, or open a new document and edit it as necessary to create the desired template.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\standard_template.xhp	0	help	par_id3159152				0	bs	You can define a document template for each $[officename] module. The following describes how to proceed for text documents.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\standard_template.xhp	0	help	par_id3145748	8			0	bs	Save the document by choosing\<emph\> File\</emph\> -\<emph\> Templates - Save \</emph\>and saving the document in the \<emph\>My Templates\</emph\> category.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\standard_template.xhp	0	help	par_id3154011				0	bs	Choose \<emph\>File - Templates - Organize\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\standard_template.xhp	0	help	par_id3146901				0	bs	Choose \<emph\>Set As Default Template\</emph\>. The next time you open a new text document, the new document will be based on the new default template.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\standard_template.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153947				0	bs	Resetting Default Templates				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\standard_template.xhp	0	help	par_id3156276				0	bs	To reset the modified text template to the original default template:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\standard_template.xhp	0	help	par_id3146792				0	bs	Choose \<emph\>File - Templates - Organize\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\standard_template.xhp	0	help	par_id3153714				0	bs	Open the context menu and choose \<emph\>Reset default template\</emph\>. In the submenu, select the document type whose default setting you want to restore. Thereafter, when you open an empty text document, it will again correspond to the $[officename] default template for text documents.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\standard_template.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153764				0	bs	Using Custom Templates				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\standard_template.xhp	0	help	par_id3150386	14			0	bs	There are several ways to make your work easier by using your own custom templates. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\standard_template.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149109				0	bs	Templates in the Template Folder				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\standard_template.xhp	0	help	par_id3155960				0	bs	You may need to update the view of the templates in the dialog before you can see a newly created template. In this case, choose \<emph\>File - Templates - Organize\</emph\> and in the submenu of the \<emph\>Commands\</emph\> button, choose \<emph\>Update\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\standard_template.xhp	0	help	par_id3147343				0	bs	To open the template for editing, choose \<emph\>File - Templates - Edit\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\standard_template.xhp	0	help	par_id3147315				0	bs	\<link href=\"text/shared/01/01110000.xhp\" name=\"Templates\"\>Templates\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	tit				0	bs	Shortcuts (%PRODUCTNAME Accessibility)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	bm_id3158421				0	bs	\<bookmark_value\>accessibility; shortcuts\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>shortcut keys; %PRODUCTNAME accessibility\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	hd_id3158421				0	bs	\<variable id=\"keyboard\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/keyboard.xhp\" name=\"Shortcuts (%PRODUCTNAME Accessibility)\"\>Shortcuts (\<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> Accessibility)\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3159201				0	bs	You can control \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> without using a mouse device, using only the keyboard.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3149177				0	bs	On each module's main help page (for example, the \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> Writer or \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> Calc main help page) there is a link to access the keyboard shortcuts' help for that module.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3145382				0	bs	In addition, under the keyword "Accessibility" you find step-by-step instructions about how to control the selected module without a mouse device.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	hd_id3166460				0	bs	Working with the \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> user interface without mouse				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154749				0	bs	Activating menu bar, toolbars, windows, and document				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3156329				0	bs	Repeatedly pressing F6 switches the focus and circles through the following objects:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3150669				0	bs	menu bar,				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3149234				0	bs	every toolbar from top to bottom and from left to right,				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3147618				0	bs	every free window from left to right,				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3154514				0	bs	document				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3153252				0	bs	Press Shift+F6 or Shift+Ctrl+Tab to switch through objects in the opposite direction.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3152360				0	bs	Press F10 to switch to the menu bar and back.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3153896				0	bs	Escape closes an open submenu, a toolbar, or the current free window.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	hd_id3161656				0	bs	Calling a menu command				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3153381				0	bs	Arrow down opens a selected menu. Any additional arrow down and up arrow move the selection through the menu commands. With right arrow you open any existing submenus.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3148798				0	bs	Press Enter to execute the selected menu command.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147086				0	bs	Executing an icon command				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3148922				0	bs	Press F6 repeatedly until the first icon on the toolbar is selected. Use the right and left arrows to select an icon on a horizontal toolbar. Similarly, use the up and down arrows to select an icon on a vertical toolbar. The Home key selects the first icon on a toolbar and the End key, the last.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3151041				0	bs	If a toolbar is longer than can be displayed on screen, it shows an icon at the right or lower edge. Select the toolbar and press PageUp or PageDown to display the remaining icons.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150440				0	bs	Special hints for toolbars				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3149983				0	bs	Press the down arrow or right arrow to open the selected toolbar. This is equivalent to a mouse click. In the toolbar use the right arrow and left arrow keys. The Home and End keys select the first and last icon in the toolbar, respectively.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3145365				0	bs	Close the toolbar with Esc. It is not possible to move the toolbar without a mouse.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	hd_id3151119				0	bs	Selection from a combo box				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3149666				0	bs	Select the combo box. Press Enter.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3155366				0	bs	Use the down arrow or Page Down key to scroll down the combo box entries, or the up arrow or Page Up key to scroll upwards. The Home key takes you to the first entry and the End key takes you to the last entry.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3145749				0	bs	Press Enter to execute the selected entry.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150685				0	bs	Selection in Tables				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3154320				0	bs	In several windows, dialogs, and in the table control field, there are tables to select data, for instance, in the right part of the \<link href=\"text/shared/guide/database_main.xhp\" name=\"Data Source View\"\>Data Source View\</link\>. The following keys are used for selections in these tables:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3154014				0	bs	Spacebar: switches from selection of the current row and cancellation of any selection, but not if the current cell is in edit mode.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150592				0	bs	Size and Position of Windows and Dialogs				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3148456				0	bs	A system menu opens with menu commands like \<emph\>Move\</emph\>, \<emph\>Resize\</emph\> and \<emph\>Close\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3149400				0	bs	Choose a command (down arrow, then Enter).				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3155083				0	bs	Now you can use the arrow keys to move or resize the dialog or window.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3147497				0	bs	Press Enter to accept the change. Press Escape to cancel the changes.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	hd_id3146988				0	bs	Docking and Undocking Windows and Toolbars				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3147176				0	bs	Press F6 until the window or toolbar is selected.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154479				0	bs	Selecting objects				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3148993				0	bs	Press \<item type=\"keycode\"\>Shift+F5\</item\> to select the first object in the current document. When an object is selected, press \<item type=\"keycode\"\>Tab\</item\> to select the next object, or press \<item type=\"keycode\"\>Esc\</item\> to go back to the text.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	hd_id3152962				0	bs	Edit Objects				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3156379				0	bs	A selected OLE object can be activated with the Enter key.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155766				0	bs	Edit Position and Size of Objects				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3148405				0	bs	Use the arrow keys to move the selected object by one grid resolution unit.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3149565				0	bs	In the handle edit mode, the arrow keys move the selected handle, which changes the object size.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147361				0	bs	Edit the Anchors of Objects				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3148534				0	bs	You can move the anchor of an object with the arrow keys. First enter the handle edit mode and select the anchor. Depending on the type of anchor, you can then move the anchor in different directions.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3163808				0	bs	Select the object.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3153919				0	bs	Use the arrow keys to move the anchor. The object follows the anchor as appropriate.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3152582				0	bs	You can change the anchor of the selected object for example in the object's context menu.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3148393				0	bs	If the object is anchored \<emph\>To Paragraph\</emph\>, the arrow keys move the object to the previous or next paragraph.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3145615	69			0	bs	If the object is anchored\<emph\> To page\</emph\>, the keys Page Up or Page Down move it to the previous or next page.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3145135				0	bs	If the object is anchored \<emph\>To character\</emph\>, the Arrow keys move it through the current paragraph.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3145256	71			0	bs	If the object is anchored\<emph\> As character\</emph\>, no anchor icon exists. You cannot move the object.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3149527				0	bs	If the object is anchored \<emph\>To frame\</emph\>, the Arrow keys move it to the next frame in the respective direction.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153270				0	bs	Controlling the Dividing Lines				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3158413	134			0	bs	Documents of \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> Calc, \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> Draw, and \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> Impress can be split horizontally and vertically into separate views. Each view can show other parts of the document. Using the mouse, you can drag a dividing line from the scrollbar into the document.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3158444				0	bs	Arrow keys: moves the current dividing line a big step in the arrow direction.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3163668				0	bs	Shift+Arrow keys: moves the current dividing line a small step in the arrow direction.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3148426				0	bs	Delete: deletes the current dividing line				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3151277				0	bs	Shift+Delete: deletes both dividing lines				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3150383				0	bs	Enter: fixes the current position of the dividing lines				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3150369				0	bs	Escape: resets the current dividing line to its default position				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154492				0	bs	Controlling the Data Source View				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3150515				0	bs	F4: opens and closes the data source view.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3159109				0	bs	F6: switches between document and toolbars.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3153229				0	bs	+ (plus key): expands the selected entry in the data source explorer.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3150312				0	bs	- (minus key): collapses the selected entry in the data source explorer.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147171				0	bs	Shortcuts in the Query Design Window				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3152455				0	bs	F6: switches between object bar, table view, and selection area.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156288				0	bs	Keys in the Table View (upper area of the query design) and in the Relations window				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3152986				0	bs	Del: removes the selected table or connection from the table view.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3145384				0	bs	Tab: switches between tables and connections in the table view.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3154529				0	bs	Enter: when a connection is selected, the Enter key opens the \<emph\>Properties\</emph\> dialog of the connection.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3159624				0	bs	Enter: when a table is selected, the Enter key enters the first data field from the list box into the selection area.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153816				0	bs	Keys in the Selection Area (bottom area of the query design)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	hd_id3146152				0	bs	Keys in the Table Design Window				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3151243				0	bs	F6: switches between toolbar, column view, and properties area.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145075				0	bs	Controlling the ImageMap Editor				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3156016				0	bs	If you press Enter while the icon \<emph\>Select\</emph\> is selected, the focus is set into the image window of the ImageMap Editor. Press Esc to set the focus back to the icons and input boxes.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3149587				0	bs	If the icon \<emph\>Select\</emph\> is selected and you press Ctrl+Enter, the first object in the image window gets selected.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3154343				0	bs	Use the icon \<emph\>Edit Points\</emph\> to switch into the point edit mode for polygons and back.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3147073				0	bs	Use Ctrl+Tab in the image window to select the next point. Use Shift+Ctrl+Tab to select the previous point.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3153285				0	bs	Use the Delete key with the focus in the image window to delete the selected object.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145377				0	bs	Controlling the Help				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3149441				0	bs	Press Shift+F2 to display the \<link href=\"text/shared/main0108.xhp\" name=\"Extended Tips\"\>Extended Tips\</link\> for the currently selected command, icon or control.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154960				0	bs	Navigating the main help pages				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3151300				0	bs	In the main help pages, use Tab to jump to the next hyperlink or Shift+Tab to jump to the previous link.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3155537				0	bs	Press Enter to execute the selected hyperlink.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
