helpcontent2	source\text\shared\07\09000000.xhp	0	help	par_id3146946				0	bs	To create a new web page for the Internet, open a new \<emph\>HTML Document\</emph\> by choosing \<emph\>File - New\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\07\09000000.xhp	0	help	par_id3143284				0	bs	A tool for creating new web pages is the Online-Layout-Mode, which you can open by choosing \<emph\>View - Online Layout\</emph\>. As soon as you have activated this mode you will see only those options in the menus and dialogs of $[officename] which can be used on HTML pages.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\07\09000000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147285				0	bs	Creating a New Web Page				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\07\09000000.xhp	0	help	par_id3150808				0	bs	Switch to the online layout mode by choosing \<emph\>View - Online Layout\</emph\> or by opening a new HTML document. $[officename] will then internally use the html.stw template.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\07\09000000.xhp	0	help	par_id3145136				0	bs	To create an HTML page from your $[officename] document, save the page using one of the "HTML Document" file types, such as the .HTM or .HTML extensions.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
