helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\dabaadvpropdat.xhp	0	help	par_idN10566				0	bs	Specifies the way you can work with data in a database.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\dabaadvpropdat.xhp	0	help	par_idN10590				0	bs	Use SQL92 naming constraints				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\dabaadvpropdat.xhp	0	help	par_idN10594				0	bs	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>Only allows characters that conform to the SQL92 naming convention in a name in a data source. All other characters are rejected. Each name must begin with a lowercase letter, an uppercase letter, or an underscore ( _ ). The remaining characters can be ASCII letters, numbers, and underscores.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\dabaadvpropdat.xhp	0	help	par_idN1059E				0	bs	Append the table alias name in SELECT statements				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\dabaadvpropdat.xhp	0	help	par_idN105A2				0	bs	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>Appends the alias to the table name in SELECT statements.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\dabaadvpropdat.xhp	0	help	par_idN105A5				0	bs	Use Outer Join syntax '{OJ }'				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\dabaadvpropdat.xhp	0	help	par_idN105A9				0	bs	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>Use escape sequences for outer joins. The syntax for this escape sequence is {oj outer-join}\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\dabaadvpropdat.xhp	0	help	par_idN105BE				0	bs	Example:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\dabaadvpropdat.xhp	0	help	par_idN105C1				0	bs	select Article.* from {oj item LEFT OUTER JOIN orders ON item.no=orders.ANR}				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\dabaadvpropdat.xhp	0	help	par_idN105C4				0	bs	Ignore the privileges from the database driver				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\dabaadvpropdat.xhp	0	help	par_idN105C8				0	bs	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>Ignores access privileges that are provided by the database driver.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\dabaadvpropdat.xhp	0	help	par_idN105CB				0	bs	Replace named parameters with ?				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\dabaadvpropdat.xhp	0	help	par_idN105CF				0	bs	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>Replaces named parameters in a data source with a question mark (?).\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\dabaadvpropdat.xhp	0	help	par_idN105D2				0	bs	Display version columns (when available)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\dabaadvpropdat.xhp	0	help	par_idN105D6				0	bs	Some databases assign version numbers to fields to track changes to records. The version number of a field is incremented by one each time the contents of the field are changed. \<ahelp hid=\"HID_DSADMIN_SUPPRESS_VERSIONCL\"\>Displays the internal version number of the record in the database table.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
