helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\3d_create.xhp	0	help	par_id3154762				0	bs	Polygon object consisting of straight line segments				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\3d_create.xhp	0	help	par_id3150051				0	bs	3D object with shading and a light source				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\3d_create.xhp	0	help	par_id3149873				0	bs	3D rotation object with shading and a light source				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\3d_create.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149048				0	bs	To convert an object to a curved shape:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\3d_create.xhp	0	help	par_id3147295				0	bs	Select a 2D object on the slide or page.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\3d_create.xhp	0	help	par_id3150654				0	bs	Right-click the object and choose \<emph\>Convert - To Curve\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\3d_create.xhp	0	help	par_id3145828				0	bs	To modify the shape of the object, click the \<emph\>Points\</emph\> icon \<image id=\"img_id1027558\" src=\"svx/res/cd015.png\" width=\"0.222inch\" height=\"0.222inch\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id1027558\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\> on the \<emph\>Drawing\</emph\> toolbar, and drag the handles of the object. You can also drag the control points of a handle to modify the shape of the curve.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\3d_create.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153738				0	bs	To convert a 2D object to a polygon:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\3d_create.xhp	0	help	par_id3145241				0	bs	Select a 2D object on the slide or page.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\3d_create.xhp	0	help	par_id3148774				0	bs	Right-click the object and choose \<emph\>Convert - To Polygon.\</emph\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\3d_create.xhp	0	help	par_id3155368				0	bs	To modify the shape of the object, click the \<emph\>Points\</emph\> icon \<image id=\"img_id7219458\" src=\"svx/res/cd015.png\" width=\"0.2201inch\" height=\"0.2201inch\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id7219458\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\> on the \<emph\>Drawing\</emph\> toolbar, and drag the handles of the object.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
