helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\rehearse_timings.xhp	0	help	tit				0	bs	Rehearse Timings of Slide Changes				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\rehearse_timings.xhp	0	help	bm_id3145253				0	bs	\<bookmark_value\>presentations;rehearse timings\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>rehearse timings\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>timings; rehearse timings\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>automatic slide changes;rehearse timings\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>recording;display times for slides\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\rehearse_timings.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145253				0	bs	\<variable id=\"rehearse_timings\"\>\<link href=\"text/simpress/guide/rehearse_timings.xhp\" name=\"Rehearse Timings of Slide Changes\"\>Rehearse Timings of Slide Changes\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\rehearse_timings.xhp	0	help	par_id3155446	1			0	bs	$[officename] assists you in defining the right rehearse timings for automatic slide changes. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\rehearse_timings.xhp	0	help	par_id3153963				0	bs	Prepare the slides, start the show using a special icon, tell your imaginary audience what you want to tell for the first slide, then advance to the next slide and so on. $[officename] records the display time for each slide, so the next time you play the show with automatic slide changes, the timing will be as recorded.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\rehearse_timings.xhp	0	help	hd_id3146317				0	bs	To record a show with rehearse timings:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\rehearse_timings.xhp	0	help	par_id3149874				0	bs	Open a presentation, and switch to \<emph\>Slide Sorter\</emph\> View.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\rehearse_timings.xhp	0	help	par_id3145590				0	bs	When it's time to advance to the next slide, click the timer. Continue for all slides in your presentation.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\rehearse_timings.xhp	0	help	par_id3150333				0	bs	$[officename] has recorded the display time for each slide. You may edit the timings in the Slide View bar. Save your presentation.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\rehearse_timings.xhp	0	help	par_id3145248				0	bs	If you want the whole presentation to auto-repeat, open the menu \<emph\>Slide Show - Slide Show Settings\</emph\>. Click \<emph\>Auto\</emph\> and \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\rehearse_timings.xhp	0	help	par_id3150935				0	bs	\<link href=\"text/simpress/01/06080000.xhp\" name=\"Slide Show Settings\"\>Slide Show Settings\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\line_edit.xhp	0	help	tit				0	bs	Editing Curves				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\line_edit.xhp	0	help	bm_id3150441				0	bs	\<bookmark_value\>curves; editing (guide)\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>editing; curves\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>points; editing\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>splitting;curves\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>closing;shapes\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>deleting;points\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>converting;points\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>adding;points\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\line_edit.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150441				0	bs	\<variable id=\"line_edit\"\>\<link href=\"text/simpress/guide/line_edit.xhp\" name=\"Editing Curves\"\>Editing Curves\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\line_edit.xhp	0	help	par_id3150342				0	bs	A curved line segment consists of two data points (endpoints) and two control points (handles). A control line connects a control point to a data point. You can change the shape of a curve by converting a data point to a different type, or by dragging the control points to a different location.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\line_edit.xhp	0	help	par_id3145252				0	bs	You can also modify the properties of the line by selecting the line and choosing \<emph\>Format - Line\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\line_edit.xhp	0	help	par_id3153711				0	bs	\<image id=\"img_id3149018\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_toggleobjectbeziermode.png\" width=\"5.64mm\" height=\"5.64mm\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3149018\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\line_edit.xhp	0	help	par_id3155959				0	bs	To view the data points and control points of a curved line, select the line, and then click the \<emph\>Points\</emph\> icon on the Drawing bar. The data points are represented by squares and the control points by circles. A control point might overlay a data point.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\line_edit.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145587				0	bs	To adjust a curved line segment:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\line_edit.xhp	0	help	par_id3151241	51			0	bs	Select a curved line, and then click the \<emph\>Points \</emph\>icon on the \<emph\>Drawing\</emph\> Bar.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\line_edit.xhp	0	help	par_id3150213				0	bs	Do one of the following:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\line_edit.xhp	0	help	par_id3153810				0	bs	Drag a data point to resize the line. If a control point overlies the data point, drag the control point until you can see the data point, and then drag the data point.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\line_edit.xhp	0	help	par_id3149872				0	bs	Drag a control point. The curve pulls in the direction that you drag the control point.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
