helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\text_enter.xhp	0	help	par_idN1082C				0	bs	Text that is added to any drawing object by double-clicking the object				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\text_enter.xhp	0	help	par_idN10830				0	bs	Text that is copied from a Writer document				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\text_enter.xhp	0	help	par_idN10834				0	bs	Text that is inserted from a text or HTML document				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\text_enter.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150202				0	bs	Adding a Text Frame				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\text_enter.xhp	0	help	par_id3155266	49			0	bs	Click the \<emph\>Text\</emph\> icon \<image id=\"img_id3156450\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_text.png\" width=\"5.64mm\" height=\"5.64mm\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3156450\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\> and move the mouse pointer to where you want to enter the text.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\text_enter.xhp	0	help	par_id3149052				0	bs	Drag a text frame to the size you want in your document.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\text_enter.xhp	0	help	par_id3151194				0	bs	Type or paste your text in the text frame.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\text_enter.xhp	0	help	par_id3145118				0	bs	Double-click the text to edit it or to format text properties, such as font size or font color. Click the border of the text object to edit the object properties, such as border color or arranging in front or behind other objects.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\text_enter.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150437				0	bs	Fitting Text to Frames				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\text_enter.xhp	0	help	par_id3146877				0	bs	Create a text frame as described in the steps above. The size of the frame determines the size of the text.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\text_enter.xhp	0	help	par_idN108A3				0	bs	With the text object selected, choose \<emph\>Format - Text\</emph\>. The \<emph\>Text\</emph\> dialog opens.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\text_enter.xhp	0	help	par_idN108AF				0	bs	On the \<emph\>Text\</emph\> tab page, clear the \<emph\>Fit height to text\</emph\> checkbox, then select the \<emph\>Fit to frame\</emph\> checkbox. Click OK.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\text_enter.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155955				0	bs	Text Tied to a Graphic				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\text_enter.xhp	0	help	par_idN10917				0	bs	You can add text to any graphic after double-clicking the graphic.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\text_enter.xhp	0	help	par_id3147366	59			0	bs	Click the arrow next to the \<emph\>Callouts\</emph\> icon \<image id=\"img_id3154508\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_calloutshapes.png\" width=\"5.64mm\" height=\"5.64mm\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3154508\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\> to open the Callouts toolbar.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\text_enter.xhp	0	help	par_idN108FD				0	bs	Select a callout and move the mouse pointer to where you want the callout to start.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\text_enter.xhp	0	help	par_id3150272				0	bs	Drag to draw the callout.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\text_enter.xhp	0	help	par_idN1091A				0	bs	Copying Text				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\text_enter.xhp	0	help	par_idN10921				0	bs	Select the text in your Writer document.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\text_enter.xhp	0	help	par_idN10925				0	bs	Copy the text to the clipboard (\<emph\>Edit - Copy\</emph\>).				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\text_enter.xhp	0	help	par_idN1092D				0	bs	Click the page or slide where you want to paste the text.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\text_enter.xhp	0	help	par_idN10931				0	bs	Paste the text using \<emph\>Edit - Paste\</emph\> or \<emph\>Edit - Paste special\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\text_enter.xhp	0	help	par_idN1093C				0	bs	Using Paste special, you can choose the text format to be pasted. Depending on formats, you can copy different text attributes.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\text_enter.xhp	0	help	par_idN1093F				0	bs	Importing Text				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\text_enter.xhp	0	help	par_idN10946				0	bs	Click the page or slide where you want to import the text.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\text_enter.xhp	0	help	par_idN1094A				0	bs	Choose \<emph\>Insert - File\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\text_enter.xhp	0	help	par_idN10952				0	bs	Select a text file (*.txt) or an HTML file and click \<emph\>Insert\</emph\>. The \<emph\>Insert Text\</emph\> dialog opens. Click OK to insert the text.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\groups.xhp	0	help	tit				0	bs	Grouping Objects				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\groups.xhp	0	help	bm_id3150793				0	bs	\<bookmark_value\>grouping; draw objects\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>draw objects; grouping\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>groups; entering\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>selecting;group objects\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\groups.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150793				0	bs	\<variable id=\"groups\"\>\<link href=\"text/sdraw/guide/groups.xhp\" name=\"Grouping Objects\"\>Grouping Objects\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\groups.xhp	0	help	par_id3153728				0	bs	You can combine several objects into a group so that they act as a single object. You can move and transform all objects in a group as a single unit. You can also change the properties (for example, line size, fill color) of all objects in a group as a whole or for individual objects in a group. Groups can be temporary or assigned:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\groups.xhp	0	help	par_id3147434				0	bs	Temporary - group only lasts as long as all of the combined objects are selected.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\groups.xhp	0	help	par_id3154490				0	bs	Assigned - group lasts until it is ungrouped through a menu command.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\groups.xhp	0	help	par_id3145252				0	bs	Groups can also be grouped in other groups. Actions applied to a group do not affect the relative position of the individual objects to each other in the group.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\groups.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150716				0	bs	To group objects:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\groups.xhp	0	help	par_id3149018				0	bs	\<image id=\"img_id3145643\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_formatgroup.png\" width=\"4.23mm\" height=\"4.23mm\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3145643\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\groups.xhp	0	help	par_id3147346				0	bs	Select the objects you want to group and choose \<emph\>Modify - Group\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\groups.xhp	0	help	par_id3148485				0	bs	For example, you can group all of the objects in a company logo to move and resize the logo as a single object.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\groups.xhp	0	help	par_id3147002				0	bs	After you have grouped objects, selecting any part of the group selects the entire group.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\groups.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150205				0	bs	Selecting Objects in a Group				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\groups.xhp	0	help	par_id3150370				0	bs	\<image id=\"img_id3155376\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_entergroup.png\" width=\"4.23mm\" height=\"4.23mm\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3155376\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\groups.xhp	0	help	par_id3156450				0	bs	You can select single objects in a group by entering the group. Double-click a group to enter it and click on the object to select it. You can also add or delete objects to and from a group in this mode. The objects that are not part of the group are grayed out.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\groups.xhp	0	help	par_id3151239				0	bs	\<image id=\"img_id3155264\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_leavegroup.png\" width=\"4.23mm\" height=\"4.23mm\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3155264\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\groups.xhp	0	help	par_id3150213				0	bs	To exit a group, double-click anywhere outside it.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\draw_sector.xhp	0	help	tit				0	bs	Drawing Sectors and Segments				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\draw_sector.xhp	0	help	bm_id3146974				0	bs	\<bookmark_value\>sectors of circles/ellipses\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>segments of circles/ellipses\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>circles; segments\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>ellipses; segments\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>drawing; sectors and segments\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\draw_sector.xhp	0	help	hd_id3146974				0	bs	\<variable id=\"draw_sector\"\>\<link href=\"text/sdraw/guide/draw_sector.xhp\" name=\"Drawing Sectors and Segments\"\>Drawing Sectors and Segments\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\draw_sector.xhp	0	help	par_id3147396				0	bs	The \<emph\>Ellipse\</emph\> toolbar contains tools for drawing ellipses and circles. You can also draw segments and sectors of circles and ellipses.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\draw_sector.xhp	0	help	hd_id3151075				0	bs	To draw a sector of a circle or an ellipse:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\draw_sector.xhp	0	help	par_id3155335	33			0	bs	Open the \<emph\>Ellipses\</emph\> toolbar and click one of the \<emph\>Circle Pie\</emph\> or \<emph\>Ellipse Pie\</emph\> icons \<image id=\"img_id3155768\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_circlepie_unfilled.png\" width=\"5.64mm\" height=\"5.64mm\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3155768\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>. The mouse pointer changes to a cross hair with a small icon of a sector.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\draw_sector.xhp	0	help	par_id3150199				0	bs	Position the pointer at the edge of the circle you want to draw and drag to create the circle.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\draw_sector.xhp	0	help	par_id3148868				0	bs	To create a circle by dragging from the center, press \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Option \</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Alt\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> while dragging.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\draw_sector.xhp	0	help	par_id3145361				0	bs	Release the mouse button when the circle has reached the size you want. A line corresponding to the circle radius appears in the circle.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\draw_sector.xhp	0	help	par_id3149872				0	bs	Position the pointer where you want to place the first boundary of the sector and click.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\draw_sector.xhp	0	help	par_id3157871				0	bs	As the radius line that follows the pointer is constrained to the circle boundaries, you can click anywhere in the document.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\draw_sector.xhp	0	help	par_id3146874				0	bs	Position the pointer where you want to place the second boundary of the sector and click. The completed sector is displayed.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\draw_sector.xhp	0	help	par_id3148581				0	bs	To draw a segment of a circle or ellipse, follow the steps for creating a sector based on a circle.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\draw_sector.xhp	0	help	par_id3153084				0	bs	To draw an arc based on an ellipse, choose one of the arc icons and follow the same steps for creating a sector based on a circle.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\join_objects3d.xhp	0	help	tit				0	bs	Assembling 3D Objects				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\join_objects3d.xhp	0	help	bm_id3154014				0	bs	\<bookmark_value\>3D objects; assembling\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>assembled objects in 3D\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>combining;3D objects\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>joining;3D objects\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\join_objects3d.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156442				0	bs	\<variable id=\"join_objects3d\"\>\<link href=\"text/sdraw/guide/join_objects3d.xhp\" name=\"Assembling 3D Objects\"\>Assembling 3D Objects\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\join_objects3d.xhp	0	help	par_id3145251				0	bs	You can combine two or more 3D objects into a single object.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\join_objects3d.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150042				0	bs	To combine 3D objects:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\join_objects3d.xhp	0	help	par_id3154702				0	bs	Insert a 3D object from the \<emph\>3D Objects\</emph\> toolbar (for example, a cube).				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\join_objects3d.xhp	0	help	par_id3155335				0	bs	Insert a second slightly larger 3D object (for example, a sphere).				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\join_objects3d.xhp	0	help	par_id3148488				0	bs	Select the second 3D object (sphere) and choose \<emph\>Edit - Cut\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\join_objects3d.xhp	0	help	par_id3149211				0	bs	Double-click the first object (cube) to enter its group.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\join_objects3d.xhp	0	help	par_id3154652				0	bs	Choose \<emph\>Edit - Paste\</emph\>. Both objects are now part of the same group. If you want, you can edit the individual objects or change their position within the group.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\join_objects3d.xhp	0	help	par_id3155376				0	bs	Double-click outside the group to exit the group.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\join_objects3d.xhp	0	help	par_id3148606				0	bs	You cannot intersect or subtract 3D objects.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\join_objects3d.xhp	0	help	par_id3154537				0	bs	\<link href=\"text/simpress/02/10090000.xhp\" name=\"Objects in 3D\"\>Objects in 3D\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\graphic_insert.xhp	0	help	tit				0	bs	Inserting Graphics				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\graphic_insert.xhp	0	help	bm_id3156443				0	bs	\<bookmark_value\>pictures; inserting\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>images; inserting\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>files; inserting pictures\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>inserting;pictures\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\graphic_insert.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156443				0	bs	\<variable id=\"graphic_insert\"\>\<link href=\"text/sdraw/guide/graphic_insert.xhp\" name=\"Inserting Graphics\"\>Inserting Pictures\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\graphic_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id3155600				0	bs	Choose \<emph\>Insert - Picture\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\graphic_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id3150749				0	bs	Locate the picture you want to insert. Select the \<emph\>Link\</emph\> check box to insert only a link to the picture. If you want to see the picture before you insert it, select \<emph\>Preview\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\graphic_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id3155764				0	bs	After you insert a linked picture, do not change the name of the source picture or move the source picture to another directory.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\graphic_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id3150044				0	bs	Click \<emph\>Open\</emph\> to insert the picture.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\main.xhp	0	help	tit				0	bs	Instructions for Using $[officename] Draw				2002-02-02 02:02:02
