helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060107.xhp	0	help	par_id3166176				0	bs	\<emph\>New Data_X\</emph\> (optional) represents the array of the X data, which are used for recalculating values.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060107.xhp	0	help	par_id3166196				0	bs	\<emph\>Linear_Type\</emph\>(Optional). If \<emph\>Linear_Type\</emph\> = 0, then lines will be calculated through the zero point. Otherwise, offset lines will also be calculated. The default is \<emph\>Linear_Type\</emph\> <> 0.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060107.xhp	0	help	hd_id3166231				0	bs	Example				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060107.xhp	0	help	par_id3166245				0	bs	Select a spreadsheet range in which the trend data will appear. Select the function. Enter the output data or select it with the mouse. Mark the \<emph\>Array\</emph\> field. click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>. The trend data calculated from the output data is displayed.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060107.xhp	0	help	bm_id3166317				0	bs	\<bookmark_value\>GROWTH function\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060107.xhp	0	help	hd_id3166317				0	bs	GROWTH				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060107.xhp	0	help	par_id3166346				0	bs	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_VARIATION\"\>Calculates the points of an exponential trend in an array.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060107.xhp	0	help	hd_id3166364				0	bs	Syntax				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060107.xhp	0	help	par_id3166377				0	bs	Growth(Data_Y;Data_X; New_Data_X; Function_type)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060107.xhp	0	help	par_id3166392				0	bs	\<emph\>Data_Y\</emph\> represents the Y Data array.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060107.xhp	0	help	par_id3166411				0	bs	\<emph\>Data_X\</emph\> (optional) represents the X Data array.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060107.xhp	0	help	par_id3173797				0	bs	\<emph\>New_Data_X\</emph\> (optional) represents the X data array, in which the values are recalculated.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060107.xhp	0	help	par_id3173817				0	bs	\<emph\>Function_Type\</emph\>(optional). If Function_Type = 0, functions in the form y = m^x will be calculated. Otherwise, y = b*m^x functions will be calculated.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060107.xhp	0	help	hd_id3173839				0	bs	Example				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060107.xhp	0	help	par_id3173852				0	bs	This function returns an array and is handled in the same way as the other array functions. Select a range where you want the answers to appear and select the function. Select Data_Y. Enter any other parameters, mark \<emph\>Array\</emph\> and click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\02140400.xhp	0	help	tit				0	bs	Left				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\02140400.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153896				0	bs	\<link href=\"text/scalc/01/02140400.xhp\" name=\"Left\"\>Left\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\02140400.xhp	0	help	par_id3150793				0	bs	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:FillLeft\" visibility=\"visible\"\>Fills a selected range of at least two columns with the contents of the far right cell.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\02140400.xhp	0	help	par_id3156280				0	bs	If a selected range has only one row, the content of the far right cell is copied into all other cells of the range. If several rows are selected, the far right cells are copied into the cells to the left.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\05030200.xhp	0	help	tit				0	bs	Optimal Row Heights				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\05030200.xhp	0	help	bm_id3148491				0	bs	\<bookmark_value\>sheets; optimal row heights\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>rows; optimal heights\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>optimal row heights\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\05030200.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148491				0	bs	Optimal Row Heights				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\05030200.xhp	0	help	par_id3154758				0	bs	\<variable id=\"optitext\"\>\<ahelp hid=\".uno:SetOptimalRowHeight\"\>Determines the optimal row height for the selected rows.\</ahelp\>\</variable\> The optimal row height depends on the font size of the largest character in the row. You can use various \<link href=\"text/shared/00/00000003.xhp#metrik\" name=\"units of measure\"\>units of measure\</link\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\05030200.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154908				0	bs	Add				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\05030200.xhp	0	help	par_id3151044				0	bs	\<ahelp hid=\"SC:METRICFIELD:RID_SCDLG_ROW_OPT:ED_VALUE\"\>Sets additional spacing between the largest character in a row and the cell boundaries.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\05030200.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150439				0	bs	Default value				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\05030200.xhp	0	help	par_id3146984				0	bs	\<ahelp hid=\"SC:CHECKBOX:RID_SCDLG_ROW_OPT:BTN_DEFVAL\"\>Restores the default value for the optimal row height.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	tit				0	bs	Spreadsheet Functions				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	bm_id3148522				0	bs	\<bookmark_value\>spreadsheets; functions\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>Function Wizard; spreadsheets\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>functions; spreadsheets\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148522				0	bs	Spreadsheet Functions				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	par_id3144508				0	bs	\<variable id=\"tabelletext\"\>This section contains descriptions of the \<emph\>Spreadsheet\</emph\> functions together with an example. \</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	bm_id3146968				0	bs	\<bookmark_value\>ADDRESS function\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	hd_id3146968				0	bs	ADDRESS				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	par_id3155762				0	bs	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_ADRESSE\"\>Returns a cell address (reference) as text, according to the specified row and column numbers.\</ahelp\> You can determine whether the address is interpreted as an absolute address (for example, $A$1) or as a relative address (as A1) or in a mixed form (A$1 or $A1). You can also specify the name of the sheet.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	hd_id3151196				0	bs	Syntax				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	par_id3154707				0	bs	ADDRESS(row; column; abs;sheet)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	par_id3147505	7			0	bs	\<emph\>row\</emph\> represents the row number for the cell reference				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	par_id3145323	8			0	bs	\<emph\>column\</emph\> represents the column number for the cell reference (the number, not the letter)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	par_id3153074	9			0	bs	\<emph\>abs\</emph\> determines the type of reference:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	par_id3153298				0	bs	1: absolute ($A$1)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	par_id3150431				0	bs	2: row reference type is absolute; column reference is relative (A$1)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	par_id3146096				0	bs	3: row (relative); column (absolute) ($A1)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	par_id3153334				0	bs	4: relative (A1)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	par_id3153962	14			0	bs	\<emph\>sheet\</emph\> represents the name of the sheet. It must be placed in double quotes.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147299				0	bs	Example:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	par_id3148744	16			0	bs	ADDRESS(1; 1; 2; "Sheet2") returns the following: Sheet2.A$1				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	par_id3159260				0	bs	If the cell A1 in sheet 2 contains the value -6, you can refer indirectly to the referenced cell using a function in B2 by entering =ABS(INDIRECT(B2)). The result is the absolute value of the cell reference specified in B2, which in this case is 6.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	bm_id3150372				0	bs	\<bookmark_value\>AREAS function\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150372				0	bs	AREAS				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	par_id3150036				0	bs	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_BEREICHE\"\>Returns the number of individual ranges that belong to a multiple range.\</ahelp\> A range can consist of contiguous cells or a single cell.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145222				0	bs	Syntax				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	par_id3155907				0	bs	AREAS(Reference)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	par_id3153118				0	bs	Reference represents the reference to a cell or cell range.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148891				0	bs	Example				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	par_id3149946	25			0	bs	=AREAS(A1:B3;F2;G1) returns 3, as it is a reference to three cells and/or areas.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	par_id3146820	26			0	bs	=AREAS(All) returns 1 if you have defined an area named All under \<emph\>Data - Define Range\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	bm_id3148727				0	bs	\<bookmark_value\>DDE function\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148727				0	bs	DDE				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	par_id3149434				0	bs	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_DDE\"\>Returns the result of a DDE-based link.\</ahelp\> If the contents of the linked range or section changes, the returned value will also change. You must reload the spreadsheet or choose \<emph\>Edit - Links\</emph\> to see the updated links. Cross-platform links, for example from a \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> installation running on a Windows machine to a document created on a Linux machine, are not allowed.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150700				0	bs	Syntax				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	par_id3148886				0	bs	DDE(server;file;range;mode)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	par_id3154842	32			0	bs	\<emph\>Server\</emph\> is the name of a server application. \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> applications have the server name "Soffice".				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	par_id3153034	33			0	bs	\<emph\>File\</emph\> is the complete file name, including path specification.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	par_id3147472	34			0	bs	\<emph\>Range\</emph\> is the area containing the data to be evaluated.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	par_id3152773	184			0	bs	\<emph\>Mode\</emph\> is an optional parameter that controls the method by which the DDE server converts its data into numbers.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	par_id3154383	185			0	bs	\<emph\>Mode\</emph\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	par_id3145146	186			0	bs	\<emph\>Effect\</emph\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	par_id3154558				0	bs	0 or missing				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	par_id3145596				0	bs	Number format from the "Default" cell style				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	par_id3152785				0	bs	1				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	par_id3154380				0	bs	Data are always interpreted in the standard format for US English				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	par_id3150279				0	bs	2				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	par_id3153775				0	bs	Data are retrieved as text; no conversion to numbers				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149546				0	bs	Example				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	par_id3148734	36			0	bs	\<item type=\"keycode\"\>=DDE("soffice";"c:\\office\\document\\data1.sxc";"sheet1.A1")\</item\> reads the contents of cell A1 in sheet1 of the \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> Calc spreadsheet data1.sxc.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	par_id3153081	37			0	bs	\<item type=\"keycode\"\>=DDE("soffice";"c:\\office\\document\\motto.sxw";"Today's motto")\</item\> returns a motto in the cell containing this formula. First, you must enter a line in the motto.sxw document containing the motto text and define it as the first line of a section named \<item type=\"literal\"\>Today's Motto\</item\> (in \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> Writer under \<emph\>Insert - Section\</emph\>). If the motto is modified (and saved) in the \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> Writer document, the motto is updated in all \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> Calc cells in which this DDE link is defined.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	bm_id3153114				0	bs	\<bookmark_value\>ERRORTYPE function\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153114				0	bs	ERRORTYPE				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	par_id3148568				0	bs	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_FEHLERTYP\"\>Returns the number corresponding to an \<link href=\"text/scalc/05/02140000.xhp\" name=\"error value\"\>error value\</link\> occurring in a different cell.\</ahelp\> With the aid of this number, you can generate an error message text.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	par_id3149877				0	bs	The Status Bar displays the predefined error code from \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> if you click the cell containing the error.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154327				0	bs	Syntax				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	par_id3151322				0	bs	ERRORTYPE(Reference)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	par_id3150132	43			0	bs	\<emph\>Reference\</emph\> contains the address of the cell in which the error occurs.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145248				0	bs	Example				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	par_id3146904				0	bs	If cell A1 displays Err:518, the function =ERRORTYPE(A1) returns the number 518.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	bm_id3151221				0	bs	\<bookmark_value\>INDEX function\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	hd_id3151221				0	bs	INDEX				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	par_id3150268				0	bs	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_INDEX\"\>INDEX returns the content of a cell, specified by row and column number or an optional range name.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156063				0	bs	Syntax				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	par_id3149007				0	bs	INDEX(reference;row;column;range)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	par_id3153260	51			0	bs	\<emph\>reference\</emph\> is a cell reference, entered either directly or by specifying a range name. If the reference consists of multiple ranges, you must enclose the reference or range name in parentheses.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	par_id3145302	52			0	bs	\<emph\>row\</emph\> (optional) represents the row number of the reference range, for which to return a value.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	par_id3154628	53			0	bs	\<emph\>column\</emph\> (optional) represents the column number of the reference range, for which to return a value.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	par_id3155514	54			0	bs	\<emph\>range\</emph\> (optional) represents the index of the subrange if referring to a multiple range.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145264				0	bs	Example				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	par_id3159112	56			0	bs	=INDEX(Prices;4;1) returns the value from row 4 and column 1 of the database range defined in \<emph\>Data - Define\</emph\> as \<emph\>Prices\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	par_id3150691	57			0	bs	=INDEX(SumX;4;1) returns the value from the range \<emph\>SumX\</emph\> in row 4 and column 1 as defined in \<emph\>Insert - Names - Define\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	par_id3158419	58			0	bs	=INDEX((multi);4;1) indicates the value contained in row 4 and column 1 of the (multiple) range, which you named under \<emph\>Insert - Names - Set\</emph\> as \<emph\>multi\</emph\>. The multiple range may consist of several rectangular ranges, each with a row 4 and column 1. If you now want to call the second block of this multiple range enter the number 2 as the \<emph\>range\</emph\> parameter.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	par_id3148595	59			0	bs	=INDEX(A1:B6;1;1) indicates the value in the upper-left of the A1:B6 range.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	bm_id3153181				0	bs	\<bookmark_value\>INDIRECT function\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153181				0	bs	INDIRECT				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	par_id3147169				0	bs	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_INDIREKT\"\>Returns the \<emph\>reference\</emph\> specified by a text string.\</ahelp\> This function can also be used to return the area of a corresponding string.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153717				0	bs	Syntax				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	par_id3149824				0	bs	INDIRECT(ref)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	par_id3154317	66			0	bs	\<emph\>ref\</emph\> represents a reference to a cell or an area (in text form) for which to return the contents.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	par_idN10CAE				0	bs	If you open an Excel spreadsheet that uses indirect addresses calculated from string functions, the sheet addresses will not be translated automatically. For example, the Excel address in INDIRECT("filename!sheetname"&B1) is not converted into the Calc address in INDIRECT("filename.sheetname"&B1).				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150389				0	bs	Example				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	par_id3150608	68			0	bs	=INDIRECT(A1) equals 100 if A1 contains C108 as a reference and cell C108 contains a value of 100.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	par_id3083286	181			0	bs	=SUM(INDIRECT("a1:" & ADDRESS(1;3))) totals the cells in the area of A1 up to the cell, whose address is defined by row 1 and column 3. Therefore, area A1:C1 is totaled.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	bm_id3154818				0	bs	\<bookmark_value\>COLUMN function\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154818				0	bs	COLUMN				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	par_id3149711				0	bs	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_SPALTE\"\>Returns the column number of a cell reference.\</ahelp\> If the reference is a cell the column number of the cell is returned; if the parameter is a cell area, the corresponding column numbers are returned in a single-row \<link href=\"text/scalc/01/04060107.xhp#wasmatrix\" name=\"array\"\>array\</link\> if the formula is entered \<link href=\"text/scalc/01/04060107.xhp#somatrixformel\" name=\"as an array formula\"\>as an array formula\</link\>. If the COLUMN function with an area reference parameter is not used for an array formula, only the column number of the first cell within the area is determined.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149283				0	bs	Syntax				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	par_id3149447				0	bs	COLUMN(reference)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	par_id3156310	74			0	bs	\<emph\>Reference\</emph\> is the reference to a cell or cell area whose first column number is to be found.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	par_id3155837				0	bs	If no reference is entered, the column number of the cell in which the formula is entered is found. \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> Calc automatically sets the reference to the current cell.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	hd_id3152932				0	bs	Example				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	par_id3147571	76			0	bs	=COLUMN(A1) equals 1. Column A is the first column in the table.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	par_id3147079	77			0	bs	=COLUMN(C3:E3) equals 3. Column C is the third column in the table.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	par_id3146861	195			0	bs	=COLUMN(D3:G10) returns 4 because column D is the fourth column in the table and the COLUMN function is not used as an array formula. (In this case, the first value of the array is always used as the result.)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	par_id3156320	196			0	bs	{=COLUMN(B2:B7)} and =COLUMN(B2:B7) both return 2 because the reference only contains column B as the second column in the table. Because single-column areas have only one column number, it does not make a difference whether or not the formula is used as an array formula.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	par_id3150872	197			0	bs	=COLUMN() returns 3 if the formula was entered in column C.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	par_id3153277	198			0	bs	{=COLUMN(Rabbit)} returns the single-row array (3, 4) if "Rabbit" is the named area (C1:D3).				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	bm_id3154643				0	bs	\<bookmark_value\>COLUMNS function\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154643				0	bs	COLUMNS				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	par_id3151182				0	bs	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_SPALTEN\"\>Returns the number of columns in the given reference.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149141				0	bs	Syntax				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	par_id3154047				0	bs	COLUMNS(array)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	par_id3154745	83			0	bs	\<emph\>array\</emph\> is the reference to a cell range whose total number of columns is to be found. The argument can also be a single cell.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153622				0	bs	Example				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	par_id3149577	200			0	bs	=Columns(B5) returns 1 because a cell only contains one column.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	par_id3145649	85			0	bs	=COLUMNS(A1:C5) equals 3. The reference comprises three columns.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	par_id3155846	201			0	bs	=COLUMNS(Rabbit) returns 2 if "Rabbit" is the named range (C1:D3).				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	bm_id3153152				0	bs	\<bookmark_value\>vertical search function\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>VLOOKUP function\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153152				0	bs	VLOOKUP				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	par_id3149984				0	bs	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_SVERWEIS\"\>Vertical search with reference to adjacent cells to the right.\</ahelp\> This function checks if a specific value is contained in the first column of an array. The function then returns the value to the same line of a specific array column named by index.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	hd_id3146898				0	bs	Syntax				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	par_id3150156				0	bs	=VLOOKUP(Search criterion;array;index;Sort order)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	par_id3149289	91			0	bs	\<emph\>Search criterion\</emph\> is the value searched for in the first column of the array.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	par_id3153884	92			0	bs	\<emph\>array\</emph\> is the reference, which is to comprise at least two columns.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	par_id3156005	93			0	bs	\<emph\>index\</emph\> is the number of the column in the array that contains the value to be returned. The first column has the number 1.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	par_id3151208	94			0	bs	\<emph\>Sort order\</emph\> is an optional parameter that indicates whether the first column in the array is sorted in ascending order. Enter the Boolean value FALSE if the first column is not sorted in ascending order. Sorted columns can be searched much faster and the function always returns a value, even if the search value was not matched exactly, if it is between the lowest and highest value of the sorted list. In unsorted lists, the search value must be matched exactly. Otherwise the function will return this message: \<emph\>Error: Value Not Available\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147487				0	bs	Example				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	par_id3154129				0	bs	You want to enter the number of a dish on the menu in cell A1, and the name of the dish is to appear as text in the neighboring cell (B1) immediately. The Number to Name assignment is contained in the D1:E100 array. D1 contains 100, E1 contains the name \<emph\>Vegetable Soup\</emph\>, and so forth, for 100 menu items. The numbers in column D are sorted in ascending order; thus, the optional \<emph\>Sort order\</emph\> parameter is not necessary.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	par_id3145663				0	bs	Enter the following formula in B1:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	par_id3151172	98			0	bs	=VLOOKUP(A1; D1:E100; 2)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	par_id3149200				0	bs	As soon as you enter a number in A1 B1 will show the corresponding text contained in the second column of reference D1:E100. Entering a nonexistent number displays the text with the next number down. To prevent this, enter FALSE as the last parameter in the formula so that an error message is generated when a nonexistent number is entered.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	bm_id3153905				0	bs	\<bookmark_value\>sheet numbers; looking up\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>SHEET function\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153905				0	bs	SHEET				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	par_id3150309				0	bs	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_TABELLE\"\>Returns the sheet number of a reference or a string representing a sheet name.\</ahelp\> If you do not enter any parameters, the result is the sheet number of the spreadsheet containing the formula.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148564				0	bs	Syntax				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	par_id3153095				0	bs	SHEET(Reference)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	par_id3154588	219			0	bs	\<emph\>Reference\</emph\> is optional and is the reference to a cell, an area, or a sheet name string.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155399				0	bs	Example				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	par_id3146988	221			0	bs	=SHEET(Sheet2.A1) returns 2 if Sheet2 is the second sheet in the spreadsheet document.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	bm_id3148829				0	bs	\<bookmark_value\>number of sheets; function\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>SHEETS function\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148829				0	bs	SHEETS				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	par_id3148820				0	bs	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_TABELLEN\"\>Determines the number of sheets in a reference.\</ahelp\> If you do not enter any parameters, it returns the number of sheets in the current document.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154220				0	bs	Syntax				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	par_id3150777				0	bs	SHEETS(Reference)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	par_id3153060	226			0	bs	\<emph\>Reference\</emph\> is the reference to a sheet or an area. This parameter is optional.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149766				0	bs	Example				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	par_id3150507	228			0	bs	=SHEETS(Sheet1.A1:Sheet3.G12) returns 3 if Sheet1, Sheet2, and Sheet3 exist in the sequence indicated.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	bm_id3158407				0	bs	\<bookmark_value\>MATCH function\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	hd_id3158407				0	bs	MATCH				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	par_id3154896				0	bs	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_VERGLEICH\"\>Returns the relative position of an item in an array that matches a specified value.\</ahelp\> The function returns the position of the value found in the lookup_array as a number.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153834				0	bs	Syntax				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	par_id3159152				0	bs	MATCH(search criterion;lookup_array;type)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	par_id3149336	105			0	bs	\<emph\>Search Criterion\</emph\> is the value which is to be searched for in the single-row or single-column array.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	par_id3159167	106			0	bs	\<emph\>lookup_array\</emph\> is the reference searched. A lookup array can be a single row or column, or part of a single row or column.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	par_id3147239	107			0	bs	\<emph\>Type\</emph\> may take the values 1, 0, or -1. If Type = 1 or if this optional parameter is missing, it is assumed that the first column of the search array is sorted in ascending order. If Type = -1 it is assumed that the column in sorted in descending order. This corresponds to the same function in Microsoft Excel.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	par_id3154265				0	bs	If Type = 0, only exact matches are found. If the search criterion is found more than once, the function returns the first one found. Only if Type = 0 can you search for regular expressions.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	par_id3147528				0	bs	If Type = 1 or the third parameter is missing, the last value that is smaller or equal to the search criterion is returned. This applies even when the search array is not sorted. For Type = -1, the first value that is larger or equal is returned.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155119				0	bs	Example				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	par_id3155343	109			0	bs	=MATCH(200; D1:D100) searches the area D1:D100, which is sorted by column D, for the value 200. As soon as this value is reached, the number of the row in which it was found is returned. If a higher value is found during the search in the column, the number of the previous row is returned.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	bm_id3158430				0	bs	\<bookmark_value\>OFFSET function\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	hd_id3158430				0	bs	OFFSET				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	par_id3149167				0	bs	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_VERSCHIEBUNG\"\>Returns the value of a cell offset by a certain number of rows and columns from a given reference point.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	hd_id3146952				0	bs	Syntax				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	par_id3159194				0	bs	OFFSET(reference;rows;columns;height;width)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	par_id3152360	115			0	bs	\<emph\>Reference\</emph\> is the cell from which the function searches for the new reference.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	par_id3156032	116			0	bs	\<emph\>Rows\</emph\> is the number of cells by which the reference was corrected up (negative value) or down.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	par_id3166458	117			0	bs	\<emph\>Columns\</emph\> is the number of columns by which the reference was corrected to the left (negative value) or to the right.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	par_id3150708	118			0	bs	\<emph\>Height\</emph\> is the optional vertical height for an area that starts at the new reference position.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	par_id3147278	119			0	bs	\<emph\>Width\</emph\> is the optional horizontal width for an area that starts at the new reference position.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155586				0	bs	Example				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	par_id3149744	121			0	bs	=OFFSET(A1; 2; 2) returns the value in cell C3 (A1 moved by two rows and two columns down). If C3 contains the value 100 this function returns the value 100.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	par_id3153739	122			0	bs	=SUM(OFFSET(A1; 2; 2; 5; 6)) determines the total of the area that starts in cell C3 and has a height of 5 rows and a width of 6 columns (area=C3:H7).				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	bm_id3159273				0	bs	\<bookmark_value\>LOOKUP function\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	hd_id3159273				0	bs	LOOKUP				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	par_id3153389				0	bs	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_VERWEIS\"\>Returns the contents of a cell either from a one-row or one-column range or from an array.\</ahelp\> Optionally, the assigned value (of the same index) is returned in a different column and row. As opposed to \<link href=\"text/scalc/01/04060109.xhp\" name=\"VLOOKUP\"\>VLOOKUP\</link\> and \<link href=\"text/scalc/01/04060109.xhp\" name=\"HLOOKUP\"\>HLOOKUP\</link\>, search and result vector may be at different positions; they do not have to be adjacent. Additionally, the search vector for the LOOKUP must be sorted, otherwise the search will not return any usable results.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	hd_id3152947				0	bs	Syntax				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	par_id3154104				0	bs	LOOKUP(Search criterion;Search vector;result_vector)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	par_id3150646	127			0	bs	\<emph\>Search criterion\</emph\> is the value to be searched for; entered either directly or as a reference.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	par_id3154854	128			0	bs	\<emph\>Search vector\</emph\> is the single-row or single-column area to be searched.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	par_id3149925	129			0	bs	\<emph\>result_vector\</emph\> is another single-row or single-column range from which the result of the function is taken. The result is the cell of the result vector with the same index as the instance found in the search vector.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148624				0	bs	Example				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	par_id3149809	131			0	bs	=LOOKUP(A1; D1:D100;F1:F100) searches the corresponding cell in range D1:D100 for the number you entered in A1. For the instance found, the index is determined, for example, the 12th cell in this range. Then, the contents of the 12th cell are returned as the value of the function (in the result vector).				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	bm_id3149425				0	bs	\<bookmark_value\>STYLE function\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149425				0	bs	STYLE				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	par_id3150826				0	bs	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_VORLAGE\"\>Applies a style to the cell containing the formula.\</ahelp\> After a set amount of time, another style can be applied. This function always returns the value 0, allowing you to add it to another function without changing the value. Together with the CURRENT function you can apply a color to a cell regardless of the value. For example: =...+STYLE(IF(CURRENT()>3;"red";"green")) applies the style "red" to the cell if the value is greater than 3, otherwise the style "green" is applied. Both cell formats have to be defined beforehand.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145373				0	bs	Syntax				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	par_id3149302				0	bs	STYLE(style;time;style2)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	par_id3150596	137			0	bs	\<emph\>Style\</emph\> is the name of a cell style assigned to the cell. Style names must be entered in quotation marks.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	par_id3156149	138			0	bs	\<emph\>Time\</emph\> is an optional time range in seconds. If this parameter is missing the style will not be changed after a certain amount of time has passed.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	par_id3149520	139			0	bs	\<emph\>Style2\</emph\> is the optional name of a cell style assigned to the cell after a certain amount of time has passed. If this parameter is missing "Standard" is assumed.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	hd_id3159254				0	bs	Example				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	par_id3151374	141			0	bs	=STYLE("Invisible";60;"Default") formats the cell in transparent format for 60 seconds after the document was recalculated or loaded, then the Default format is assigned. Both cell formats have to be defined beforehand.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	bm_id3150430				0	bs	\<bookmark_value\>CHOOSE function\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150430				0	bs	CHOOSE				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	par_id3143270				0	bs	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_WAHL\"\>Uses an index to return a value from a list of up to 30 values.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153533				0	bs	Syntax				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	par_id3155425				0	bs	CHOOSE(Index; value1;...value30)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	par_id3144755	146			0	bs	\<emph\>Index\</emph\> is a reference or number between 1 and 30 indicating which value is to be taken from the list.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	par_id3149939	147			0	bs	\<emph\>Value1...Value30\</emph\> is the list of values entered as a reference to a cell or as individual values.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	hd_id3151253				0	bs	Example				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	par_id3150625	149			0	bs	=CHOOSE(A1; B1; B2; B3; "Today"; "Yesterday"; "Tomorrow"), for example, returns the contents of cell B2 for A1 = 2; for A1 = 4, the function returns the text "Today".				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	bm_id3151001				0	bs	\<bookmark_value\>HLOOKUP function\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	hd_id3151001				0	bs	HLOOKUP				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	par_id3148688				0	bs	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_WVERWEIS\"\>Searches for a value and reference to the cells below the selected area.\</ahelp\> This function verifies if the first row of an array contains a certain value. The function returns then the value in a row of the array, named in the \<emph\>Index\</emph\>, in the same column.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154661				0	bs	Syntax				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	par_id3146070				0	bs	=HLOOKUP(search_criteria;array;Index;sorted)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	par_id3148672				0	bs	See also:\<link href=\"text/scalc/01/04060109.xhp\" name=\"VLOOKUP\"\>VLOOKUP\</link\> (columns and rows are exchanged)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	bm_id3147321				0	bs	\<bookmark_value\>ROW function\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147321				0	bs	ROW				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	par_id3154564				0	bs	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_ZEILE\"\>Returns the row number of a cell reference.\</ahelp\> If the reference is a cell, it returns the row number of the cell. If the reference is a cell range, it returns the corresponding row numbers in a one-column \<link href=\"text/scalc/01/04060107.xhp#wasmatrix\" name=\"Array\"\>Array\</link\> if the formula is entered \<link href=\"text/scalc/01/04060107.xhp#somatrixformel\" name=\"as an array formula\"\>as an array formula\</link\>. If the ROW function with a range reference is not used in an array formula, only the row number of the first range cell will be returned.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	hd_id3158439				0	bs	Syntax				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	par_id3154916				0	bs	ROW(reference)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	par_id3156336	161			0	bs	\<emph\>Reference\</emph\> is a cell, an area, or the name of an area.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	par_id3151109				0	bs	If you do not indicate a reference, the row number of the cell in which the formula is entered will be found. \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> Calc automatically sets the reference to the current cell.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155609				0	bs	Example				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	par_id3154830	205			0	bs	=ROW(B3) returns 3 because the reference refers to the third row in the table.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	par_id3147094	206			0	bs	{=ROW(D5:D8)} returns the single-column array (5, 6, 7, 8) because the reference specified contains rows 5 through 8.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	par_id3153701	207			0	bs	=ROW(D5:D8) returns 5 because the ROW function is not used as array formula and only the number of the first row of the reference is returned.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	par_id3150996	208			0	bs	{=ROW(A1:E1)} and =ROW(A1:E1) both return 1 because the reference only contains row 1 as the first column in the table. (Because single-row areas only have one row number it does not make any difference whether or not the formula is used as an array formula.)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	par_id3153671	209			0	bs	=ROW() returns 3 if the formula was entered in row 3.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	par_id3153790	210			0	bs	{=ROW(Rabbit)} returns the single-column array (1, 2, 3) if "Rabbit" is the named area (C1:D3).				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	bm_id3145772				0	bs	\<bookmark_value\>ROWS function\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145772				0	bs	ROWS				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	par_id3148971				0	bs	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_ZEILEN\"\>Returns the number of rows in a reference or array.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156051				0	bs	Syntax				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	par_id3154357				0	bs	ROWS(array)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	par_id3155942	170			0	bs	\<emph\>array\</emph\> is the reference or named area whose total number of rows is to be determined.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155869				0	bs	Example				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	par_id3154725	212			0	bs	=Rows(B5) returns 1 because a cell only contains one row.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	par_id3150102	172			0	bs	=ROWS(A10:B12) returns 3.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	par_id3155143	213			0	bs	=ROWS(Rabbit) returns 3 if "Rabbit" is the named area (C1:D3).				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	bm_id9959410				0	bs	\<bookmark_value\>HYPERLINK function\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	par_idN11798				0	bs	HYPERLINK				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	par_idN117F1				0	bs	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_HYPERLINK\"\>When you click a cell that contains the HYPERLINK function, the hyperlink opens.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	par_idN11800				0	bs	If you use the optional \<emph\>cell text\</emph\> parameter, the formula locates the URL, and then displays the text.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	par_idN11803				0	bs	To open a hyperlinked cell with the keyboard, select the cell, press F2 to enter the Edit mode, move the cursor in front of the hyperlink, press Shift+F10, and then choose \<emph\>Open Hyperlink\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	par_idN1180A				0	bs	Syntax				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	par_idN1180E				0	bs	HYPERLINK (URL) or HYPERLINK (URL;cell text)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	par_idN11811				0	bs	\<emph\>URL\</emph\> specifies the link target. The optional \<emph\>cell text\</emph\> parameter is the text that is displayed in the cell and the result of the function. If the \<emph\>cell text\</emph\> parameter is not specified, the \<emph\>URL\</emph\> is displayed in the cell text and in the result of the function.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	par_idN11823				0	bs	Example				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	par_idN11827				0	bs	=HYPERLINK("http://www.example.org") displays the text "http://www.example.org" in the cell and executes the hyperlink http://www.example.org when clicked.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	par_idN1182A				0	bs	=HYPERLINK("http://www.example.org";"Click here") displays the text "Click here" in the cell and executes the hyperlink http://www.example.org when clicked.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	par_idN1182D				0	bs	=HYPERLINK($B4) where cell B4 contains "http://www.example.org". The function adds "http://www.example.org" to the URL of the hyperlink cell and returns the same text which is used as formula result.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	par_idN11830				0	bs	=HYPERLINK("http://www.";"Click ") & "example.org" displays the text "Click example.org" in the cell and executes the hyperlink http://www.example.org when clicked.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12040100.xhp	0	help	tit				0	bs	AutoFilter				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12040100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153541				0	bs	\<link href=\"text/scalc/01/12040100.xhp\" name=\"AutoFilter\"\>AutoFilter\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12040100.xhp	0	help	par_id3148550				0	bs	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:DataFilterAutoFilter\"\>Automatically filters the selected cell range, and creates one-row list boxes where you can choose the items that you want to display.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12040100.xhp	0	help	par_id3145171				0	bs	\<link href=\"text/shared/02/12090000.xhp\" name=\"Default filter\"\>Default filter\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12050200.xhp	0	help	tit				0	bs	Options				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12050200.xhp	0	help	bm_id3154758				0	bs	\<bookmark_value\>subtotals; sorting options\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12050200.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154758				0	bs	\<link href=\"text/scalc/01/12050200.xhp\" name=\"Options\"\>Options\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12050200.xhp	0	help	par_id3154124				0	bs	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_SCPAGE_SUBT_OPTIONS\"\>Specify the settings for calculating and presenting subtotals.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12050200.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156422				0	bs	Page break between groups				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12050200.xhp	0	help	par_id3147317				0	bs	\<ahelp hid=\"SC:CHECKBOX:RID_SCPAGE_SUBT_OPTIONS:BTN_PAGEBREAK\"\>Inserts a new page after each group of subtotaled data.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12050200.xhp	0	help	hd_id3146985				0	bs	Case sensitive				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12050200.xhp	0	help	par_id3153190				0	bs	\<ahelp hid=\"SC:CHECKBOX:RID_SCPAGE_SUBT_OPTIONS:BTN_CASE\"\>Recalculates subtotals when you change the case of a data label.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12050200.xhp	0	help	hd_id3151119				0	bs	Pre-sort area according to groups				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12050200.xhp	0	help	par_id3149664				0	bs	\<ahelp hid=\"SC:CHECKBOX:RID_SCPAGE_SUBT_OPTIONS:BTN_SORT\"\>Sorts the area that you selected in the \<emph\>Group by\</emph\> box of the Group tabs according to the columns that you selected.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12050200.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153951				0	bs	Sort				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12050200.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145252				0	bs	Include formats				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12050200.xhp	0	help	par_id3147125				0	bs	\<ahelp hid=\"SC:CHECKBOX:RID_SCPAGE_SUBT_OPTIONS:BTN_FORMATS\"\>Considers formatting attributes when sorting.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12050200.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155418				0	bs	Custom sort order				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12050200.xhp	0	help	par_id3149400				0	bs	\<ahelp hid=\"SC:LISTBOX:RID_SCPAGE_SUBT_OPTIONS:LB_USERDEF\"\>Uses a custom sorting order that you defined under \<emph\>Tools - Options - %PRODUCTNAME Calc - Sort Lists\</emph\>.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12050200.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149121				0	bs	Ascending				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12050200.xhp	0	help	par_id3155068				0	bs	\<ahelp hid=\"SC:RADIOBUTTON:RID_SCPAGE_SUBT_OPTIONS:BTN_ASCENDING\"\>Sorts beginning with the lowest value, for example, from A to Z or 0 to 9.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12050200.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155443				0	bs	Descending				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12050200.xhp	0	help	par_id3153766				0	bs	\<ahelp hid=\"SC:RADIOBUTTON:RID_SCPAGE_SUBT_OPTIONS:BTN_DESCENDING\"\>Sorts beginning with the highest value, for example, from Z to A or 9 to 0.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_now.xhp	0	help	tit				0	bs	NOW				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_now.xhp	0	help	bm_id3150521				0	bs	\<bookmark_value\>NOW function\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_now.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150521				0	bs	\<variable id=\"now\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/01/func_now.xhp\"\>NOW\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_now.xhp	0	help	par_id3148829				0	bs	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_JETZT\"\>Returns the computer system date and time.\</ahelp\> The value is updated when you recalculate the document or each time a cell value is modified.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_now.xhp	0	help	hd_id3146988				0	bs	Syntax				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_now.xhp	0	help	par_id3154897				0	bs	NOW()				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_now.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154205				0	bs	Example				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_now.xhp	0	help	par_id3150774				0	bs	=NOW()-A1 returns the difference between the date in A1 and now. Format the result as a number.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\06060100.xhp	0	help	tit				0	bs	Protecting Sheet				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\06060100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153087				0	bs	Protecting Sheet				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\06060100.xhp	0	help	par_id3148664				0	bs	\<variable id=\"tabelletext\"\>\<ahelp hid=\".uno:Protect\"\>Protects the cells in the current sheet from being modified.\</ahelp\>\</variable\> Choose \<emph\>Tools - Protect Document - Sheet\</emph\> to open the \<emph\>Protect Sheet\</emph\> dialog in which you then specify sheet protection with or without a password.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\06060100.xhp	0	help	par_id3149664				0	bs	To protect cells from further editing, the \<emph\>Protected\</emph\> check box must be checked on the \<link href=\"text/scalc/01/05020600.xhp\" name=\"Format - Cells - Cell Protection\"\>\<emph\>Format - Cells - Cell Protection\</emph\>\</link\> tab page or on the \<emph\>Format Cells\</emph\> context menu.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\06060100.xhp	0	help	par_id3154490	8			0	bs	Unprotected cells or cell ranges can be set up on a protected sheet by using the \<emph\>Tools - Protect Document - Sheet\</emph\> and \<emph\>Format - Cells - Cell Protection\</emph\> menus: 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\06060100.xhp	0	help	par_id3149123				0	bs	Select the cells that will be unprotected				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\06060100.xhp	0	help	par_id3150329				0	bs	Select \<emph\>Format - Cells - Cell Protection\</emph\>. Unmark the \<emph\>Protected\</emph\> box and click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\06060100.xhp	0	help	par_id3156384				0	bs	On the \<emph\>Tools - Protect Document - Sheet\</emph\> menu, activate protection for the sheet. Effective immediately, only the cell range you selected in step 1 can be edited.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\06060100.xhp	0	help	par_id3149566	9			0	bs	To later change an unprotected area to a protected area, select the range. Next, on the \<emph\>Format - Cells - Cell Protection\</emph\> tab page, check the \<emph\>Protected\</emph\> box. Finally, choose the \<emph\>Tools - Protect Document - Sheet \</emph\>menu. The previously editable range is now protected.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\06060100.xhp	0	help	par_id3153964				0	bs	Sheet protection also affects the context menu of the sheet tabs at the bottom of the screen. The \<emph\>Delete\</emph\> and \<emph\>Move/Copy\</emph\> commands cannot be selected.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\06060100.xhp	0	help	par_id3150301				0	bs	If a sheet is protected, you will not be able to modify or delete any Cell Styles.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\06060100.xhp	0	help	par_id3154656				0	bs	A protected sheet or cell range can no longer be modified until this protection is disabled. To disable the protection, choose the \<emph\>Tools - Protect Document - Sheet\</emph\> command. If no password was set, the sheet protection is immediately disabled. If the sheet was password protected, the \<emph\>Remove Protection\</emph\> dialog opens, where you must enter the password.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\06060100.xhp	0	help	par_id3149815				0	bs	Once saved, protected sheets can only be saved again by using the \<emph\>File - Save As\</emph\> command.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\06060100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150206				0	bs	Password (optional)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\06060100.xhp	0	help	par_id3152990				0	bs	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:Protect\"\>Allows you to enter a password to protect the sheet from unauthorized changes.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\06060100.xhp	0	help	par_id3148700				0	bs	Complete protection of your work can be achieved by combining both options on the \<emph\>Tools - Protect Document\</emph\> menu, including password protection. To prohibit opening the document altogether, in the \<emph\>Save\</emph\> dialog mark the \<emph\>Save with password\</emph\> box before you click the \<emph\>Save\</emph\> button.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\06030200.xhp	0	help	tit				0	bs	Remove Precedents				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\06030200.xhp	0	help	bm_id3155628				0	bs	\<bookmark_value\>cells; removing precedents\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>formula cells;tracing precedents\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\06030200.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155628				0	bs	\<link href=\"text/scalc/01/06030200.xhp\" name=\"Remove Precedents\"\>Remove Precedents\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\06030200.xhp	0	help	par_id3149456				0	bs	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:ClearArrowPrecedents\"\>Deletes one level of the trace arrows that were inserted with the \<emph\>Trace Precedents\</emph\> command.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12080100.xhp	0	help	tit				0	bs	Hide Details				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12080100.xhp	0	help	bm_id3155628				0	bs	\<bookmark_value\>sheets; hiding details\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12080100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155628				0	bs	\<link href=\"text/scalc/01/12080100.xhp\" name=\"Hide Details\"\>Hide Details\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
