helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04020000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156023				0	bs	 Insert Cells				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04020000.xhp	0	help	par_id3150542	2			0	bs	\<variable id=\"zelleneinfuegentext\"\>\<ahelp hid=\".uno:InsertCell\"\>Opens the\<emph\> Insert Cells \</emph\>dialog, in which you can insert new cells according to the options that you specify.\</ahelp\>\</variable\> You can delete cells by choosing \<link href=\"text/scalc/01/02160000.xhp\" name=\"Edit - Delete Cells\"\>\<emph\>Edit - Delete Cells\</emph\>\</link\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04020000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153768				0	bs	Selection				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04020000.xhp	0	help	par_id3149262				0	bs	This area contains the options available for inserting cells into a sheet. The cell quantity and position is defined by selecting a cell range in the sheet beforehand.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04020000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3146120				0	bs	Shift cells down				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04020000.xhp	0	help	par_id3152596				0	bs	\<variable id=\"zellenuntentext\"\>\<ahelp hid=\"SC:RADIOBUTTON:RID_SCDLG_INSCELL:BTN_CELLSDOWN\"\>Moves the contents of the selected range downward when cells are inserted.\</ahelp\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04020000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147434				0	bs	Shift cells right				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04020000.xhp	0	help	par_id3144764				0	bs	\<variable id=\"zellenrechtstext\"\>\<ahelp hid=\"SC:RADIOBUTTON:RID_SCDLG_INSCELL:BTN_CELLSRIGHT\"\>Moves the contents of the selected range to the right when cells are inserted.\</ahelp\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04020000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153877				0	bs	Entire row				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04020000.xhp	0	help	par_id3155417				0	bs	\<variable id=\"zeilenganzetext\"\>\<ahelp hid=\"SC:RADIOBUTTON:RID_SCDLG_INSCELL:BTN_INSROWS\"\>Inserts an entire row. The position of the row is determined by the selection on the sheet.\</ahelp\>\</variable\> The number of rows inserted depends on how many rows are selected. The contents of the original rows are moved downward.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04020000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3146971				0	bs	Entire column				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04020000.xhp	0	help	par_id3155068				0	bs	\<variable id=\"spaltenganzetext\"\>\<ahelp hid=\"SC:RADIOBUTTON:RID_SCDLG_INSCELL:BTN_INSCOLS\"\>Inserts an entire column. The number of the columns to be inserted is determined by the selected number of columns.\</ahelp\>\</variable\> The contents of the original columns are shifted to right.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04070300.xhp	0	help	tit				0	bs	Creating Names				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04070300.xhp	0	help	bm_id3147264				0	bs	\<bookmark_value\>cell ranges;creating names automatically\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>names; for cell ranges\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04070300.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147264				0	bs	Creating Names				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04070300.xhp	0	help	par_id3153969				0	bs	\<variable id=\"namenuebernehmentext\"\>\<ahelp hid=\".uno:CreateNames\"\>Allows you to automatically name multiple cell ranges.\</ahelp\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04070300.xhp	0	help	par_id3156280				0	bs	Select the area containing all the ranges that you want to name. Then choose \<emph\>Insert - Names - Create\</emph\>. This opens the \<emph\>Create Names\</emph\> dialog, from which you can select the naming options that you want.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04070300.xhp	0	help	hd_id3151116				0	bs	Create names from				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04070300.xhp	0	help	par_id3152597				0	bs	Defines which part of the spreadsheet is to be used for creating the name.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04070300.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153729				0	bs	Top row				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04070300.xhp	0	help	par_id3149263				0	bs	\<ahelp hid=\"SC:CHECKBOX:RID_SCDLG_NAMES_CREATE:BTN_TOP\"\>Creates the range names from the header row of the selected range.\</ahelp\> Each column receives a separated name and cell reference.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04070300.xhp	0	help	hd_id3146984				0	bs	Left Column				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04070300.xhp	0	help	par_id3153190				0	bs	\<ahelp hid=\"SC:CHECKBOX:RID_SCDLG_NAMES_CREATE:BTN_LEFT\"\>Creates the range names from the entries in the first column of the selected sheet range.\</ahelp\> Each row receives a separated name and cell reference.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04070300.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156284				0	bs	Bottom row				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04070300.xhp	0	help	par_id3147124				0	bs	\<ahelp hid=\"SC:CHECKBOX:RID_SCDLG_NAMES_CREATE:BTN_BOTTOM\"\>Creates the range names from the entries in the last row of the selected sheet range.\</ahelp\> Each column receives a separated name and cell reference.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04070300.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154731				0	bs	Right Column				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04070300.xhp	0	help	par_id3153158				0	bs	\<ahelp hid=\"SC:CHECKBOX:RID_SCDLG_NAMES_CREATE:BTN_RIGHT\"\>Creates the range names from the entries in the last column of the selected sheet range.\</ahelp\> Each row receives a separated name and cell reference.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060000.xhp	0	help	tit				0	bs	Function Wizard				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060000.xhp	0	help	bm_id3147426				0	bs	\<bookmark_value\>inserting functions; Function Wizard\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>functions;Function Wizard\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>wizards; functions\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147426				0	bs	\<link href=\"text/scalc/01/04060000.xhp\" name=\"AutoPilot: Functions\"\>Function Wizard\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060000.xhp	0	help	par_id3145271				0	bs	\<variable id=\"funktionsautopilottext\"\>\<ahelp hid=\".uno:FunctionDialog\"\>Opens the \<emph\>Function Wizard\</emph\>, which helps you to interactively create formulas.\</ahelp\>\</variable\> Before you start the Wizard, select a cell or a range of cells from the current sheet, in order to determine the position at which the formula will be inserted.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060000.xhp	0	help	par_id3159153				0	bs	The \<emph\>Function Wizard\</emph\> has two tabs: \<emph\>Functions\</emph\> is used to create formulas, and \<emph\>Structure\</emph\> is used to check the formula build.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154490				0	bs	Functions Tab				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060000.xhp	0	help	par_id3149378				0	bs	\<link href=\"text/scalc/01/04060100.xhp\" name=\"List of Categories and Functions\"\>List of Categories and Functions\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154730				0	bs	Category				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060000.xhp	0	help	par_id3153417	37			0	bs	\<variable id=\"kategorienliste\"\>\<ahelp hid=\"SC:LISTBOX:RID_SCTAB_FUNCTION:LB_CATEGORY\"\>Lists all the categories to which the different functions are assigned. Select a category to view the appropriate functions in the list field below.\</ahelp\> Select "All" to view all functions in alphabetical order, irrespective of category. "Last Used" lists the functions you have most recently used.\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150749				0	bs	Function				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060000.xhp	0	help	par_id3155445				0	bs	\<ahelp hid=\"SC:LISTBOX:RID_SCTAB_FUNCTION:LB_FUNCTION\"\>Displays the functions found under the selected category. Double-click to select a function.\</ahelp\> A single-click displays a short function description.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3159264				0	bs	Array				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060000.xhp	0	help	par_id3149566	9			0	bs	\<ahelp hid=\"SC:CHECKBOX:RID_SCDLG_FORMULA:BTN_MATRIX\"\>Specifies that the selected function is inserted into the selected cell range as an array formula. \</ahelp\> Array formulas operate on multiple cells. Each cell in the array contains the formula, not as a copy but as a common formula shared by all matrix cells.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060000.xhp	0	help	par_id3155959				0	bs	The \<emph\>Array\</emph\> option is identical to the \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+Shift+Enter command, which is used to enter and confirm formulas in the sheet: The formula is inserted as a matrix formula indicated by two braces { }.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060000.xhp	0	help	par_id3152993				0	bs	The maximum size of an array range is 128 by 128 cells.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150367				0	bs	Arguments Input Fields				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060000.xhp	0	help	par_id3145587				0	bs	When you double-click a function, the arguments input field(s) appear on the right side of the dialog. To select a cell reference as an argument, click directly into the cell or drag the required range in the sheet while holding down the mouse button. You can also enter numerical and other values or references directly into the corresponding fields in the dialog. When using \<link href=\"text/scalc/01/04060102.xhp\" name=\"date entries\"\>date entries\</link\> make sure you use the correct format. Click OK to insert the result into the spreadsheet.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149408				0	bs	Function Result				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060000.xhp	0	help	par_id3155809				0	bs	As soon you enter arguments in the function, the result is calculated. This preview informs you if the calculation can be carried out with the arguments given. If the arguments result in an error, the corresponding \<link href=\"text/scalc/05/02140000.xhp\" name=\"error code\"\>error code\</link\> is displayed.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060000.xhp	0	help	par_id3148700				0	bs	The input entries that are required are indicated by bold argument names.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153064				0	bs	f(x) (dependent on selected function)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060000.xhp	0	help	par_id3157980				0	bs	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_SC_FAP_BTN_FX4\"\>Allows you to access a subordinate level of the \<emph\>Function Wizard\</emph\> in order to enter a nested function within the function, instead of a value or reference.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145076				0	bs	Argument/Parameter/Cell Reference (dependent on selected function)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060000.xhp	0	help	par_id3159097				0	bs	\<ahelp hid=\"SC:EDIT:RID_SCDLG_FORMULA:ED_REF\"\>The number of visible text fields depends on the function. Enter arguments either directly into the argument fields or click a cell in the table.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154957				0	bs	Result				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060000.xhp	0	help	par_id3150211				0	bs	Displays the calculation result or an error message.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3151304				0	bs	Formula				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060000.xhp	0	help	par_id3149898				0	bs	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_SC_FAP_FORMULA\"\>Displays the created formula. Type your entries directly or create the formula with assistance of the Wizard.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153249				0	bs	Back				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060000.xhp	0	help	par_id3152869				0	bs	\<ahelp hid=\"SC:PUSHBUTTON:RID_SCDLG_FORMULA:BTN_BACKWARD\"\>Moves the focus to back through the formula components, marking them as it does so.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060000.xhp	0	help	par_id3146966				0	bs	To select a single function from a complex formula consisting of several functions, double-click the function in the formula window.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155762				0	bs	Next				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060000.xhp	0	help	par_id3149316	55			0	bs	\<ahelp hid=\"SC:PUSHBUTTON:RID_SCDLG_FORMULA:BTN_FORWARD\"\>Moves forward through the formula components in the formula window.\</ahelp\> This button can also be used to assign functions to the formula. If you select a function and click the \<emph\>Next \</emph\>button, the selection appears in the formula window.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060000.xhp	0	help	par_id3159262				0	bs	Double-click a function in the selection window to transfer it to the formula window.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148745				0	bs	Cancel				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060000.xhp	0	help	par_id3147402				0	bs	Closes the dialog without implementing the formula.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150534				0	bs	OK				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060000.xhp	0	help	par_id3153029				0	bs	Ends \<emph\>Function Wizard\</emph\> and transfer the formula into the selected cell or cells.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060000.xhp	0	help	par_id3156400				0	bs	\<link href=\"text/scalc/01/04060100.xhp\" name=\"List of Categories and Functions\"\>List of Categories and Functions\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147610				0	bs	Structure tab				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060000.xhp	0	help	par_id3153122				0	bs	In this page you can view the structure of the function.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060000.xhp	0	help	par_id3149350				0	bs	If you start \<emph\>Function Wizard\</emph\> while the cell cursor is positioned in a cell that already contains a function, the \<emph\>Structure\</emph\> tab is opened and shows the composition of the current formula.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149014				0	bs	Structure				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060000.xhp	0	help	par_id3150481				0	bs	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_SC_FAP_STRUCT\"\>Displays a hierarchical representation of the current function.\</ahelp\> You can hide or show the arguments by a click on the plus or minus sign in front.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060000.xhp	0	help	par_id3148886				0	bs	Blue dots denote correctly entered arguments. Red dots indicate incorrect data types. For example: if the SUM function has one argument entered as text, this is highlighted in red as SUM only permits number entries.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_month.xhp	0	help	tit				0	bs	MONTH 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_month.xhp	0	help	bm_id3149936				0	bs	\<bookmark_value\>MONTH function\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_month.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149936				0	bs	\<variable id=\"month\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/01/func_month.xhp\"\>MONTH\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_month.xhp	0	help	par_id3153538				0	bs	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_MONAT\"\>Returns the month for the given date value.\</ahelp\> The month is returned as an integer between 1 and 12.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_month.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149517				0	bs	Syntax				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_month.xhp	0	help	par_id3145602				0	bs	MONTH(Number)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_month.xhp	0	help	par_id3149485				0	bs	\<emph\>Number\</emph\>, as a time value, is a decimal for which the month is to be returned.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_month.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153322				0	bs	Examples				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_month.xhp	0	help	par_id3149244				0	bs	MONTH(NOW()) returns the current month				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_month.xhp	0	help	par_id3154790				0	bs	MONTH(C4) returns 7 if contents of C4 = 7/7/00.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\02140500.xhp	0	help	tit				0	bs	Fill Sheet				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\02140500.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153897				0	bs	Fill Sheet				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\02140500.xhp	0	help	par_id3150791				0	bs	\<variable id=\"tabellenfuellentext\"\>\<ahelp hid=\".uno:FillTable\" visibility=\"visible\"\>Specifies the options for transferring spreadsheets or ranges of a certain spreadsheet.\</ahelp\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\02140500.xhp	0	help	par_id3150767				0	bs	In contrast to copying an area to the clipboard, you can filter certain information and calculate values. This command is only visible if you have selected two sheets in the document. To select multiple sheets, click each sheet tab while pressing \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\> \<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\> \<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\> \</switchinline\> or Shift.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\02140500.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155131				0	bs	Filling a Spreadsheet				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\02140500.xhp	0	help	par_id3146119				0	bs	Select the entire sheet by clicking the empty gray box in the upper left of the spreadsheet. You can also select an area of the sheet to be copied.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\02140500.xhp	0	help	par_id3153726				0	bs	Press \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\> \<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\> \<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\> \</switchinline\> and click the tab of the worksheet where you want to insert the contents.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\02140500.xhp	0	help	par_id3147436				0	bs	Select the command \<emph\>Edit - Fill - Sheet\</emph\>. In the dialog which appears, the check box \<emph\>Numbers\</emph\> must be selected (or \<emph\>Paste All\</emph\>) if you want to combine operations with the values. You can also choose the desired operation here.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\02140500.xhp	0	help	par_id3154942				0	bs	Click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\02140500.xhp	0	help	par_id3156283				0	bs	This dialog is similar to the \<link href=\"text/shared/01/02070000.xhp\" name=\"Paste Contents\"\>Paste Contents\</link\> dialog, where you can find additional tips.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\05020000.xhp	0	help	tit				0	bs	Format Cells				2002-02-02 02:02:02
