helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060111.xhp	0	help	par_id3147402				0	bs	WEEKS(Start date, End date, Type)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060111.xhp	0	help	par_id3151387				0	bs	Start date: First date				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060111.xhp	0	help	par_id3146324				0	bs	End date: Second date				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060111.xhp	0	help	par_id3166467				0	bs	Type: Calculates the type of difference. The possible values are 0 (interval) and 1 (in numbers of weeks).				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060111.xhp	0	help	bm_id3145237				0	bs	\<bookmark_value\>WEEKSINYEAR function\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060111.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145237				0	bs	WEEKSINYEAR				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060111.xhp	0	help	par_id3147410				0	bs	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_DAI_FUNC_WEEKSINYEAR\"\>Calculates the number of weeks in a year until a certain date.\</ahelp\> The number of weeks is defined as follows: a week that spans two years is added to the year in which most days of that week occur.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060111.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149719				0	bs	Syntax				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060111.xhp	0	help	par_id3145638				0	bs	WEEKSINYEAR(Date)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060111.xhp	0	help	par_id3149946				0	bs	Date: The date until which the weeks in the year will be calculated. The Date parameter must be a valid date according to the locale settings of %PRODUCTNAME.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060111.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150037				0	bs	Example				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060111.xhp	0	help	par_id3147614				0	bs	WEEKSINYEAR(A1) returns 53 if A1 contains 2/17/70, a valid date for the year 1970.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
