helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3155544				0	bs	\<emph\>Count 2\</emph\> is the select count from the elements.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154584				0	bs	Example:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3152904				0	bs	If you enter 2 in text boxes Count 1 and 2, 3 will be returned as the result.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	bm_id3156086				0	bs	\<bookmark_value\>TRUNC function\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156086				0	bs	TRUNC				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3157866				0	bs	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_KUERZEN\"\>Truncates a number by removing decimal places of the number according to the precision specified in \<emph\>count\</emph\>.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148499				0	bs	Syntax:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3148511				0	bs	TRUNC(number; count)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3150796				0	bs	\<emph\>Number\</emph\> is the number whose decimal places are to be cut off.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3150816				0	bs	\<emph\>Count\</emph\> is the number of places after the decimal delimiter that are not to be truncated.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3152555				0	bs	Example:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3152569				0	bs	If you enter the number 34.5678 and the count 1, 34.5 will be returned as the result.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	bm_id3153601				0	bs	\<bookmark_value\>LN function\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153601				0	bs	LN				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3154974				0	bs	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_LN\"\>Returns the natural logarithm based on the constant e of a number.\</ahelp\> The constant e has a value of approximately 2.71828182845904.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154993				0	bs	Syntax:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3155284				0	bs	LN(number)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3155297				0	bs	\<emph\>Number\</emph\> is the value whose natural logarithm is to be calculated.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153852				0	bs	Example:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3153866				0	bs	The natural logarithm to the base e of the value 3 will return the rounded value of 1.1 as the result.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	bm_id3109813				0	bs	\<bookmark_value\>LOG function\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3109813				0	bs	LOG				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3109841				0	bs	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_LOG\"\>Returns the logarithm of a number to the specified base.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3144719				0	bs	Syntax:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3144732				0	bs	LOG(number; base)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3144746				0	bs	\<emph\>Number\</emph\> is the value whose logarithm is to be calculated.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3152840				0	bs	\<emph\>Base\</emph\> is the base for the logarithm calculation.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3152860				0	bs	Example:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3154429				0	bs	The logarithm of the number 10 to the base 3 will return 2.1 as the result.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	bm_id3154187				0	bs	\<bookmark_value\>LOG10 function\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154187				0	bs	LOG10				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3155476				0	bs	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_LOG10\"\>Returns the base-10 logarithm of a number.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155494				0	bs	Syntax:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3159294				0	bs	LOG10(number)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3159308				0	bs	\<emph\>Number\</emph\> is the value whose logarithm to the base 10 is to be calculated.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3159328				0	bs	Example:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3157916				0	bs	The logarithm to the base 10 of the value 3 will return 0.48 as the result.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	bm_id3152518				0	bs	\<bookmark_value\>CEILING function\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3152518				0	bs	CEILING				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3153422				0	bs	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_OBERGRENZE\"\>Rounds a number up to the nearest multiple of Significance.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153440				0	bs	Syntax:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3153454				0	bs	CEILING(Number; Significance; Mode)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3153467				0	bs	\<emph\>Number\</emph\> is the number that is to be rounded up.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3155000				0	bs	\<emph\>Significance\</emph\> is the number to whose multiple the value is to be rounded up.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3155020				0	bs	\<emph\>Mode\</emph\> is an optional value. If the \<emph\>Mode\</emph\> value is given and not equal to zero, and if \<emph\>Number\</emph\> and \<emph\>Significance\</emph\> are negative, then rounding is done based on the absolute value of \<emph\>Number\</emph\>. This parameter is ignored when exporting to MS Excel as Excel does not know any third parameter.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3163792				0	bs	If both parameters \<emph\>Number\</emph\> and \<emph\>Significance\</emph\> are negative and the Mode value is equal to zero or is not given, the results in $[officename] and Excel will differ after the import has been completed. If you export the spreadsheet to Excel, use Mode=1 to see the same results in Excel as in Calc.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145697				0	bs	Example:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3145710				0	bs	=CEILING( -11; -2) returns -10				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3145725				0	bs	=CEILING( -11; -2; 0) returns -10				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3145740				0	bs	=CEILING( -11; -2; 1) returns -12				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	bm_id3157762				0	bs	\<bookmark_value\>PI function\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3157762				0	bs	PI				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3157790				0	bs	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_PI\"\>Returns the value of PI (rounded value 3.14159).\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3157809				0	bs	Syntax:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3157822				0	bs	PI()				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3157836				0	bs	Example:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3152370				0	bs	Pi is 3.14159... as a rounded value.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	bm_id3152418				0	bs	\<bookmark_value\>MULTINOMIAL function\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3152418				0	bs	MULTINOMIAL				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3152454				0	bs	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_AAI_FUNC_MULTINOMIAL\"\> Returns the factorial of the sum of the arguments divided by the product of the factorials of the arguments.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155646				0	bs	Syntax				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3155660				0	bs	MULTINOMIAL (Number(s))				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3155673				0	bs	Number(s): a list of up to 30 numbers.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155687				0	bs	Example				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3155701				0	bs	=MULTINOMIAL(F11:H11) returns 1260, if F11 to H11 contain the values 2, 3 and 4. This corresponds to the formula =(2+3+4)! / (2!*3!*4!)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	bm_id3155717				0	bs	\<bookmark_value\>POWER function\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155717				0	bs	POWER				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3159495				0	bs	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_POTENZ\"\>Returns the result of a number raised to a power.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3159513				0	bs	Syntax:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3159526				0	bs	POWER(base; power) or base ^ power				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3159540				0	bs	\<emph\>Base\</emph\> is the number that is to be raised to a given power.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3159580				0	bs	Example:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3159594				0	bs	If you enter 3 as the base and -2 as the power, 0.11 will be returned as the result.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	bm_id3152651				0	bs	\<bookmark_value\>SERIESSUM function\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3152651				0	bs	SERIESSUM				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3152708				0	bs	SERIESSUM(x;n;m;coefficients) = coefficient_1*x^n + coefficient_2*x^(n+m) + coefficient_3*x^(n+2m) +...+ coefficient_i*x^(n+(i-1)m)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3152724				0	bs	Syntax				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_idN11BD9				0	bs	SERIESSUM(x; n; m; coefficients)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3152737				0	bs	x: the number as an independent variable				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3144344				0	bs	n: the starting power				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3144357				0	bs	m: the increment				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3144370				0	bs	coefficients: a series of coefficients. For each coefficient the series sum is extended by one section.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	bm_id3144386				0	bs	\<bookmark_value\>PRODUCT function\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3144386				0	bs	PRODUCT				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3144414				0	bs	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_PRODUKT\"\>Multiplies all the numbers given as arguments and returns the product.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3144433				0	bs	Syntax:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3144446				0	bs	PRODUCT(number 1 to 30)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3144460				0	bs	\<emph\>Number 1 to number 30\</emph\> are up to 30 arguments whose product is to be calculated.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3144480				0	bs	Example:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3144494				0	bs	If you enter the numbers 2; 3 and 4 in the Number 1; 2 and 3 text boxes, 24 will be returned as the result.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	bm_id3160340				0	bs	\<bookmark_value\>SUMSQ function\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3160340				0	bs	SUMSQ				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3160368				0	bs	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_QUADRATESUMME\"\>If you want to calculate the sum of the squares of numbers (totaling up of the squares of the arguments), enter these into the text fields.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3160388				0	bs	Syntax:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3160402				0	bs	SUMSQ(number 1 to 30)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3160415				0	bs	\<emph\>Number 1 to number 30\</emph\> are up to 30 arguments the sum of whose squares is to be calculated.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3160436				0	bs	Example:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3160449				0	bs	If you enter the numbers 2; 3 and 4 in the \<emph\>Number 1\</emph\>; \<emph\>2\</emph\> and \<emph\>3\</emph\> text boxes, 29 is returned as the result.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	bm_id3158247				0	bs	\<bookmark_value\>MOD function\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
