helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3158121				0	bs	ROUND				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3158150				0	bs	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_RUNDEN\"\>Returns a number rounded to a certain number of decimal places.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3158169				0	bs	Syntax:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3158182				0	bs	ROUND(number; count)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3158196				0	bs	\<emph\>number\</emph\> is the number to be rounded.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145863				0	bs	Example:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3145876				0	bs	If you enter the number 17.546 in the \<emph\>number\</emph\> field, with 1 specified as the number of rounding places, 17.5 will be returned as the result.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3145899				0	bs	=ROUND(-32.4834; 3) returns -32.483. Change the cell format to see all decimals.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	bm_id3145991				0	bs	\<bookmark_value\>ROUNDDOWN function\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145991				0	bs	ROUNDDOWN				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3146020				0	bs	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_ABRUNDEN\"\>Rounds a number down, toward zero.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3146037				0	bs	Syntax:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3146051				0	bs	ROUNDDOWN(number; count)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3146064				0	bs	\<emph\>number\</emph\> is the number to be rounded down.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3163164				0	bs	Example:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3163178				0	bs	Entering the value 567.567 and the value 2 in the \<emph\>count\</emph\> field will return 567.56.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	bm_id3163268				0	bs	\<bookmark_value\>ROUNDUP function\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3163268				0	bs	ROUNDUP				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3163297				0	bs	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_AUFRUNDEN\"\>Rounds a number up, according to the specified decimal place.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3163315				0	bs	Syntax:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3163328				0	bs	ROUNDUP(number; count)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3163342				0	bs	\<emph\>number\</emph\> is the number to be rounded up.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3163381				0	bs	Example:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3144786				0	bs	Entering the value 123.343 and the value 2 in the \<emph\>count\</emph\> field will return the value 123.35.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	bm_id3144877				0	bs	\<bookmark_value\>SIN function\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3144877				0	bs	SIN				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3144906				0	bs	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_SIN\"\>Returns the sine of the given number (angle).\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3144923				0	bs	Syntax:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3144937				0	bs	SIN(number)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3144950				0	bs	\<emph\>Number\</emph\> is the angle in radians.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3144969				0	bs	Example:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3144983				0	bs	The sine of the angle (in radians) 3.14 (Pi) is 0.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	bm_id3163397				0	bs	\<bookmark_value\>SINH function\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3163397				0	bs	SINH				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3163426				0	bs	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_SINHYP\"\>Returns the hyperbolic sine of a number.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3163444				0	bs	Syntax:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3163457				0	bs	SINH(number)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3163471				0	bs	\<emph\>Number\</emph\> is the number whose hyperbolic sine is to be calculated.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3163491				0	bs	Example:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3163504				0	bs	If you enter the value -5, -74.2 will be returned as the hyperbolic sine.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	bm_id3163596				0	bs	\<bookmark_value\>SUM function\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3163596				0	bs	SUM				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3163625				0	bs	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_SUMME\"\>Adds all the numbers in a range of cells.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3163643				0	bs	Syntax:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3163656				0	bs	SUM(number1; number 2; ...; number 30)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3163671				0	bs	\<emph\>Number 1 to number 30\</emph\> are up to 30 arguments whose sum is to be calculated.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3163690				0	bs	Example:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3163704				0	bs	If you enter the numbers 2; 3 and 4 in the Number 1; 2 and 3 text boxes, 9 will be returned as the result.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3151740				0	bs	SUM(A1;A3;B5) calculates the sum of the three cells. SUM (A1:E10) calculates the sum of all cells in the A1 to E10 cell range.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3151756				0	bs	Conditions linked by AND can be used with the function SUM() in the following manner:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3151774				0	bs	Example assumption: You have entered invoices into a table. Column A contains the date value of the invoice, column B the amounts. You want to find a formula that you can use to return the total of all amounts only for a specific month, e.g. only the amount for the period >=1.1.99 to <1.2.99. The range with the date values covers A1:A40, the range containing the amounts to be totaled is B1:B40. C1 contains the start date, 1.1.99, of the invoices to be included and C2 the date, 1.2.99, that is no longer included.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3151799				0	bs	Enter the following formula as an array formula:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3151813				0	bs	=SUM((A1:A40>=C1)*(A1:A40<C2)*B1:B40)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3151828				0	bs	In order to enter this as an array formula, you must press the Shift \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command \</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>+ Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> + Enter key instead of simply pressing the Enter key to close the formula. The formula will then be shown in the \<emph\>Formula\</emph\> bar enclosed in braces.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3151869				0	bs	{=SUM((A1:A40>=C1)*(A1:A40<C2)*B1:B40)}				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3151884				0	bs	The formula is based on the fact that the result of a comparison is 1, if the criterion is met and 0 if it is not. The individual comparison results will be treated as an array and used in matrix multiplication, and at the end the individual values will be totaled to give the result matrix. The SUM() function can also be used in this way, for example, as COUNTIF() with several criteria.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	bm_id3151957				0	bs	\<bookmark_value\>SUMIF function\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3151957				0	bs	SUMIF				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3151986				0	bs	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_SUMMEWENN\"\>Adds the cells specified by a given criteria.\</ahelp\> This function is used to browse a range when you search for a certain value.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3152015				0	bs	Syntax:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3152028				0	bs	SUMIF(range; criteria; sum_range)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3152043				0	bs	\<emph\>Range\</emph\> is the range to which the criteria are to be applied.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3152062				0	bs	\<emph\>Criteria\</emph\> is the cell in which the search criterion is shown, or the search criterion itself. If the criteria is written into the formula, it has to be surrounded by double quotes.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3152083				0	bs	\<emph\>Sum_range\</emph\> is the range from which values are summed. If this parameter has not been indicated, the values found in the \<emph\>Range\</emph\> are summed.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3152110				0	bs	Example:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3152148				0	bs	To sum up only negative numbers: SUMIF(A1:A10;"<0")				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	bm_id3152195				0	bs	\<bookmark_value\>TAN function\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3152195				0	bs	TAN				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3152224				0	bs	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_TAN\"\>Returns the tangent of the given angle.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3152242				0	bs	Syntax:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3152255				0	bs	TAN(number)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3152269				0	bs	\<emph\>Number\</emph\> is the angle in radians.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3152287				0	bs	Example:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3152301				0	bs	The tangent of the angle (in radians) 3.14 (Pi) is 0.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	bm_id3165434				0	bs	\<bookmark_value\>TANH function\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3165434				0	bs	TANH				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3165462				0	bs	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_TANHYP\"\>Returns the hyperbolic tangent of a number.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3165480				0	bs	Syntax:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3165494				0	bs	TANH(number)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3165508				0	bs	\<emph\>Number\</emph\> is the number whose hyperbolic tangent is to be calculated.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3165527				0	bs	Example:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3165541				0	bs	If you enter the value -5, the system returns the hyperbolic tangent -1.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	bm_id3165633				0	bs	\<bookmark_value\>AutoFilter function; subtotals\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>sums of filtered data\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>filtered data; sums\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>SUBTOTAL function\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3165633				0	bs	SUBTOTAL				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3165682				0	bs	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_TEILERGEBNIS\"\>Calculates subtotals.\</ahelp\> If a range already contains subtotals, these are not used for further calculations. Use this function with the AutoFilters to take only the filtered records into account.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3165704				0	bs	Syntax:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3165717				0	bs	SUBTOTAL(function; range)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3165731				0	bs	\<emph\>Function\</emph\> is a number that stands for one of the following functions:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3165782				0	bs	Function index				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3165806				0	bs	Function				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3165833				0	bs	1				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3165856				0	bs	AVERAGE				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3165883				0	bs	2				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3165906				0	bs	COUNT				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3165933				0	bs	3				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3165956				0	bs	COUNTA				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3165983				0	bs	4				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3166006				0	bs	MAX				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3166033				0	bs	5				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3166056				0	bs	MIN				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3143316				0	bs	6				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3143339				0	bs	PRODUCT				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3143366				0	bs	7				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3143389				0	bs	STDEV				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3143416				0	bs	8				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3143439				0	bs	STDEVP				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3143466				0	bs	9				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3143489				0	bs	SUM				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3143516				0	bs	10				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3143539				0	bs	VAR				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3143566				0	bs	11				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3143589				0	bs	VARP				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3143606				0	bs	\<emph\>Range\</emph\> is the range whose cells are included.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3143625				0	bs	Example:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3143638				0	bs	You have a table in the cell range A1:B5 containing cities in column A and accompanying figures in column B. You have used an AutoFilter so that you only see rows containing the city Hamburg. You want to see the sum of the figures that are displayed; that is, just the subtotal for the filtered rows. In this case the correct formula would be:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3143658				0	bs	=SUBTOTAL(9; B2:B5)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	bm_id3143672				0	bs	\<bookmark_value\>Euro; converting in\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>CONVERT function\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3143672				0	bs	CONVERT				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3143708				0	bs	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_UMRECHNEN\"\>This function allows you to convert a European currency value into Euros.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3143748				0	bs	CONVERT(value;"Text"; "Text")				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3143763				0	bs	\<emph\>Value\</emph\> is the amount in the currency to be converted.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3143782				0	bs	\<emph\>Text\</emph\> is the official abbreviation for the currency in question (for example, "EUR"). The first \<emph\>Text\</emph\> parameter gives the source value to be converted, the second \<emph\>Text\</emph\> parameter gives the destination value.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3143819				0	bs	\<emph\>Example:\</emph\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3143837				0	bs	=CONVERT(100;"ATS";"EUR") converts 100 Austrian Schilling into Euro.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3143853				0	bs	=CONVERT(100;"EUR";"DEM") converts 100 Euro into German Mark.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	bm_id3157177				0	bs	\<bookmark_value\>ODD function\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3157177				0	bs	ODD				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3157205				0	bs	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_UNGERADE\"\>Rounds a positive number up to the nearest odd integer and a negative number down to the nearest odd integer.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3157223				0	bs	Syntax:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3157237				0	bs	ODD(number)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3157250				0	bs	\<emph\>Number\</emph\> is the number that is to be rounded.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3157270				0	bs	Example:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3157283				0	bs	If you enter the number 1.01, 3 will be returned as the result.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	bm_id3157404				0	bs	\<bookmark_value\>FLOOR function\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3157404				0	bs	FLOOR				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3157432				0	bs	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_UNTERGRENZE\"\>Rounds a number down to the nearest multiple of Significance.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3157451				0	bs	Syntax:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3157464				0	bs	FLOOR(Number; Significance; Mode)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3157478				0	bs	\<emph\>Number\</emph\> is the number that is to be rounded down.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3157497				0	bs	\<emph\>Significance\</emph\> is the value to whose multiple the number is to be rounded down.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3157517				0	bs	\<emph\>Mode\</emph\> is an optional value. If the \<emph\>Mode\</emph\> value is given and not equal to zero, and if \<emph\>Number\</emph\> and \<emph\>Significance\</emph\> are negative, then rounding is done based on the absolute value of the number. This parameter is ignored when exporting to MS Excel as Excel does not know any third parameter.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3163894				0	bs	If both parameters \<emph\>Number\</emph\> and \<emph\>Significance\</emph\> are negative, and if the \<emph\>Mode\</emph\> value is equal to zero or is not specified, then the results in $[officename] Calc and Excel will differ after exporting. If you export the spreadsheet to Excel, use Mode=1 to see the same results in Excel as in Calc.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3163932				0	bs	Example:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3163945				0	bs	=FLOOR( -11; -2) returns -12				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3163966				0	bs	=FLOOR( -11; -2; 0) returns -12				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3163988				0	bs	=FLOOR( -11; -2; 1) returns -10				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	bm_id3164086				0	bs	\<bookmark_value\>SIGN function\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3164086				0	bs	SIGN				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3164115				0	bs	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_VORZEICHEN\"\>Returns the sign of a number. \</ahelp\> The function returns the result 1 for a positive sign and -1 for a negative sign. If the number is zero, then the function likewise produces a zero.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3164136				0	bs	Syntax:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3164150				0	bs	SIGN(number)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3164164				0	bs	\<emph\>Number\</emph\> is the number whose sign is to be determined.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3164183				0	bs	Example:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3164197				0	bs	If you enter the number 3.4, 1 will be returned as the result.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3164212				0	bs	If you enter the number -4.5, -1 will be returned as the result.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	bm_id3164252				0	bs	\<bookmark_value\>MROUND function\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3164252				0	bs	MROUND				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3164288				0	bs	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_AAI_FUNC_MROUND\"\>The result is the nearest integer multiple of the number.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3164306				0	bs	Syntax				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3164320				0	bs	MROUND(Number; Multiple)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3164333				0	bs	Example				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3164347				0	bs	Which integer multiple of 3 is the number 15.5 closest to?				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_idN14DD6				0	bs	=MROUND(1.6;0.5) returns 1.5, the nearest integer multiple of 0.5 to approach 1.6.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	bm_id3164375				0	bs	\<bookmark_value\>SQRT function\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3164375				0	bs	SQRT				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3164404				0	bs	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_WURZEL\"\>Returns the positive square root of a number.\</ahelp\> The value of the number must be positive.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3164424				0	bs	Syntax:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3164437				0	bs	SQRT(number)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3164451				0	bs	\<emph\>Number\</emph\> is the number whose square root is to be calculated.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3164471				0	bs	Example:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3164484				0	bs	The square root of 16 is 4.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	bm_id3164560				0	bs	\<bookmark_value\>SQRTPI function\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3164560				0	bs	SQRTPI				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3164596				0	bs	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_AAI_FUNC_SQRTPI\"\>Returns the square root of a number*PI.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3164614				0	bs	Syntax				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3164627				0	bs	SQRTPI (Number)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3164641				0	bs	Example				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3164654				0	bs	=SQRTPI(2) returns the rounded value 2.506628.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	bm_id3164669				0	bs	\<bookmark_value\>random numbers; calculating\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>RANDBETWEEN function\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3164669				0	bs	RANDBETWEEN				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3164711				0	bs	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_AAI_FUNC_RANDBETWEEN\"\>Returns an integer random number between \<emph\>Bottom\</emph\> and \<emph\>Top\</emph\> (both inclusive).\</ahelp\> To recalculate press Shift+Ctrl+F9.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3164745				0	bs	Syntax				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3164758				0	bs	RANDBETWEEN (Bottom; Top)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3164772				0	bs	Example				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3164785				0	bs	=RANDBETWEEN (20;30) returns an integer of between 20 and 30.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	bm_id3164800				0	bs	\<bookmark_value\>RAND function\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3164800				0	bs	RAND				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3164829				0	bs	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_ZUFALLSZAHL\"\>Returns a random number between 0 and 1.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3164870				0	bs	Syntax:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3164884				0	bs	RAND( )				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	bm_id3164897				0	bs	\<bookmark_value\>COUNTIF function\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3164897				0	bs	COUNTIF				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3164926				0	bs	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_ZAEHLENWENN\"\>Returns the number of elements that meet with certain criteria within a cell range.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3164953				0	bs	Syntax:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3164967				0	bs	COUNTIF(range; criteria)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3164980				0	bs	\<emph\>Range\</emph\> is the range to which the criteria are to be applied.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3165000				0	bs	\<emph\>Criteria\</emph\> indicates the criteria in the form of a number, an expression or a character string. These criteria determine which cells are counted. You may also enter a search text in the form of a regular expression, e.g. "b.*" for all words that begin with b. You may also indicate a cell range that contains the search criterion. If you search for literal text, enclose the text in double quotes.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3165037				0	bs	Example:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3166505				0	bs	An example can be found under SUM().				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_today.xhp	0	help	tit				0	bs	TODAY				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_today.xhp	0	help	bm_id3145659				0	bs	\<bookmark_value\>TODAY function\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_today.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145659				0	bs	\<variable id=\"today\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/01/func_today.xhp\"\>TODAY\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_today.xhp	0	help	par_id3153759				0	bs	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_HEUTE\"\>Returns the current computer system date.\</ahelp\> The value is updated when you reopen the document or modify the values of the document.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_today.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154051				0	bs	Syntax				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_today.xhp	0	help	par_id3153154				0	bs	TODAY()				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_today.xhp	0	help	par_id3154741				0	bs	\<emph\>Today\</emph\> is a function without arguments.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_today.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153627				0	bs	Example				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_today.xhp	0	help	par_id3156106				0	bs	TODAY() returns the current computer system date.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_days360.xhp	0	help	tit				0	bs	DAYS360 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_days360.xhp	0	help	bm_id3148555				0	bs	\<bookmark_value\>DAYS360 function\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_days360.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148555				0	bs	\<variable id=\"days360\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/01/func_days360.xhp\"\>DAYS360\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_days360.xhp	0	help	par_id3156032				0	bs	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_TAGE360\"\>Returns the difference between two dates based on the 360 day year used in interest calculations.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_days360.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155347				0	bs	Syntax				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_days360.xhp	0	help	par_id3155313				0	bs	DAYS360(Date_1;Date_2;Type)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_days360.xhp	0	help	par_id3145263				0	bs	If Date_2 is earlier than Date_1, the function will return a negative number.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_days360.xhp	0	help	par_id3151064				0	bs	The optional argument \<emph\>Type\</emph\> determines the type of difference calculation. If Type = 0 or if the argument is missing, the US method (NASD, National Association of Securities Dealers) is used. If Type <> 0, the European method is used.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_days360.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148641				0	bs	Examples				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_days360.xhp	0	help	par_id3156348				0	bs	DAYS360("1/1/2000";NOW()) returns the number of interest days from January 1, 2000 until today.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_datevalue.xhp	0	help	tit				0	bs	DATEVALUE 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_datevalue.xhp	0	help	bm_id3145621				0	bs	\<bookmark_value\>DATEVALUE function\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
