helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12100000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153662				0	bs	\<link href=\"text/scalc/01/12100000.xhp\" name=\"Refresh Range\"\>Refresh Range\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12100000.xhp	0	help	par_id3153088				0	bs	\<variable id=\"aktualisieren\"\>\<ahelp hid=\".uno:DataAreaRefresh\" visibility=\"visible\"\>Updates a data range that was inserted from an external database. The data in the sheet is updated to match the data in the external database.\</ahelp\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_weeknum.xhp	0	help	tit				0	bs	WEEKNUM				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_weeknum.xhp	0	help	bm_id3159161				0	bs	\<bookmark_value\>WEEKNUM function\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_weeknum.xhp	0	help	hd_id3159161				0	bs	\<variable id=\"weeknum\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/01/func_weeknum.xhp\"\>WEEKNUM\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_weeknum.xhp	0	help	par_id3149770				0	bs	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_KALENDERWOCHE\"\>WEEKNUM calculates the week number of the year for the internal date value.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_weeknum.xhp	0	help	par_idN105E4				0	bs	The International Standard ISO 8601 has decreed that Monday shall be the first day of the week. A week that lies partly in one year and partly in another is assigned a number in the year in which most of its days lie. That means that week number 1 of any year is the week that contains the January 4\<emph\>th\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_weeknum.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153055				0	bs	Syntax				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_weeknum.xhp	0	help	par_id3147236				0	bs	WEEKNUM(number; mode)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_weeknum.xhp	0	help	par_id3147511				0	bs	\<emph\>Number\</emph\> is the internal date number.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_weeknum.xhp	0	help	par_id3154269				0	bs	\<emph\>Mode\</emph\> sets the start of the week and the calculation type.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_weeknum.xhp	0	help	par_id3148930				0	bs	1 = Sunday				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_weeknum.xhp	0	help	par_id3154280				0	bs	2 = Monday				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_weeknum.xhp	0	help	hd_id3146948				0	bs	Examples				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_weeknum.xhp	0	help	par_id3150704				0	bs	WEEKNUM("1/1/95";1) returns 1 (1/1/95 was a Sunday)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_weeknum.xhp	0	help	par_id3149792				0	bs	WEEKNUM("1/1/95";2) returns 52. If the week starts on Monday, Sunday belongs to the last week of the previous year.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04070100.xhp	0	help	tit				0	bs	Define Names				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04070100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156330				0	bs	Define Names				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04070100.xhp	0	help	par_id3154366				0	bs	\<variable id=\"namenfestlegentext\"\>\<ahelp hid=\".uno:DefineName\"\>Opens a dialog where you can specify a name for a selected area.\</ahelp\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04070100.xhp	0	help	par_id3154123	31			0	bs	Use the mouse to define ranges or type the reference into the \<emph\>Define Name \</emph\>dialog fields.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04070100.xhp	0	help	par_id3155131				0	bs	The \<emph\>Sheet Area\</emph\> box on the Formula bar contains a list of defined names for the ranges. Click a name from this box to highlight the corresponding reference on the spreadsheet. Names given formulas or parts of a formula are not listed here.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04070100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3151118				0	bs	Name				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04070100.xhp	0	help	par_id3163712				0	bs	\<ahelp hid=\"SC:COMBOBOX:RID_SCDLG_NAMES:ED_NAME\"\>Enter the name of the area for which you want to define a reference. All area names already defined in the spreadsheet are listed in the text field below.\</ahelp\> If you click a name on the list, the corresponding reference in the document will be shown with a blue frame. If multiple cell ranges belong to the same area name, they are displayed with different colored frames.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04070100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153728				0	bs	Assigned to				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04070100.xhp	0	help	par_id3147435				0	bs	\<ahelp hid=\"SC:EDIT:RID_SCDLG_NAMES:ED_ASSIGN\"\>The reference of the selected area name is shown here as an absolute value.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04070100.xhp	0	help	par_id3146986				0	bs	To insert a new area reference, place the cursor in this field and use your mouse to select the desired area in any sheet of your spreadsheet document.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
