helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12030000.xhp	0	help	par_id3155922				0	bs	\<variable id=\"sorttext\"\>\<ahelp hid=\".uno:DataSort\"\>Sorts the selected rows according to the conditions that you specify.\</ahelp\>\</variable\> $[officename] automatically recognizes and selects database ranges.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12030000.xhp	0	help	par_id3147428				0	bs	You cannot sort data if the \<link href=\"text/shared/01/02230000.xhp\" name=\"Record changes\"\>Record changes\</link\> options is enabled.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\06050000.xhp	0	help	tit				0	bs	Create Scenario				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\06050000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156023				0	bs	Create Scenario				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\06050000.xhp	0	help	par_id3150541				0	bs	\<variable id=\"szenariotext\"\>\<ahelp hid=\".uno:ScenarioManager\"\>Defines a scenario for the selected sheet area.\</ahelp\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\06050000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156280				0	bs	Name of scenario				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\06050000.xhp	0	help	par_id3151041	13			0	bs	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_SC_SCENWIN_TOP\"\>Defines the name for the scenario. Use a clear and unique name so you can easily identify the scenario.\</ahelp\> You can also modify a scenario name in the Navigator through the \<emph\>Properties \</emph\>context menu command.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\06050000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153954				0	bs	Comment				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\06050000.xhp	0	help	par_id3155411	15			0	bs	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_SC_SCENWIN_BOTTOM\"\>Specifies additional information about the scenario. This information will be displayed in the \<link href=\"text/scalc/01/02110000.xhp\" name=\"Navigator\"\>Navigator\</link\> when you click the \<emph\>Scenarios\</emph\> icon and select the desired scenario.\</ahelp\> You can also modify this information in the Navigator through the \<emph\>Properties \</emph\>context menu command.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\06050000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145273				0	bs	Settings				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\06050000.xhp	0	help	par_id3153364				0	bs	This section is used to define some of the settings used in the scenario display.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\06050000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145367				0	bs	Display border				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\06050000.xhp	0	help	par_id3151073				0	bs	\<ahelp hid=\"SC:LISTBOX:RID_SCDLG_NEWSCENARIO:LB_COLOR\"\>Highlights the scenario in your table with a border. The color for the border is specified in the field to the right of this option.\</ahelp\> The border will have a title bar displaying the name of the last scenario. The button on the right of the scenario border offers you an overview of all the scenarios in this area, if several have been defined. You can choose any of the scenarios from this list without restrictions.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\06050000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149582				0	bs	Copy back				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\06050000.xhp	0	help	par_id3154942				0	bs	\<ahelp hid=\"SC:CHECKBOX:RID_SCDLG_NEWSCENARIO:CB_TWOWAY\"\>Copies the values of cells that you change into the active scenario. If you do not select this option, the scenario is not changed when you change cell values. The behavior of the \<emph\>Copy back\</emph\> setting depends on the cell protection, the sheet protection, and the \<emph\>Prevent changes\</emph\> settings.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\06050000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149402				0	bs	Copy entire sheet				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\06050000.xhp	0	help	par_id3146969	23			0	bs	\<ahelp hid=\"SC:CHECKBOX:RID_SCDLG_NEWSCENARIO:CB_COPYALL\"\>Copies the entire sheet into an additional scenario sheet. \</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\06050000.xhp	0	help	par_idN1075A				0	bs	Prevent changes				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\06050000.xhp	0	help	par_idN1075E				0	bs	\<ahelp hid=\"sc:CheckBox:RID_SCDLG_NEWSCENARIO:CB_PROTECT\"\>Prevents changes to the active scenario. The behavior of the \<emph\>Copy back\</emph\> setting depends on the cell protection, the sheet protection, and the \<emph\>Prevent changes\</emph\> settings.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\06050000.xhp	0	help	par_idN10778				0	bs	You can only change the scenario properties if the \<emph\>Prevent changes\</emph\> option is not selected and if the sheet is not protected.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\06050000.xhp	0	help	par_idN10780				0	bs	You can only edit cell values if the \<emph\>Prevent changes\</emph\> option is selected, if the \<emph\>Copy back\</emph\> is option is not selected, and if the cells are not protected.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\06050000.xhp	0	help	par_idN1078C				0	bs	You can only change scenario cell values and write them back into the scenario if the \<emph\>Prevent changes\</emph\> option is not selected, if the \<emph\>Copy back\</emph\> option is selected, and if the cells are not protected.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12070000.xhp	0	help	tit				0	bs	Consolidate				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12070000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148946				0	bs	Consolidate				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12070000.xhp	0	help	par_id3148798				0	bs	\<variable id=\"konsolidieren\"\>\<ahelp hid=\".uno:DataConsolidate\"\>Combines data from one or more independent cell ranges and calculates a new range using the function that you specify.\</ahelp\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12070000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150010				0	bs	Function				2002-02-02 02:02:02
