helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\05110000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3146115				0	bs	Alignment				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\05110000.xhp	0	help	par_id3156445				0	bs	\<ahelp hid=\"SC:CHECKBOX:RID_SCDLG_AUTOFORMAT:BTN_ALIGNMENT\"\>When marked, specifies that you want to retain the alignment of the selected format.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\05110000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155811				0	bs	AutoFit width and height				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\05110000.xhp	0	help	par_id3148703				0	bs	\<ahelp hid=\"SC:CHECKBOX:RID_SCDLG_AUTOFORMAT:BTN_ADJUST\"\>When marked, specifies that you want to retain the width and height of the selected cells of the selected format.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\05110000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3159223				0	bs	Rename				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\05110000.xhp	0	help	par_id3153064				0	bs	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_SC_RENAME_AUTOFMT\"\>Opens a dialog where you can change the specification of the selected AutoFormat.\</ahelp\> The button is only visible if you clicked the \<emph\>More\</emph\> button.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\05110000.xhp	0	help	par_id3153912				0	bs	The \<emph\>Rename AutoFormat\</emph\> dialog opens.\<ahelp hid=\"HID_SC_REN_AFMT_NAME\"\> Enter the new name of the AutoFormat here.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\05110000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155264				0	bs	More				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\05110000.xhp	0	help	par_id3159094				0	bs	Closes the \<emph\>Formatting\</emph\> options section, if it is currently open.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060112.xhp	0	help	tit				0	bs	Add-in for Programming in $[officename] Calc				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060112.xhp	0	help	bm_id3151076				0	bs	\<bookmark_value\>programming; add-ins\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>shared libraries; programming\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>external DLL functions; programming\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>functions; shared library for $[officename] Calc\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>functions; $[officename] Calc add-in DLL\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>add-ins; for programming\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060112.xhp	0	help	hd_id3151076				0	bs	Add-in for Programming in $[officename] Calc				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060112.xhp	0	help	par_id3147001				0	bs	The method of extending Calc by Add-Ins that is described in the following is outdated. The interfaces are still valid and supported, to ensure compatibility with existing Add-Ins, but for programming new Add-Ins you should use the new \<link href=\"text/shared/guide/integratinguno.xhp\" name=\"API functions\"\>API functions\</link\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060112.xhp	0	help	par_id3150361	2			0	bs	$[officename] Calc can be expanded by Add-Ins, which are external programming modules providing additional functions for working with spreadsheets. These are listed in the \<emph\>Function Wizard\</emph\> in the \<emph\>Add-In\</emph\> category. If you would like to program an Add-In yourself, you can learn here which functions must be exported by the \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"UNIX\"\>shared library \</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>external DLL\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> so that the Add-In can be successfully attached.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060112.xhp	0	help	par_id3149211	3			0	bs	$[officename] searches the folder defined in \<emph\>Tools - Options - $[officename] - Paths - Add-ins \</emph\>for a suitable \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"UNIX\"\>shared library \</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>DLL\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>. To be recognized by $[officename], the \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"UNIX\"\>shared library \</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>DLL\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> must have certain properties, as explained in the following. This information allows you to program your own Add-In for \<emph\>Function Wizard\</emph\> of $[officename] Calc.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060112.xhp	0	help	hd_id3146981				0	bs	The Add-In Concept				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060112.xhp	0	help	par_id3156292				0	bs	Each Add-In library provides several functions. Some functions are used for administrative purposes. You can choose almost any name for your own functions. However, they must also follow certain rules regarding parameter passing. The exact naming and calling conventions vary for different platforms.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060112.xhp	0	help	hd_id3152890	6			0	bs	Functions of \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"UNIX\"\>Shared Library \</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>AddIn DLL\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060112.xhp	0	help	par_id3148837				0	bs	At a minimum, the administrative functions \<link href=\"text/scalc/01/04060112.xhp\" name=\"GetFunctionCount\"\>GetFunctionCount\</link\> and \<link href=\"text/scalc/01/04060112.xhp\" name=\"GetFunctionData\"\>GetFunctionData\</link\> must exist. Using these, the functions as well as parameter types and return values can be determined. As return values, the Double and String types are supported. As parameters, additionally the cell areas \<link href=\"text/scalc/01/04060112.xhp\" name=\"Double Array\"\>Double Array\</link\>, \<link href=\"text/scalc/01/04060112.xhp\" name=\"String Array\"\>String Array\</link\>, and \<link href=\"text/scalc/01/04060112.xhp\" name=\"Cell Array\"\>Cell Array\</link\> are supported.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060112.xhp	0	help	par_id3148604				0	bs	Parameters are passed using references. Therefore, a change of these values is basically possible. However, this is not supported in $[officename] Calc because it does not make sense within spreadsheets.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060112.xhp	0	help	par_id3150112				0	bs	Libraries can be reloaded during runtime and their contents can be analyzed by the administrative functions. For each function, information is available about count and type of parameters, internal and external function names and an administrative number.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060112.xhp	0	help	par_id3155269				0	bs	The functions are called synchronously and return their results immediately. Real time functions (asynchronous functions) are also possible; however, they are not explained in detail because of their complexity.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060112.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145077				0	bs	General information about the interface				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060112.xhp	0	help	par_id3146776				0	bs	The maximum number of parameters in an Add-In function attached to $[officename] Calc is 16: one return value and a maximum of 15 function input parameters.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060112.xhp	0	help	par_id3149899				0	bs	The data types are defined as follows:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060112.xhp	0	help	par_id3151302				0	bs	\<emph\>Data types\</emph\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060112.xhp	0	help	par_id3143222				0	bs	\<emph\>Definition\</emph\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060112.xhp	0	help	par_id3149384				0	bs	CALLTYPE				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060112.xhp	0	help	par_id3146963				0	bs	Under Windows: FAR PASCAL (_far _pascal)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060112.xhp	0	help	par_id3153809				0	bs	Other: default (operating system specific default)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060112.xhp	0	help	par_id3154734				0	bs	USHORT				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060112.xhp	0	help	par_id3155760				0	bs	2 Byte unsigned Integer				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060112.xhp	0	help	par_id3145320				0	bs	DOUBLE				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060112.xhp	0	help	par_id3150956				0	bs	8 byte platform-dependent format				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060112.xhp	0	help	par_id3146097				0	bs	Paramtype				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060112.xhp	0	help	par_id3150432				0	bs	Platform-dependent like int				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060112.xhp	0	help	par_id3153955				0	bs	PTR_DOUBLE =0 pointer to a double				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060112.xhp	0	help	par_id3159262				0	bs	PTR_STRING =1 pointer to a zero-terminated string				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060112.xhp	0	help	par_id3148747				0	bs	PTR_DOUBLE_ARR =2 pointer to a double array				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060112.xhp	0	help	par_id3147406				0	bs	PTR_STRING_ARR =3 pointer to a string array				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060112.xhp	0	help	par_id3151392				0	bs	PTR_CELL_ARR =4 pointer to a cell array				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060112.xhp	0	help	par_id3153028				0	bs	NONE =5				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060112.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156396	31			0	bs	\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"UNIX\"\>Shared Library \</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>DLL\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> functions				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060112.xhp	0	help	par_id3153019	32			0	bs	Following you will find a description of those functions, which are called at the \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"UNIX\"\>Shared Library \</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>external DLL\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060112.xhp	0	help	par_id3150038	33			0	bs	For all \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"UNIX\"\>Shared Library \</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>DLL\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> functions, the following applies:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060112.xhp	0	help	par_id3157876				0	bs	void CALLTYPE fn(out, in1, in2, ...)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060112.xhp	0	help	par_id3147616				0	bs	Output: Resulting value				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060112.xhp	0	help	par_id3159119				0	bs	Input: Any number of types (double&, char*, double*, char**, Cell area), where the \<link href=\"text/scalc/01/04060112.xhp\" name=\"Cell area\"\>Cell area\</link\> is an array of types double array, string array, or cell array.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060112.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150653				0	bs	GetFunctionCount()				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060112.xhp	0	help	par_id3152981				0	bs	Returns the number of functions without the management functions of the reference parameter. Each function has a unique number between 0 and nCount-1. This number will be needed for the \<link href=\"text/scalc/01/04060112.xhp\" name=\"GetFunctionData\"\>GetFunctionData\</link\> and \<link href=\"text/scalc/01/04060112.xhp\" name=\"GetParameterDescription\"\>GetParameterDescription\</link\> functions later.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060112.xhp	0	help	par_id3150742				0	bs	\<emph\>Syntax\</emph\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060112.xhp	0	help	par_id3148728				0	bs	void CALLTYPE GetFunctionCount(USHORT& nCount)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060112.xhp	0	help	par_id3154677				0	bs	\<emph\>Parameter\</emph\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060112.xhp	0	help	par_id3146940				0	bs	USHORT &nCount:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060112.xhp	0	help	par_id3149893				0	bs	Output: Reference to a variable, which is supposed to contain the number of Add-In functions. For example: If the Add-In provides 5 functions for $[officename] Calc, then nCount=5.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060112.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147476				0	bs	GetFunctionData()				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060112.xhp	0	help	par_id3154841				0	bs	Determines all the important information about an Add-In function.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060112.xhp	0	help	par_id3148888				0	bs	\<emph\>Syntax\</emph\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060112.xhp	0	help	par_id3148434				0	bs	void CALLTYPE GetFunctionData(USHORT& nNo, char* pFuncName, USHORT& nParamCount, Paramtype* peType, char* pInternalName)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060112.xhp	0	help	par_id3149253				0	bs	\<emph\>Parameter\</emph\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060112.xhp	0	help	par_id3149686				0	bs	USHORT& nNo:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060112.xhp	0	help	par_id3149949				0	bs	Input: Function number between 0 and nCount-1, inclusively.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060112.xhp	0	help	par_id3149546				0	bs	char* pFuncName:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060112.xhp	0	help	par_id3148579	52			0	bs	Output: Function name as seen by the programmer, as it is named in the \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"UNIX\"\>Shared Library \</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>DLL\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>. This name does not determine the name used in the \<emph\>Function Wizard\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060112.xhp	0	help	par_id3153935				0	bs	USHORT& nParamCount:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060112.xhp	0	help	par_id3150142				0	bs	Output: Number of parameters in AddIn function. This number must be greater than 0, because there is always a result value; the maximum value is 16.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060112.xhp	0	help	par_id3145143				0	bs	Paramtype* peType:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060112.xhp	0	help	par_id3148750				0	bs	Output: Pointer to an array of exactly 16 variables of type Paramtype. The first nParamCount entries are filled with the suitable type of parameter.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060112.xhp	0	help	par_id3153078				0	bs	char* pInternalName:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060112.xhp	0	help	par_id3155261				0	bs	Output: Function name as seen by the user, as it appears in the \<emph\>Function Wizard\</emph\>. May contain umlauts.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060112.xhp	0	help	par_id3153327				0	bs	The pFuncName and pInternalName parameters are char arrays, which are implemented with size 256 in $[officename] Calc.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060112.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148567				0	bs	GetParameterDescription()				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060112.xhp	0	help	par_id3153000				0	bs	Provides a brief description of the Add-In function and its parameters. As an option, this function can be used to show a function and parameter description in the \<emph\>Function Wizard\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060112.xhp	0	help	par_id3154501				0	bs	\<emph\>Syntax\</emph\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060112.xhp	0	help	par_id3153564				0	bs	void CALLTYPE GetParameterDescription(USHORT& nNo, USHORT& nParam, char* pName, char* pDesc)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060112.xhp	0	help	par_id3157995				0	bs	\<emph\>Parameter\</emph\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060112.xhp	0	help	par_id3155925				0	bs	USHORT& nNo:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060112.xhp	0	help	par_id3149883				0	bs	Input: Number of the function in the library; between 0 and nCount-1.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060112.xhp	0	help	par_id3154326				0	bs	USHORT& nParam:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060112.xhp	0	help	par_id3159139				0	bs	Input: Indicates, for which parameter the description is provided; parameters start at 1. If nParam is 0, the description itself is supposed to be provided in pDesc; in this case, pName does not have any meaning.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060112.xhp	0	help	par_id3147374				0	bs	char* pName:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060112.xhp	0	help	par_id3145245				0	bs	Output: Takes up the parameter name or type, for example, the word "Number" or "String" or "Date", and so on. Implemented in $[officename] Calc as char[256].				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060112.xhp	0	help	par_id3151020				0	bs	char* pDesc:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060112.xhp	0	help	par_id3148389				0	bs	Output: Takes up the description of the parameter, for example, "Value, at which the universe is to be calculated." Implemented in $[officename] Calc as char[256].				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060112.xhp	0	help	par_id3145303				0	bs	pName and pDesc are char arrays; implemented in $[officename] Calc with size 256. Please note that the space available in the \<emph\>Function Wizard\</emph\> is limited and that the 256 characters cannot be fully used.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060112.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148874				0	bs	Cell areas				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060112.xhp	0	help	par_id3150265				0	bs	The following tables contain information about which data structures must be provided by an external program module in order to pass cell areas. $[officename] Calc distinguishes between three different arrays, depending on the data type.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060112.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156060				0	bs	Double Array				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060112.xhp	0	help	par_id3149540				0	bs	As a parameter, a cell area with values of the Number/Double type can be passed. A double array in $[officename] Calc is defined as follows:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060112.xhp	0	help	par_id3149388				0	bs	\<emph\>Offset\</emph\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060112.xhp	0	help	par_id3154636				0	bs	\<emph\>Name\</emph\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060112.xhp	0	help	par_id3153228				0	bs	\<emph\>Description\</emph\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060112.xhp	0	help	par_id3150685				0	bs	0				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060112.xhp	0	help	par_id3154869				0	bs	Col1				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060112.xhp	0	help	par_id3147541				0	bs	Column number in the upper-left corner of the cell area. Numbering starts at 0.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060112.xhp	0	help	par_id3149783				0	bs	2				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060112.xhp	0	help	par_id3155986				0	bs	Row1				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060112.xhp	0	help	par_id3147483				0	bs	Row number in the upper-left corner of the cell area; numbering starts at 0.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060112.xhp	0	help	par_id3153721				0	bs	4				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060112.xhp	0	help	par_id3154317				0	bs	Tab1				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060112.xhp	0	help	par_id3149820				0	bs	Table number in the upper-left corner of the cell area; numbering starts at 0.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060112.xhp	0	help	par_id3163820				0	bs	6				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060112.xhp	0	help	par_id3149710				0	bs	Col2				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060112.xhp	0	help	par_id3154819				0	bs	Column number in the lower-right corner of the cell area. Numbering starts at 0.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060112.xhp	0	help	par_id3145083				0	bs	8				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060112.xhp	0	help	par_id3156310				0	bs	Row2				2002-02-02 02:02:02
