helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\rename_table.xhp	0	help	tit				0	bs	Renaming Sheets				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\rename_table.xhp	0	help	bm_id3150398				0	bs	\<bookmark_value\>renaming sheets\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>sheet tabs;renaming\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>tables;renaming\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>sheets; changing names\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>names; sheets\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\rename_table.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150398				0	bs	\<variable id=\"rename_table\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/rename_table.xhp\" name=\"Renaming Sheets\"\>Renaming Sheets\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\rename_table.xhp	0	help	par_id3155131				0	bs	Click the name of the sheet that you want to change.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\rename_table.xhp	0	help	par_id3149260				0	bs	Enter a new name for the sheet and click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\rename_table.xhp	0	help	par_id3149667				0	bs	Alternatively, hold down the \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Option key \</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Alt-key\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> and click on any sheet name and enter the new name directly.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\rename_table.xhp	0	help	par_id3155444				0	bs	The name of a sheet is independent of the name of the spreadsheet. You enter the spreadsheet name when you save it for the first time as a file. The document can contain up to 256 individual sheets, which can have different names.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\table_rotate.xhp	0	help	tit				0	bs	Rotating Tables (Transposing)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\table_rotate.xhp	0	help	bm_id3154346				0	bs	\<bookmark_value\>tables; transposing\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>transposing tables\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>inverting tables\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>swapping tables\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>columns; swap with rows\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>rows; swapping with columns\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>tables; rotating\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>rotating; tables\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\table_rotate.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154346				0	bs	\<variable id=\"table_rotate\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/table_rotate.xhp\" name=\"Rotating Tables (Transposing)\"\>Rotating Tables (Transposing)\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\table_rotate.xhp	0	help	par_id3154013				0	bs	In $[officename] Calc, there is a way to "rotate" a spreadsheet so that rows become columns and columns become rows.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\table_rotate.xhp	0	help	par_id3153142				0	bs	Select the cell range that you want to transpose.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\table_rotate.xhp	0	help	par_id3153191				0	bs	Choose \<emph\>Edit - Cut\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\table_rotate.xhp	0	help	par_id3148575				0	bs	Click the cell that is to be the top left cell in the result.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\table_rotate.xhp	0	help	par_id3156286				0	bs	Choose \<emph\>Edit - Paste Special\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\table_rotate.xhp	0	help	par_id3144764				0	bs	In the dialog, mark \<emph\>Paste all\</emph\> and \<emph\>Transpose\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\table_rotate.xhp	0	help	par_id3155600				0	bs	If you now click OK the columns and rows are transposed.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\table_rotate.xhp	0	help	par_id3146969				0	bs	\<link href=\"text/shared/01/02070000.xhp\" name=\"Paste Special\"\>Paste Special\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\dbase_files.xhp	0	help	tit				0	bs	Importing and Exporting dBase Files				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\dbase_files.xhp	0	help	bm_id1226844				0	bs	\<bookmark_value\>exporting;spreadsheets to dBase\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>importing;dBase files\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>dBase;importing and exporting files\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>spreadsheets; importing dBase files\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>spreadsheets; exporting to dBase files\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>database tables;importing dBase files\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\dbase_files.xhp	0	help	par_idN10738				0	bs	\<variable id=\"dbase_files\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/dbase_files.xhp\"\>Importing and Exporting dBase Files\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\dbase_files.xhp	0	help	par_idN10756				0	bs	You can open and save data in the dBase file format (*.dbf file extension) in $[officename] Base or a spreadsheet. A dBase database is directory that contains a collection of files with the .dbf file extension. Each file corresponds to a table in the database. Formulas and formatting are lost when you open and save a dBase file from %PRODUCTNAME.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\dbase_files.xhp	0	help	par_idN10759				0	bs	To Import a dBase File Into a Spreadsheet				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\dbase_files.xhp	0	help	par_idN10760				0	bs	Choose \<emph\>File - Open\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\dbase_files.xhp	0	help	par_idN1071F				0	bs	Locate the *.dbf file that you want to import. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\dbase_files.xhp	0	help	par_idN10768				0	bs	Click \<emph\>Open\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\dbase_files.xhp	0	help	par_idN10730				0	bs	The \<emph\>Import dBase files\</emph\> dialog opens.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\dbase_files.xhp	0	help	par_idN10774				0	bs	Click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\dbase_files.xhp	0	help	par_idN10777				0	bs	The dBase file opens as a new Calc spreadsheet.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\dbase_files.xhp	0	help	par_idN1074E				0	bs	If you want to save the spreadsheet as a dBase file, do not alter or delete the first row in the imported file. This row contains information that is required by a dBase database.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\dbase_files.xhp	0	help	par_idN1077A				0	bs	To Import a dBase File Into a Database Table				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\dbase_files.xhp	0	help	par_idN1076C				0	bs	A %PRODUCTNAME Base database table is actually a link to an existing database.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\dbase_files.xhp	0	help	par_idN10796				0	bs	Choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>File - New - Database\</item\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\dbase_files.xhp	0	help	par_idN10786				0	bs	In the \<emph\>File name\</emph\> box of the \<emph\>Save As\</emph\> dialog, enter a name for the database.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\dbase_files.xhp	0	help	par_idN10792				0	bs	Click \<emph\>Save\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\dbase_files.xhp	0	help	par_idN1079A				0	bs	In the \<emph\>Database type \</emph\>box of the \<emph\>Database Properties\</emph\> dialog, select "dBASE".				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\dbase_files.xhp	0	help	par_idN107A6				0	bs	Click \<emph\>Next\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\dbase_files.xhp	0	help	par_idN107AE				0	bs	Click \<emph\>Browse\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\dbase_files.xhp	0	help	par_idN107B6				0	bs	Locate the directory that contains the dBase file, and click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\dbase_files.xhp	0	help	par_idN107BE				0	bs	Click \<emph\>Create\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\dbase_files.xhp	0	help	par_idN107F1				0	bs	To Export a Spreadsheet to a dBase File				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\dbase_files.xhp	0	help	par_idN107F8				0	bs	Choose \<emph\>File - Export\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\dbase_files.xhp	0	help	par_idN10800				0	bs	In the \<emph\>File format\</emph\> box, select "dBase file".				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\dbase_files.xhp	0	help	par_idN107F9				0	bs	In the \<emph\>File name\</emph\> box, type a name for the dBase file.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\dbase_files.xhp	0	help	par_idN10801				0	bs	Click \<emph\>Export\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\dbase_files.xhp	0	help	par_idN10808				0	bs	Only the data on the current sheet is exported.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\mark_cells.xhp	0	help	tit				0	bs	Selecting Multiple Cells				2002-02-02 02:02:02
