helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\text_wrap.xhp	0	help	tit				0	bs	Writing Multi-line Text				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\text_wrap.xhp	0	help	bm_id3154346				0	bs	\<bookmark_value\>text in cells; multi-line\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>cells; text breaks\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>breaks; in cells\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>multi-line text in cells\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\text_wrap.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154346				0	bs	\<variable id=\"text_wrap\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/text_wrap.xhp\" name=\"Writing Multi-line Text\"\>Writing Multi-line Text\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\text_wrap.xhp	0	help	par_id3156280				0	bs	Pressing the \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command \</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+Enter keys inserts a manual line break. This shortcut only works directly in the cell, not in the input line.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\text_wrap.xhp	0	help	par_id3153142				0	bs	If you want the text to automatically break at the right border of the cell, proceed as follows:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\text_wrap.xhp	0	help	par_id3153951				0	bs	Select all the cells where you want the text to break at the right border.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\text_wrap.xhp	0	help	par_id3148575				0	bs	In \<emph\>Format - Cells - Alignment\</emph\>, mark the \<emph\>Automatic line break\</emph\> option and click OK.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\text_wrap.xhp	0	help	par_id3145799				0	bs	\<link href=\"text/scalc/01/05020000.xhp\" name=\"Format - Cell\"\>Format - Cell\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot_createtable.xhp	0	help	par_id3156023				0	bs	Position the cursor within a range of cells containing values, row and column headings.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot_createtable.xhp	0	help	par_id3150868				0	bs	Drag the desired buttons into one of the four areas.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot_createtable.xhp	0	help	par_id3154011				0	bs	If the button is dropped in the \<emph\>Data Fields\</emph\> area it will be given a caption that also shows the formula that will be used to calculate the data.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot_createtable.xhp	0	help	par_id3146974				0	bs	By double-clicking on one of the fields in the \<emph\>Data Fields\</emph\> area you can call up the \<link href=\"text/scalc/01/12090105.xhp\" name=\"Data Field\"\>\<emph\>Data Field\</emph\>\</link\> dialog.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot_createtable.xhp	0	help	par_id3150329				0	bs	The order of the buttons can be changed at any time by moving them to a different position in the area with the mouse.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot_createtable.xhp	0	help	par_id3153714				0	bs	Remove a button by dragging it back to the area of the other buttons at the right of the dialog.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot_createtable.xhp	0	help	par_id3147338				0	bs	To open the \<link href=\"text/scalc/01/12090105.xhp\" name=\"Data Field\"\>\<emph\>Data Field\</emph\>\</link\> dialog, double-click one of the buttons in the \<emph\>Row\</emph\> or \<emph\>Column\</emph\> area. Use the dialog to select if and to what extent \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> calculates display subtotals.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellreferences.xhp	0	help	tit				0	bs	Referencing a Cell in Another Document				2002-02-02 02:02:02
