helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellcopy.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150440				0	bs	\<variable id=\"cellcopy\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/cellcopy.xhp\" name=\"Only Copy Visible Cells\"\>Only Copy Visible Cells\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellcopy.xhp	0	help	par_id3148577				0	bs	Assume you have hidden a few rows in a cell range. Now you want to copy, delete, or format only the remaining visible rows.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellcopy.xhp	0	help	par_id3154729				0	bs	$[officename] behavior depends on how the cells were made invisible, by a filter or manually.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellcopy.xhp	0	help	par_id3155603				0	bs	Method and Action				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellcopy.xhp	0	help	par_id3150751				0	bs	Result				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellcopy.xhp	0	help	par_id3149018				0	bs	Cells were filtered by AutoFilters, standard filters or advanced filters.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellcopy.xhp	0	help	par_id3150044				0	bs	Copy, delete, move, or format a selection of currently visible cells.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellcopy.xhp	0	help	par_id3146918				0	bs	Only the visible cells of the selection are copied, deleted, moved, or formatted.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellcopy.xhp	0	help	par_id3166427				0	bs	Cells were hidden using the \<emph\>Hide\</emph\> command in the context menu of the row or column headers, or through an \<link href=\"text/scalc/01/12080000.xhp\" name=\"outline\"\>outline\</link\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellcopy.xhp	0	help	par_id3152990				0	bs	Copy, delete, move, or format a selection of currently visible cells.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellcopy.xhp	0	help	par_id3154371				0	bs	All cells of the selection, including the hidden cells, are copied, deleted, moved, or formatted.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\print_landscape.xhp	0	help	tit				0	bs	Printing Sheets in Landscape Format				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\print_landscape.xhp	0	help	bm_id3153418				0	bs	\<bookmark_value\>printing; sheet selection\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>sheets; printing in landscape\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>printing; landscape\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>landscape printing\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\print_landscape.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153418				0	bs	\<variable id=\"print_landscape\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/print_landscape.xhp\" name=\"Printing Sheets in Landscape Format\"\>Printing Sheets in Landscape Format\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\print_landscape.xhp	0	help	par_id3149257				0	bs	In order to print a sheet you have a number of interactive options available under \<emph\>View - Page Break Preview\</emph\>. Drag the delimiter lines to define the range of printed cells on each page.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\print_landscape.xhp	0	help	par_id3153963				0	bs	To print in landscape format, proceed as follows:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\print_landscape.xhp	0	help	par_id3154020				0	bs	Go to the sheet to be printed.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\print_landscape.xhp	0	help	par_id3150786				0	bs	Choose \<emph\>Format - Page\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\print_landscape.xhp	0	help	par_id3150089	5			0	bs	The command is not visible if the sheet has been opened with write protection on. In that case, click the \<emph\>Edit File \</emph\>icon on the \<emph\>Standard\</emph\> bar.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\print_landscape.xhp	0	help	par_id3166430				0	bs	Select the \<emph\>Page\</emph\> tab. Select the \<emph\>Landscape\</emph\> paper format and click OK.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\print_landscape.xhp	0	help	par_id3150885				0	bs	Choose \<emph\>File - Print\</emph\>. You will see the \<emph\>Print\</emph\> dialog.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\print_landscape.xhp	0	help	par_id3156288				0	bs	Depending on the printer driver and the operating system, it may be necessary to click the \<emph\>Properties\</emph\> button and to change your printer to landscape format there.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\print_landscape.xhp	0	help	par_id3149404	9			0	bs	In the \<emph\>Print \</emph\>dialog under \<emph\>Print range\</emph\>, select the pages to be printed:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\print_landscape.xhp	0	help	par_id3153305	10			0	bs	\<emph\>All\</emph\> - All sheets will be printed.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\print_landscape.xhp	0	help	par_id3148699	11			0	bs	\<emph\>Pages\</emph\> - Enter the pages to be printed. The pages will also be numbered from the first sheet onwards. If you see in the Page Break Preview that Sheet1 will be printed on 4 pages and you want to print the first two pages of Sheet2, enter 5-6 here.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\print_landscape.xhp	0	help	par_id3145076				0	bs	If under \<emph\>Format - Print ranges\</emph\> you have defined one or more print ranges, only the contents of these print ranges will be printed.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\print_landscape.xhp	0	help	par_id3156019				0	bs	\<link href=\"text/scalc/01/03100000.xhp\" name=\"View - Page Break Preview\"\>View - Page Break Preview\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
