helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\03091100.xhp	0	help	par_id3147129				0	bs	The following examples, however, do not look identical:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\03091100.xhp	0	help	par_id3147073				0	bs	x^{a_{size 8 n}}				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\03091100.xhp	0	help	par_id3147086				0	bs	x^{a_{size +2 n}}				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\03091100.xhp	0	help	par_id3154386				0	bs	x^{a_{size *1.333 n}}				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\03091100.xhp	0	help	par_id3153354				0	bs	Note that all n here have different sizes. The size 1.333 results from 8/6, the desired size divided by the default index size 6. (Index size 50% with a base size of 12)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
