helpcontent2	source\text\smath\guide\newline.xhp	0	help	hd_id3146970				0	bs	\<variable id=\"newline\"\>\<link href=\"text/smath/guide/newline.xhp\" name=\"Entering Line Breaks\"\>Entering Line Breaks\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\guide\newline.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147339				0	bs	How to write formulas in $[officename] Math over two lines (with manual line break):				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\guide\newline.xhp	0	help	par_id3154702				0	bs	Create a line break by using the "newline" command. Everything coming after the line break is placed on the next line.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\guide\comment.xhp	0	help	tit				0	bs	Entering Comments				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\guide\comment.xhp	0	help	bm_id3155961				0	bs	\<bookmark_value\>comments; entering in $[officename] Math\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>inserting;comments in $[officename] Math\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\guide\comment.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155961				0	bs	\<variable id=\"comment\"\>\<link href=\"text/smath/guide/comment.xhp\" name=\"Entering Comments\"\>Entering Comments\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\guide\comment.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154657				0	bs	How does one attach comments that don't appear in the document to a formula?				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\guide\comment.xhp	0	help	par_id3149499				0	bs	A comment begins with a double percent sign \<emph\>%%\</emph\>, and extends to the next line-end character (Enter key). Everything that lies in between is ignored and is not printed out. If there are percent signs in the text, they are treated as part of the text.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\guide\comment.xhp	0	help	par_idN105D0				0	bs	Example:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\guide\comment.xhp	0	help	par_idN105D3				0	bs	a^2+b^2=c^2 %% Pythagorean theorem.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03010201.xhp	0	help	tit				0	bs	InputBox Function [Runtime]				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03010201.xhp	0	help	bm_id3148932				0	bs	\<bookmark_value\>InputBox function\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03010201.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148932				0	bs	\<link href=\"text/sbasic/shared/03010201.xhp\" name=\"InputBox Function [Runtime]\"\>InputBox Function [Runtime]\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03010201.xhp	0	help	par_id3151262				0	bs	Displays a prompt in a dialog at which the user can input text. The input is assigned to a variable.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03010201.xhp	0	help	par_id3151100				0	bs	The \<emph\>InputBox\</emph\> statement is a convenient method of entering text through a dialog. Confirm the input by clicking OK or pressing Return. The input is returned as the function return value. If you close the dialog with Cancel, \<emph\>InputBox\</emph\> returns a zero-length string ("").				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03010201.xhp	0	help	hd_id3152347				0	bs	Syntax:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03010201.xhp	0	help	par_id3159201	5			0	bs	InputBox (Msg As String[, Title As String[, Default As String[, x_pos As Integer, y_pos As Integer]]]]) 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03010201.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150713				0	bs	Return value:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
