helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03132500.xhp	0	help	par_idN10580				0	bs	\<link href=\"text/sbasic/shared/03132500.xhp\"\>GetDefaultContext Function [Runtime]\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03132500.xhp	0	help	par_idN10590				0	bs	Returns the default context of the process service factory, if existent, else returns a null reference. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03132500.xhp	0	help	par_idN10593				0	bs	This runtime function returns the default component context to be used, if instantiating services via XmultiServiceFactory. See the \<item type=\"literal\"\>Professional UNO\</item\> chapter in the \<item type=\"literal\"\>Developer's Guide\</item\> on \<link href=\"http://api.openoffice.org\"\>api.openoffice.org\</link\> for more information.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03100100.xhp	0	help	tit				0	bs	CBool Function [Runtime]				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03100100.xhp	0	help	bm_id3150616				0	bs	\<bookmark_value\>CBool function\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03100100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150616				0	bs	\<link href=\"text/sbasic/shared/03100100.xhp\" name=\"CBool Function [Runtime]\"\>CBool Function [Runtime]\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03100100.xhp	0	help	par_id3145136				0	bs	Converts a string comparison or numeric comparison to a Boolean expression, or converts a single numeric expression to a Boolean expression.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03100100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153345				0	bs	Syntax:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03100100.xhp	0	help	par_id3149514				0	bs	CBool (Expression1 {= | <> | < | > | <= | >=} Expression2) or CBool (Number)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03100100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156152				0	bs	Return value:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03100100.xhp	0	help	par_id3155419				0	bs	Bool				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03100100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147530				0	bs	Parameters:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03100100.xhp	0	help	par_id3156344				0	bs	\<emph\>Expression1, Expression2:\</emph\> Any string or numeric expressions that you want to compare. If the expressions match, the \<emph\>CBool\</emph\> function returns \<emph\>True\</emph\>, otherwise \<emph\>False\</emph\> is returned.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03100100.xhp	0	help	par_id3149655				0	bs	\<emph\>Number:\</emph\> Any numeric expression that you want to convert. If the expression equals 0, \<emph\>False\</emph\> is returned, otherwise \<emph\>True\</emph\> is returned.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03100100.xhp	0	help	par_id3145171				0	bs	The following example uses the \<emph\>CBool\</emph\> function to evaluate the value that is returned by the \<emph\>Instr\</emph\> function. The function checks if the word "and" is found in the sentence that was entered by the user.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03100100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156212				0	bs	Example:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03100100.xhp	0	help	par_id3147288				0	bs	Sub ExampleCBool				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03100100.xhp	0	help	par_id3153768				0	bs	Dim sText As String				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03100100.xhp	0	help	par_id3155132				0	bs	sText = InputBox("Please enter a short sentence:")				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03100100.xhp	0	help	par_id3155855				0	bs	REM Proof if the word »and« appears in the sentence.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03100100.xhp	0	help	par_id3146984				0	bs	REM Instead of the command line				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03100100.xhp	0	help	par_id3148576				0	bs	REM If Instr(Input, "and")<>0 Then...				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03100100.xhp	0	help	par_id3154014				0	bs	REM the CBool function is applied as follows:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03100100.xhp	0	help	par_id3155413				0	bs	If CBool(Instr(sText, "and")) Then				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03100100.xhp	0	help	par_id3152940				0	bs	MsgBox "The word »and« appears in the sentence you entered!"				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03100100.xhp	0	help	par_id3153954				0	bs	EndIf				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03100100.xhp	0	help	par_id3152886				0	bs	End Sub				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\01020500.xhp	0	help	tit				0	bs	Libraries, Modules and Dialogs				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\01020500.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147317				0	bs	\<link href=\"text/sbasic/shared/01020500.xhp\" name=\"Libraries, Modules and Dialogs\"\>Libraries, Modules and Dialogs\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\01020500.xhp	0	help	par_id3147427				0	bs	The following describes the basic use of libraries, modules and dialogs in $[officename] Basic.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\01020500.xhp	0	help	par_id3146120				0	bs	$[officename] Basic provides tools to help you structuring your projects. It supports various "units" which enable you to group individual SUBS and FUNCTIONS in a Basic project.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\01020500.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148575				0	bs	Libraries				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\01020500.xhp	0	help	par_id3150011				0	bs	Libraries serve as a tool for organizing modules, and can either be attached to a document or a template. When the document or a template is saved, all modules contained in the library are automatically saved as well.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\01020500.xhp	0	help	par_id3151112				0	bs	A library can contain up to 16,000 modules.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\01020500.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149262				0	bs	Modules				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\01020500.xhp	0	help	par_id3156441				0	bs	A module contains SUBS and FUNCTIONS along with variable declarations. The length of the program that can be saved in a module is limited to 64 KB. If more space is required you can divide a $[officename] Basic project among several modules, and then save them in a single library.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\01020500.xhp	0	help	hd_id3152577				0	bs	Dialog Modules				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\01020500.xhp	0	help	par_id3149377				0	bs	Dialog modules contain dialog definitions, including the dialog box properties, the properties of each dialog element and the events assigned. Since a dialog module can only contain a single dialog, they are often referred to as "dialogs".				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03030302.xhp	0	help	tit				0	bs	Time Statement [Runtime]				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03030302.xhp	0	help	bm_id3145090				0	bs	\<bookmark_value\>Time statement\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03030302.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145090				0	bs	\<link href=\"text/sbasic/shared/03030302.xhp\"\>Time Statement [Runtime]\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03030302.xhp	0	help	par_id3150984				0	bs	This function returns the current system time as a string in the format "HH:MM:SS".				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03030302.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154346				0	bs	Syntax:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03030302.xhp	0	help	par_id3149670				0	bs	Time				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03030302.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150792				0	bs	Parameters:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03030302.xhp	0	help	par_id3149656				0	bs	\<emph\>Text:\</emph\> Any string expression that specifies the new time in the format "HH:MM:SS".				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03030302.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145173				0	bs	Example:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
