helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03030302.xhp	0	help	par_id3150870				0	bs	MsgBox Time,0,"The time is"				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03030302.xhp	0	help	par_id3154123				0	bs	end sub				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03030104.xhp	0	help	tit				0	bs	Month Function [Runtime]				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03030104.xhp	0	help	bm_id3153127				0	bs	\<bookmark_value\>Month function\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03030104.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153127				0	bs	\<link href=\"text/sbasic/shared/03030104.xhp\" name=\"Month Function [Runtime]\"\>Month Function [Runtime]\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03030104.xhp	0	help	par_id3148550				0	bs	Returns the month of a year from a serial date that is generated by the DateSerial or the DateValue function.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03030104.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145068				0	bs	Syntax:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03030104.xhp	0	help	par_id3150398				0	bs	Month (Number)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03030104.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154366				0	bs	Return value:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03030104.xhp	0	help	par_id3154125				0	bs	Integer				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03030104.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150768				0	bs	Parameters:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03030104.xhp	0	help	par_id3156423				0	bs	\<emph\>Number:\</emph\> Numeric expression that contains the serial date number that is used to determine the month of the year.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03030104.xhp	0	help	par_id3153770	9			0	bs	This function is the opposite of the \<emph\>DateSerial \</emph\>function. It returns the month in the year that corresponds to the serial date that is generated by \<emph\>DateSerial\</emph\> or \<emph\>DateValue\</emph\>. For example, the expression				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03030104.xhp	0	help	par_id3147426				0	bs	Print Month(DateSerial(1994, 12, 20))				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03030104.xhp	0	help	par_id3145366				0	bs	returns the value 12.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03030104.xhp	0	help	hd_id3146923				0	bs	Example:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03030104.xhp	0	help	par_id3156442				0	bs	Sub ExampleMonth				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03030104.xhp	0	help	par_id3149664				0	bs	MsgBox "" & Month(Now) ,64,"The current month"				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03030104.xhp	0	help	par_id3150012				0	bs	End sub				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03020204.xhp	0	help	tit				0	bs	Put Statement [Runtime]				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03020204.xhp	0	help	bm_id3150360				0	bs	\<bookmark_value\>Put statement\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03020204.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150360				0	bs	\<link href=\"text/sbasic/shared/03020204.xhp\" name=\"Put Statement [Runtime]\"\>Put Statement [Runtime]\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03020204.xhp	0	help	par_id3154909				0	bs	Writes a record to a relative file or a sequence of bytes to a binary file.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03020204.xhp	0	help	par_id3156281				0	bs	See also: \<link href=\"text/sbasic/shared/03020201.xhp\" name=\"Get\"\>\<item type=\"literal\"\>Get\</item\>\</link\> statement				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03020204.xhp	0	help	hd_id3125863				0	bs	Syntax:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03020204.xhp	0	help	par_id3155132				0	bs	Put [#] FileNumber As Integer, [position], Variable				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03020204.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153190				0	bs	Parameters:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03020204.xhp	0	help	par_id3146120				0	bs	\<emph\>FileNumber:\</emph\> Any integer expression that defines the file that you want to write to.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03020204.xhp	0	help	par_id3155411	8			0	bs	\<emph\>Position: \</emph\>For relative files (random access files), the number of the record that you want to write.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03020204.xhp	0	help	par_id3148576				0	bs	For binary files (binary access), the position of the byte in the file where you want to start writing.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03020204.xhp	0	help	par_id3153729				0	bs	\<emph\>Variable:\</emph\> Name of the variable that you want to write to the file.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03020204.xhp	0	help	par_id3146974				0	bs	Note for relative files: If the contents of this variable does not match the length of the record that is specified in the \<emph\>Len\</emph\> clause of the \<emph\>Open\</emph\> statement, the space between the end of the newly written record and the next record is padded with existing data from the file that you are writing to.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03020204.xhp	0	help	par_id3155855				0	bs	Note for binary files: The contents of the variables are written to the specified position, and the file pointer is inserted directly after the last byte. No space is left between the records.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
