helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\01030200.xhp	0	help	tit				0	bs	The Basic Editor				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\01030200.xhp	0	help	bm_id3148647				0	bs	\<bookmark_value\>saving;Basic code\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>Basic;loading and saving source code\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>loading;Basic code\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>Basic editor\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>navigating;in Basic projects\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>long lines;in Basic editor\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>lines;in Basic editor\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>continuation;long lines in editor\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\01030200.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147264				0	bs	\<link href=\"text/sbasic/shared/01030200.xhp\" name=\"The Basic Editor\"\>The Basic Editor\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\01030200.xhp	0	help	par_id3145069				0	bs	The Basic Editor provides the standard editing functions you are familiar with when working in a text document. It supports the functions of the \<emph\>Edit\</emph\> menu (Cut, Delete, Paste), the ability to select text with the Shift key, as well as cursor positioning functions (for example, moving from word to word with \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Option \</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> and the arrow keys).				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\01030200.xhp	0	help	par_id3154686				0	bs	Long lines can be split into several parts by inserting an underline character _ as the last character of a line. This connects the line with the following line to one logical line.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\01030200.xhp	0	help	par_id3151042				0	bs	If you press the \<emph\>Run BASIC\</emph\> icon on the \<emph\>Macro\</emph\> bar, program execution starts at the first line of the Basic editor. The "Sub Main" does not take precedence on program execution.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\01030200.xhp	0	help	hd_id3125863				0	bs	Navigating in a Project				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\01030200.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145785				0	bs	The Library List				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\01030200.xhp	0	help	par_id3146120				0	bs	Select a library from the \<emph\>Library\</emph\> list at the left of the toolbar to load the library in the editor. The first module of the selected library will be displayed.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\01030200.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153190				0	bs	The Object Catalog				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\01030200.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148647				0	bs	Saving and Loading Basic Source Code				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\01030200.xhp	0	help	par_id3154320				0	bs	You can save Basic code in a text file for saving and importing in other programming systems.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\01030200.xhp	0	help	par_id3149959				0	bs	You cannot save Basic dialogs to a text file.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\01030200.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149403				0	bs	Saving Source Code to a Text File				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\01030200.xhp	0	help	par_id3150327				0	bs	Select the module that you want to export as text from the object catalog.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\01030200.xhp	0	help	par_id3150752				0	bs	Click the \<emph\>Save Source As\</emph\> icon in the Macro toolbar.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\01030200.xhp	0	help	par_id3154754				0	bs	Select a file name and click \<emph\>OK\</emph\> to save the file.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\01030200.xhp	0	help	hd_id3159264				0	bs	Loading Source Code From a Text File				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\01030200.xhp	0	help	par_id3147343				0	bs	Select the module where you want to import the source code from the object catalog.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
