helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03080202.xhp	0	help	par_id3150869				0	bs	The natural logarithm is the logarithm to the base e. Base e is a constant with an approximate value of 2.718282...				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03080202.xhp	0	help	par_id3153968				0	bs	You can calculate logarithms to any base (n) for any number (x) by dividing the natural logarithm of x by the natural logarithm of n, as follows:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03080202.xhp	0	help	par_id3145420				0	bs	Log n(x) = Log(x) / Log(n)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
