helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03030101.xhp	0	help	hd_id3157896				0	bs	\<link href=\"text/sbasic/shared/03030101.xhp\" name=\"DateSerial Function [Runtime]\"\>DateSerial Function [Runtime]\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03030101.xhp	0	help	par_id3143267				0	bs	Returns a \<emph\>Date\</emph\> value for a specified year, month, or day.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03030101.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147264				0	bs	Syntax:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03030101.xhp	0	help	par_id3149670				0	bs	DateSerial (year, month, day)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03030101.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150792				0	bs	Return value:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03030101.xhp	0	help	par_id3150398				0	bs	Date				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03030101.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154141				0	bs	Parameters:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03030101.xhp	0	help	par_id3147229				0	bs	\<emph\>Year:\</emph\> Integer expression that indicates a year. All values between 0 and 99 are interpreted as the years 1900-1999. For years that fall outside this range, you must enter all four digits.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03030101.xhp	0	help	par_id3156280				0	bs	\<emph\>Month:\</emph\> Integer expression that indicates the month of the specified year. The accepted range is from 1-12.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03030101.xhp	0	help	par_id3151043				0	bs	\<emph\>Day:\</emph\> Integer expression that indicates the day of the specified month. The accepted range is from 1-31, depending on the month.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03030101.xhp	0	help	par_id3161832				0	bs	The \<emph\>DateSerial function\</emph\> returns the number of days between December 30,1899 and the given date. You can use this function to calculate the difference between two dates.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03030101.xhp	0	help	par_id3155306				0	bs	The \<emph\>DateSerial function\</emph\> returns the data type Variant with VarType 7 (Date). Internally, this value is stored as a Double value, so that when the given date is 1.1.1900, the returned value is 2. Negative values correspond to dates before December 30, 1899 (not inclusive).				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03030101.xhp	0	help	par_id3152576				0	bs	If a date is defined that lies outside of the accepted range, $[officename] Basic returns an error message.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03030101.xhp	0	help	par_id3149481				0	bs	Whereas you define the \<emph\>DateValue function\</emph\> as a string that contains the date, the \<emph\>DateSerial function\</emph\> evaluates each of the parameters (year, month, day) as separate numeric expressions.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
