helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04040000.xhp	0	help	par_id3154762	41			0	bs	\<ahelp hid=\"SCH:CHECKBOX:DLG_AXIS:CB_Y_SECONDARY\"\>The major axis and the secondary axis can have different scaling. For example, you can scale one axis to 2 in. and the other to 1.5 in. \</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\05040201.xhp	0	help	tit				0	bs	Scaling				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\05040201.xhp	0	help	bm_id3150868				0	bs	\<bookmark_value\>scaling; axes\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>logarithmic scaling along axes\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>charts;scaling axes\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>X axes;scaling\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>axes; scaling\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>axes;interval marks\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
